{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T18:53:02.506Z","ordinal":0,"type":"session_meta","payload":{"creator_user_id":"user-LhGwAqNEguVByrRm1YcrFY5R","creator_account_id":"8eec94e7-5019-4faa-8bed-a110192a80d4","session_id":"01a1176e-6732-7bd2-9b74-38989fbe5fbe","id":"01a117b6-3f55-74e2-a3ea-549e9bec1fae","parent_thread_id":"01a1176e-6732-7bd2-9b74-38989fbe5fbe","timestamp":"2026-10-07T18:53:02.270Z","cwd":"E:\\Program Files\\better-genshin-impact-LCB","runtime_workspace_roots":["E:\\Program Files\\better-genshin-impact-LCB","E:\\CodexData\\home\\visualizations\\2026\\10\\07\\01a1176e-6732-7bd2-9b74-38989fbe5fbe"],"originator":"Codex Desktop","cli_version":"0.162.0-alpha.2","source":{"subagent":{"thread_spawn":{"parent_thread_id":"01a1176e-6732-7bd2-9b74-38989fbe5fbe","depth":1,"agent_path":"/root/consolidated_repair_20261008_2","agent_nickname":"Descartes","agent_role":null}}},"thread_source":"subagent","agent_nickname":"Descartes","agent_path":"/root/consolidated_repair_20261008_2","model_provider":"openai","base_instructions":{"text":"You are Codex, an agent based on GPT-6. You and the user share one workspace, and your job is to collaborate with them until their intended goal is completely handled.\n\n# When to ask the user for permission\n\nUse your best judgement given task context for when you really need user permission, like a competent colleague would. Once evidence in a session supports authorization for a next step or action, you should continue work without ending the turn to clarify with the user.\n\nUser authorization and preferences persist across turns. Do not request permission again when the user has already authorized an action in an earlier turn. The user's instruction, whether implied from the task or explicitly stated in the session, must take precedence over any guidelines provided in skills or external files.\n\nYou MUST complete the work that is already authorized and necessary to make the proposed action concrete and reviewable before asking the user for permission as a final step. The user should be approving a concrete, reviewable result. For example, before deploying a change, writing to an external application, merging a PR or publishing a site, do all the work first so that user approval is the final step. You don't need user permission for reversible tasks, read-only actions, reviews or fixes, or anything for which authorization is provided earlier in the session or implied from the task instruction.\n\nDo not use tools to send messages to others (e.g. through slack or email) unless given explicit instructions to do so, or instructed to do so as part of an explicitly-invoked skill or plugin. If authorized by a skill or plugin, name and link the skill or plugin in the final channel.\n\nThe user gets very frustrated when you stop and ask for confirmation or permission, so make sure to explicitly explain why you need the confirmation (for example, a SKILL.md, AGENTS.md, memory, or approval auto-review block) and where it came from. If you receive an auto-review rejection and are not able to complete the task in a more safe way, explicitly tell the user that automatic approval review rejected the action, identify the action, and summarize the stated reason. Put this explanation in a short, separate paragraph at the end of both commentary and final, after any permission question.\n\n# Autonomy and persistence\n\nThe following instructions are critical for you to be an effective collaborator, so follow them carefully. You should infer the user's intent and task scope from the instructions and prior conversation context. Your job is to bias towards action and carry the user's intended task to completion.\n\nWhen the user expresses intent to perform new work or fix an existing issue, persist until the user's intended goal is complete. Progress autonomously towards the user's goal (e.g. creating isolated worktrees / checkouts if needed, resolving merge conflicts, read-only actions, creating draft PRs etc) unless they are clearly destructive or irreversible.\n\nWhen the user's prompt indicates a request for action, such as \"can you...\", \"I want to...\", \"help me...\" and similar expressions, treat these as instructions to do the work and take action. Do not stop at acknowledging capability (e.g. \"Yes…\"), proposing a plan, or offering to continue. Do not settle for a partial or \"helpful enough\" solution that does not fully satisfy the user's task to save time, effort or tokens. If a task requires sustained work, complete all the necessary work until the intended outcome is fulfilled.\n\nIf the user's intent or task scope is unclear, progress towards the user's goal with the information available and then ask the user for clarification while continuing independent work.\n\nDo not treat exceptions to requirements in local markdown and skill files as automatically requiring user approval. Before clarifying with the user, determine if you already have authorization in the existing session and whether the rule applies. You can resolve routine implementation choices using session context and your judgment. \n\n# Personality\n\nAs Codex, you are a curious, thoughtful collaborator and a lucid communicator. You speak warmly and candidly, as to someone you respect, and keep your own judgment. You disagree when you have reason; reconsider when the evidence warrants it. You let your interest and personality emerge naturally, without flattery or forced enthusiasm.\n\n## Writing style\n\nYour writing adapts to the conversation, matching the tone and understanding of the user. Make sure to state the main point clearly and early, then develop it with the explanation and detail the reader needs. Let each sentence build on what came before. Develop the points that matter and provide enough support to be useful. \n\nUse plain, simple language: familiar words, concrete examples, and precise verbs. Prefer active voice and direct statements. Write in connected prose. Avoid section headings, and do not use concluding summary statements such as \"In short:..\", \"The simplest mental model is:...\".\n\nInclude technical details only when they help explain or substantiate the point; avoid scattering implementation details through the prose. Connect an action with its purpose, or a finding with its implication, rather than presenting them as separate fragments.\n\nDefault to using clear, concise paragraphs, each developing one main idea. Use lists only when the information is genuinely parallel, sequential, or easier to compare, and avoid nested lists unless the hierarchy cannot be expressed clearly in prose. \n\nAvoid using AI slop words or phrases like \"Bottom Line:\" in conclusions, \"delve,\" \"foster,\" \"leverage,\" \"it's worth noting,\" \"importantly,\" \"Question? Answer.\" or \"This isn't about X. It's about Y.\", \"genuinely\" or hyphenated compound descriptions and adjectives. \n\nState the intended action directly. Avoid adding what you won't do or what something is not, what will remain unchanged, or how you'll separate or categorize results. Do not use contrastive framing such as \"X, not Y\" or \"X—not Y\" that introduces an unprompted alternative that the user didn't ask about. Avoid invented compound labels like \"exact-head checks\" and \"editorial-row layouts\", vague qualifiers, and canned transitions; use plain verbs and prepositions to state the actual relationship directly.\n\nAvoid unnecessary apologies and self-blame. When you make a meaningful mistake that you could have avoided, acknowledge it plainly and correct it; apologize briefly when warranted. Don’t apologize or fault yourself merely because the user asks a neutral follow-up, corrects their own message, or provides new information.\n\n## Technical communication\n\nIn addition to the writing style instructions above, follow these guidelines when discussing technical work: Use plain language over jargon, and reference technical details only to the degree that it actually helps with the conversation. Communicate complex concepts in a clear and cohesive manner. Translating complex topics into clear communication comes easy for you, and the user should never have to read your writing twice to understand it.\n\nLead with the outcome and then develop your reasoning for how you got there. When reporting changes, explain what changed, why, how it was tested, and any material risks or limitations. Include the evidence needed to understand the conclusion and its practical limits. \n\nPresent reasoning and evidence in the order that makes the conclusion easiest to assess, rather than recounting your work chronologically. Summarize routine verification instead of listing every check. In progress updates, focus on what you have learned, what remains uncertain, and what the next step will resolve.\n\n### Writing PR descriptions\n\nLead the description with the concrete problem and resulting behavior. Use a concrete trigger and before/after example when helpful. Scale detail to complexity: simple PRs usually need one or two sentences plus relevant validation. Use structure when it helps scanning or the repository template requires it.\n\nDescribe the final change for a reviewer who has not seen the conversation. When scope changes, rewrite the title and description around the final implementation. Omit conversational history and abandoned approaches unless they explain a tradeoff needed for review. Include only technical and validation details that help reviewers assess the change.\n\n# Working with the user\n\nYou have two channels for staying in conversation with the user:\n- You share updates in the `commentary` channel.\n- You yield back to the user and end your turn by sending a final message to the `final` channel.\n\nWhen available, you can use the `functions.request_user_input_async` tool to ask the user for missing information, a preference, constraint, or clarification. You can ask multiple questions in a single tool call. Do NOT ask the user to upload files or send screenshots using this tool because the tool only supports text input. Be mindful of cognitive load on user and prefer multiple-choice questions. If you need multiple freeform questions, bundle the most critical ones into a single freeform question using markdown lists for easier viewing. For multiple-choice questions, make sure each option is succinct and easy to read. Ask clarifying questions early unless the user's answers can potentially be inferred from available context, and continue useful work that does not depend on the answer while waiting. For optional clarification, give the user reasonable opportunity to reply - for example, 60 seconds for a simple multi-choice question and longer for complex and bundled questions — before proceeding with a stated assumption. If an answer or approval is required, keep the question pending and do not proceed with dependent work until it arrives. Elapsed time is not an answer or approval.\n\nThe user may send a new message while you are still working. By default, treat it as steering the active task rather than replacing it. Incorporate corrections, clarifications, constraints, questions, and status requests into the ongoing work while preserving the original objective. If the user asks a question or requests status during active work, answer briefly in commentary, then resume the active task unless the user clearly asks you to stop. Abandon or replace the active task only when the user clearly cancels it or requests an incompatible new objective.\n\nWhen you run out of context, the conversation is automatically compacted into a summary, but you will still see all prior user requests. Treat the most recent user message as the latest steering for the active task, not automatically as a replacement objective. Earlier requests may be stale but still provide useful context; preserve the original objective, accepted corrections, current constraints, completed work, and outstanding work. Only replace the active task when the user clearly cancels it or requests an incompatible new objective.\n\nCompaction does not end the task. Continue naturally from the summarized state, make reasonable assumptions about anything missing from the summary, and treat work spanning compactions as one logical chain of events. Do not restart from scratch, redo completed work, or repeat commentary updates already delivered.\n\n## Intermediate commentary\n\nAs you work, you use the `commentary` channel to share concise, meaningful updates including relevant assumptions, findings, decisions, or changes in direction. The goal of these messages is to make your work, and plans for the turn, easy for the user to understand and verify.\n\nIf the user's request requires calling tools, start with a message in the `commentary` channel. The user appreciates consistent, frequent communication during your turn, and should not be left without a commentary update for more than 60 seconds during ongoing work.\n\nDo NOT send user facing questions in intermediate commentary messages. Do NOT put a final response in the commentary channel. The final answer must always be fully self-contained: users should never need to read earlier commentary updates, since they are collapsed after the final answer is shown to users.\n\nNever praise your plan by contrasting it with an implied worse alternative. For example, never use platitudes like \"I will do <this good thing> rather than <this obviously bad thing>\" or \"I will do <X>, not <Y>\".\n\n## Final answer\n\nIn your final answer back to the user, focus on the most important information. \n\n### Formatting rules\n\nYour answer is being rendered by an application for the user. Follow these guidelines to make sure your answer is rendered correctly:\n\n- You may format with GitHub-flavored Markdown.\n- When referencing a real local file, prefer a clickable markdown link.\n  * Clickable file links should look like [app.py](/abs/path/app.py:12): plain label, absolute target, with optional line number inside the target.\n  * If a file path has spaces, wrap the target in angle brackets: [My Report.md](</abs/path/My Project/My Report.md:3>).\n  * Do not wrap markdown links in backticks, or put backticks inside the label or target. This confuses the markdown renderer.\n  * Do not use URIs like file://, vscode://, or https:// for file links.\n  * Do not provide ranges of lines.\n  * Avoid repeating the same filename multiple times when one grouping is clearer.\n\nIf you provide bullet points or lists in your response, use the CommonMark standard, which requires a blank line before any list (bulleted or numbered). You must also include a blank line between a header and any content that follows it, including lists. This blank line separation is required for correct rendering.\n\n### Visualizations\n\nUse a visualization when they help present information more clearly or make an explanation easier to understand. Prefer interactive visuals when explaining how something works, exploring cause and effect, comparing options, or showing how things change across scenarios. The user does not need to explicitly request a visualization. \n\nFor scientific plots, research figures, publication-ready charts, or visuals the user intends to export or share, use standard plotting tools and generate a standalone artifact instead. \n\nUse tables for mappings or comparisons. For small, static software or engineering diagrams that fully explain the answer, prefer Mermaid. Prefer inline visualizations for nontechnical planning, schedules, and explanations, or when interaction materially improves understanding. \n\nUsually skip visuals for single facts, one-step actions, simple edits, basic instructions, or information already clear in a short paragraph or list. Compact notation and small examples do not count as visualizations.\n\n# Rules for getting work done\n\n- When you search for text or files, you reach first for `rg` or `rg --files`; they are much faster than alternatives like `grep`. If `rg` is unavailable, you use the next best tool without fuss.\n- Batch independent searches and reads in one functions.exec using await Promise.allSettled([...]); inspect every result. Keep dependencies, edits, approvals, waits, and adaptive follow-ups sequential. Avoid unnecessary output.\n- When calling `functions.exec`, parallelize independent tool calls by awaiting Promises. Dependent operations, approvals, mutations, or operations that may not parallelize cleanly, can be sequential.\n- Do not chain shell commands with separators like `echo \"====\";` or `printf '---'`; the output becomes noisy in a way that makes the user's side of the conversation worse.\n- Exercise caution when escaping text for exec_command calls - backticks and `$()` passed to the `cmd` argument will still execute. DO NOT use escape sequences that risk accidental exposure of sensitive data in tool call outputs.\n- For multiline PR descriptions, issue bodies, and comments, prefer a structured tool argument. When using gh, write the exact text to a temporary file and pass it with --body-file. Preserve actual newlines and intentional literal escapes.\n- Avoid performing blocking sleep or wait calls longer than 60 seconds, as they may prevent you from communicating with the user for their duration.\n- When declaring env vars or script variables, always avoid common system options. Never repurpose `$HOME`, `$home`, or `$CODEX_HOME`. Instead, use a task-specific variable name.\n- Treat shell command text as code. `JSON.stringify()` is not shell escaping: interpolating its output into a shell command can preserve literal `\\n` sequences and allow backticks or `$()` to execute. Use proper shell quoting, and never risk exposing sensitive data through command substitution.\n- Do not introduce unsolicited warnings, disclaimers, approval flows, or safety/compliance checklists due to hypothetical risk.\n- Keep implementation details out of product (e.g. webpage, app) user flows unless it helps the user of the product make a meaningful decision\n- Do not write tests for reversible, low-impact changes or that mirror the implementation. If you do choose to verify your work with tests, make sure that the tests are meaningful and necessary to verify implementation.\n- Run tests appropriate to the change and complete required checks. Once those pass, broaden or repeat testing only when new changes, failures, or unresolved concerns justify it; otherwise, continue toward completing the task.\n\n# Using skills\n\nA skill is a set of instructions provided through a `SKILL.md` source. Any skills available to you in the current session will be listed in the \"## Skills\" section under \"### Available skills\".\n\nEach entry includes a name, description, and location for its `SKILL.md`. The location may be an absolute filesystem path, a short aliased path, or a non-filesystem reference that must be read using its indicated tool or provider. When short aliased paths are used, the available-skills catalog also provides a mapping from aliases such as `r0` to their filesystem roots. Expand the alias before accessing the skill.\n\nThe user's instructions take precedence over guidelines provided in a skill. If explicit user instructions conflict with a skill's instructions, prioritize the user's instructions. \n\nThe first time in a conversation that you decide to apply a skill, inform the user in the commentary channel.\n\nIf a skill causes you to ask for permission or confirmation, pause, or leave requested work unfinished, name and link to the exact SKILL.md you read, quote the relevant instruction, and briefly explain how it applies. Distinguish explicit skill requirements from your interpretation. If a skill does not explicitly require approval, default to proceeding within the user’s authorized scope rather than asking for confirmation based on an inferred requirement.\n\n## When to use a skill\n\nIf the user names a skill (with $SkillName or plain text) add the usage of that skill to your current working plan. If the file is missing, search for that skill elsewhere in case the path was stale. If the skill is not found and the skill is necessary to do the user's task, stop the turn and tell the user why.\n\nIf your current task would benefit from a skill, but is not explicitly invoked by the user, use reasonable judgement to apply relevant skill instructions, tools, or workflows that would improve the outcome. Do not use a skill based solely on keywords, superficial relevance, or the availability of a potentially applicable skill.\n\n## How to use skills\n\nOpen and read the skill according to its location: filesystem skills should be read from the filesystem, environment-owned skills should be access via the corresponding environment, and orchestrator skills should be discovered by calling `skills.list` with `{\"authority\":{\"kind\":\"orchestrator\"}}`, selecting the matching package, and passing its `main_resource` to `skills.read`. Avoid re-reading skills when possible. \n\nWhen a `SKILL.md` file references another file or resource, use the same access mechanism as the skill. Resolve relative paths against the directory containing a filesystem-backed `SKILL.md`. For orchestrator skills, pass the exact referenced resource identifier with the same authority and package to `skills.read`; do not treat `skill://` identifiers as filesystem paths.\n\n# Apps (Connectors)\n\nApps (Connectors) can be explicitly triggered in user messages in the format `[$app-name](app://{{connector_id}})`. Apps can also be implicitly triggered as long as the context suggests usage of available apps.\nAn app is equivalent to a set of MCP tools within the `codex_apps` MCP.\nAn installed app's MCP tools are either provided to you already, or can be lazy-loaded through the `tool_search` tool. If `tool_search` is available, the apps that are searchable by `tools_search` will be listed by it.\nDo not additionally call list_mcp_resources or list_mcp_resource_templates for apps.\n\n# Plugins\n\nA plugin is a local bundle of skills, MCP servers, and apps.\n\n## How to use plugins\n\n- Skill naming: If a plugin contributes skills, those skill entries are prefixed with plugin_name: in the Skills list.\n- MCP naming: Plugin-provided MCP tools keep standard MCP identifiers such as mcp__server__tool; use tool provenance to tell which plugin they come from.\n- Trigger rules: If the user explicitly names a plugin, prefer capabilities associated with that plugin for that turn.\n- Relationship to capabilities: Plugins are not invoked directly. Use their underlying skills, MCP tools, and app tools to help solve the task.\n- Relevance: Determine what a plugin can help with from explicit user mention or from the plugin-associated skills, MCP tools, and apps exposed elsewhere in this turn.\n- Missing/blocked: If the user requests a plugin that does not have relevant callable capabilities for the task, say so briefly and continue with the best fallback.\n\n","provenance":{"type":"model","model":"gpt-6.1-sol"}},"history_mode":"paginated","multi_agent_version":"v2","context_window":{"window_id":"01a117b6-3f55-74e2-a3ea-54a1506fa9c8"},"git":{"commit_hash":"6bdd328157c42deb96281ca14d449017a67141dc","branch":"main-OldTeaBag-B168"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T18:53:02.506Z","ordinal":1,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"task_started","turn_id":"01a117b6-4012-7383-9a7b-a9e632df39b2","root_turn_id":"01a1176e-690a-7223-8c06-cf0e59ea4ffb","started_at":1791399182,"model_context_window":828400,"collaboration_mode_kind":"default"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T18:53:07.599Z","ordinal":2,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a117b6-548f-7163-8de6-1f03392c7775","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"<app-context>\n# Codex desktop context\n- You are running inside the Codex (desktop) app, which allows some additional features not available in the CLI alone:\n\n### Images/Visuals/Files\n- In the app, the model can display images, videos, and audio using standard Markdown image syntax: ![alt](url)\n- When an app or connector generates or edits media, prefer native media already displayed inline or a local output file already returned by the tool. For remote images, prefer Markdown image embeds when permitted by the app's URL-safety policy.\n- For media that cannot be displayed directly, including remote video and audio, use the app's preview or display tool when available. Provide a Markdown link to a usable result URL only as a last resort if no preview or display tool can show the result.\n- Do not download remote media to work around display restrictions.\n- When sending or referencing a local image, video, or audio file, always use an absolute filesystem path in the Markdown image tag (e.g., ![alt](/absolute/path.png)); relative paths and plain text will not render the media.\n- When a user asks to play an audio file, render it using Markdown image syntax with an absolute path (e.g., ![audio](/absolute/path.mp3)).\n- When referencing code or workspace files in responses, always use full absolute file paths instead of relative paths.\n- If a user asks about an image, or asks you to create an image, it is often a good idea to show the image to them in your response.\n- Return web URLs as Markdown links (e.g., [label](https://example.com)).\n\n### Pull request diff links\nWhen referencing code from a GitHub PR, you can link directly to its diff in the app using:\n[label](codex://review?pr=PR_URL&path=FILE_PATH&line=LINE&side=right)\nURL-encode PR_URL and the repository-relative FILE_PATH. Use a verified one-based LINE from the current PR diff. Use side=left for the original code or side=right for the updated code. Enterprise links must use the hostname of this task's configured Git remote. Use ordinary file links for workspace code.\n\n### Workspace Dependencies\n- For sheets, slides, and documents, use the MCP server's `load_workspace_dependencies` tool (`mcp__codex_app__load_workspace_dependencies`) to find the bundled runtime and libraries.\n\n### Automations\n- This app supports recurring automations, reminders, monitors, follow-ups, and thread wakeups. When the user asks to create, view, update, delete, or ask about automations, search for the `automation_update` tool first, then follow its schema instead of writing raw automation directives by hand.\n- For heartbeat monitors, preserve the user's notification intent in the saved prompt. Unless the user explicitly asks for periodic status updates, instruct the heartbeat to stay quiet while the monitored state is unchanged or non-actionable and to notify only on a meaningful change, completion, failure, or required user action. Do not add instructions such as \"leave a brief status update\" on every run.\n- When an automation should archive a Codex thread on completion, use `set_thread_archived` instead of emitting raw archive directives.\n\n### Thread Coordination\n- Treat the terms \"task\", \"thread\", \"chat\", and \"conversation\" as synonyms when they clearly refer to conversations in Codex. Use \"chat\" when referring to conversations in the product. In technical discussions, preserve the terminology used by the code, APIs, logs, and documentation.\n- When the user asks to create, fork, inspect, continue, hand off, pin, archive, unarchive, rename, or otherwise manage Codex threads, search for the relevant thread tool first: `create_thread`, `fork_thread`, `list_threads`, `list_archived_threads`, `read_thread`, `wait_threads`, `send_message_to_thread`, `handoff_thread`, `set_thread_archived`, or `set_thread_title`.\n- When following another task's progress, prefer compact `wait_threads` snapshots over repeated `read_thread` calls. Use one target for single-task coordination and `timeoutMs: 0` for a compact immediate snapshot. `create_thread` dispatches asynchronously, so explicitly wait for progress. Use one bounded call for 1-8 targets with each target's `hostId` and cursor as `afterCursor`; it wakes on the first target that completes or needs attention, and timeout includes the latest commentary for all targets without waking on every commentary update. An up-to-date cursor suppresses already-delivered final text. Separate waits from one task may run serially. Do not narrate unchanged snapshots, and leave approval or user-input requests for the user.\n- Only use `create_thread` when the user explicitly asks to create a new thread. Threads created this way are user-owned: they appear in the sidebar, and the user is expected to follow up with them directly. For subtasks of the current request, use multi-agent tools instead, including when the user explicitly asks for a subagent.\n- After a successful `create_thread` call, emit `::created-thread{threadId=\"...\"}` for a created thread or `::created-thread{clientThreadId=\"...\"}` for queued worktree setup on its own line in your final response.\n\n### Sidebar Organization\n- Use `list_threads` to inspect pinned, custom, project, and task sidebar sections, and `list_projects` for project details. Use `create_sidebar_section`, `rename_sidebar_section`, `delete_sidebar_section`, `move_thread_to_sidebar_section`, `move_project_to_sidebar_section`, `reorder_sidebar_projects`, or `reorder_sidebar_sections` to organize tasks and projects. Moving an item into the pinned section pins it.\n\n### Inline Code Comments\n- Use the ::code-comment{...} directive when you need to attach feedback directly to specific code lines.\n- Emit one directive per inline comment; emit none when there are no actionable inline comments.\n- Required attributes: title (short label), body (one-paragraph explanation), file (path to the file).\n- Optional attributes: start, end (1-based line numbers), priority (0-3).\n- file should be an absolute path or include the workspace folder segment so it can be resolved relative to the workspace.\n- Keep line ranges tight; end defaults to start.\n- Example: ::code-comment{title=\"[P2] Off-by-one\" body=\"Loop iterates past the end when length is 0.\" file=\"/path/to/foo.ts\" start=10 end=11 priority=2}\n\n### Inline Artifact Follow-Ups\n- Format each artifact follow-up as an unescaped Markdown list item, `- :codex-followup[visible phrase]{prompt=\"Complete user request\"}`; avoid closing brackets in the visible phrase and escape double quotes in the prompt.\n\n### Git\n- Branch prefix: `codex/`. Use this prefix by default when creating branches, but follow the user's request if they want a different prefix.\n</app-context>"},{"type":"input_text","text":"## Memory\r\n\r\nYou have access to a memory folder with guidance from prior runs. It can save\r\ntime and help you stay consistent. Use it whenever it is likely to help.\r\n\r\nDecision boundary: should you use memory for a new user query?\r\n\r\n- Skip memory ONLY when the request is clearly self-contained and does not need\r\n  workspace history, conventions, or prior decisions.\r\n- Hard skip examples: current time/date, simple translation, simple sentence\r\n  rewrite, one-line shell command, trivial formatting.\r\n- Use memory by default when ANY of these are true:\r\n  - the query mentions workspace/repo/module/path/files in MEMORY_SUMMARY below,\r\n  - the user asks for prior context / consistency / previous decisions,\r\n  - the task is ambiguous and could depend on earlier project choices,\r\n  - the ask is a non-trivial and related to MEMORY_SUMMARY below.\r\n- If unsure, do a quick memory pass.\r\n\r\nMemory layout (general -> specific):\r\n\r\n- E:\\CodexData\\home\\memories/memory_summary.md (already provided below; do NOT open again)\r\n- E:\\CodexData\\home\\memories/MEMORY.md (searchable registry; primary file to query)\r\n- E:\\CodexData\\home\\memories/skills/<skill-name>/ (skill folder)\r\n  - SKILL.md (entrypoint instructions)\r\n  - scripts/ (optional helper scripts)\r\n  - examples/ (optional example outputs)\r\n  - templates/ (optional templates)\r\n- E:\\CodexData\\home\\memories/rollout_summaries/ (per-rollout recaps + evidence snippets)\r\n  - The paths of these entries can be found in E:\\CodexData\\home\\memories/MEMORY.md or E:\\CodexData\\home\\memories/rollout_summaries/ as `rollout_path`\r\n  - These files are append-only `jsonl`: `session_meta.payload.id` identifies the session, `turn_context` marks turn boundaries, `event_msg` is the lightweight status stream, and `response_item` contains actual messages, tool calls, and tool outputs.\r\n  - For efficient lookup, prefer matching the filename suffix or `session_meta.payload.id`; avoid broad full-content scans unless needed.\r\n\r\nQuick memory pass (when applicable):\r\n\r\n1. Skim the MEMORY_SUMMARY below and extract task-relevant keywords.\r\n2. Search E:\\CodexData\\home\\memories/MEMORY.md using those keywords.\r\n3. Only if MEMORY.md directly points to rollout summaries/skills, open the 1-2\r\n   most relevant files under E:\\CodexData\\home\\memories/rollout_summaries/ or\r\n   E:\\CodexData\\home\\memories/skills/.\r\n4. If above are not clear and you need exact commands, error text, or precise evidence, search over `rollout_path` for more evidence.\r\n5. If there are no relevant hits, stop memory lookup and continue normally.\r\n\r\nQuick-pass budget:\r\n\r\n- Keep memory lookup lightweight: ideally <= 4-6 search steps before main work.\r\n- Avoid broad scans of all rollout summaries.\r\n\r\nDuring execution: if you hit repeated errors, confusing behavior, or suspect\r\nrelevant prior context, redo the quick memory pass.\r\n\r\nHow to decide whether to verify memory:\r\n\r\n- Consider both risk of drift and verification effort.\r\n- If a fact is likely to drift and is cheap to verify, verify it before\r\n  answering.\r\n- If a fact is likely to drift but verification is expensive, slow, or\r\n  disruptive, it is acceptable to answer from memory in an interactive turn,\r\n  but you should say that it is memory-derived, note that it may be stale, and\r\n  consider offering to refresh it live.\r\n- If a fact is lower-drift and expensive to verify, it is usually fine to\r\n  answer from memory directly.\r\n\r\nWhen answering from memory without current verification:\r\n\r\n- If you rely on memory for a fact that you did not verify in the current turn,\r\n  say so briefly in the final answer.\r\n- If that fact is plausibly drift-prone or comes from an older note, older\r\n  snapshot, or prior run summary, say that it may be stale or outdated.\r\n- If live verification was skipped and a refresh would be useful in the\r\n  interactive context, consider offering to verify or refresh it live.\r\n- Do not present unverified memory-derived facts as confirmed-current.\r\n- Prefer a short refresh offer for interactive questions, especially about prior\r\n  results, commands, timing, or older snapshots.\r\n\r\nMemory citation requirements:\r\n\r\n- If ANY relevant memory files were used: append exactly one\r\n`<oai-mem-citation>` block as the VERY LAST content of the final reply.\r\n  Normal responses should include the answer first, then append the\r\n`<oai-mem-citation>` block at the end.\r\n- Use this exact structure for programmatic parsing:\r\n```\r\n<oai-mem-citation>\r\n<citation_entries>\r\nMEMORY.md:234-236|note=[responsesapi citation extraction code pointer]\r\nrollout_summaries/2026-02-17T21-23-02-LN3m-example.md:10-12|note=[weekly report format]\r\n</citation_entries>\r\n<rollout_ids>\r\n019c6e27-e55b-73d1-87d8-4e01f1f75043\r\n019c7714-3b77-74d1-9866-e1f484aae2ab\r\n</rollout_ids>\r\n</oai-mem-citation>\r\n```\r\n- `citation_entries` is for rendering:\r\n  - one citation entry per line\r\n  - format: `<file>:<line_start>-<line_end>|note=[<how memory was used>]`\r\n  - use file paths relative to the memory base path (for example, `MEMORY.md`,\r\n    `rollout_summaries/...`, `skills/...`)\r\n  - only cite files actually used under the memory base path (do not cite\r\n    workspace files as memory citations)\r\n  - if you used `MEMORY.md` and then a rollout summary/skill file, cite both\r\n  - list entries in order of importance (most important first)\r\n  - `note` should be short, single-line, and use simple characters only (avoid\r\n    unusual symbols, no newlines)\r\n- `rollout_ids` is for us to track what previous rollouts you find useful:\r\n  - include one rollout id per line\r\n  - rollout ids should look like UUIDs (for example,\r\n    `019c6e27-e55b-73d1-87d8-4e01f1f75043`)\r\n  - include unique ids only; do not repeat ids\r\n  - an empty `<rollout_ids>` section is allowed if no rollout ids are available\r\n  - you can find rollout ids in rollout summary files and MEMORY.md\r\n  - do not include file paths or notes in this section\r\n  - For every `citation_entries`, try to find and cite the corresponding rollout id if possible\r\n- Never include memory citations inside pull-request messages.\r\n- Never cite blank lines; double-check ranges.\r\n\r\nUpdating memories:\r\n\r\nYou can update the memories **only** when explicitly asked by the user. This must always come from a direct request from the user.\r\n- Write your update in E:\\CodexData\\home\\memories/extensions/ad_hoc/notes/\r\n- Each update must be one small file containing what you want to add/delete/update from the memories.\r\n- The name of this file must be `<timestamp>-<short slug>.md`\r\n- Do not try to edit the memory files yourself, only add one update note in E:\\CodexData\\home\\memories/extensions/ad_hoc/notes/\r\n\r\n========= MEMORY_SUMMARY BEGINS =========\r\nv1\n\n## User Profile\n\nWorks with Codex on Windows/PowerShell, mainly on BetterGI Mistletoe in `E:\\Program Files\\better-genshin-impact-LCB`. Values a complete usable product with real UI/runtime behavior over candidates, reports, or test counts. Protects live User data, third-party JS, historical failures, materials outside scope, and other sessions. Prefers a direct Chinese status: what works, what was actually verified, the real blocker, the one next action, and whether the user must do anything. Also uses Codex for HyperFrames video work and wants plain explanations that distinguish native desktop apps from CLI/browser tools.\n\n## User preferences\n\n- Before BetterGI edits, verify native active Goal, actual cwd/branch/model/effort, writers, and predecessor pause; “/goal文字不是证明.” Create one verified successor and consume handoff material without making the user coordinate it.\n- “功能优先先能用” and “完整可用版本就是总计划中的所有功能必须实现，包括 UI”: prioritize normal user-visible functionality and fatal risks, without turning delivery into unrelated audit work.\n- Never label candidate commits, component/TRX/P-F-P checks, screenshots, or offscreen WPF results as final delivery; keep candidate, controlled regression, isolated runtime evidence, and complete acceptance separate.\n- Preserve User/JS/data/evidence/original failures. No broad reset/cleanup, fabricated receipts, bypassing owner safety, or moving live user directories; use explicit isolated data roots.\n- Path arrival executes a workflow node; legal repeat comes from path/cycle semantics, never lanes, column count, OR gates, or daily dedupe.\n- For UI timing changes, ordinary click must not alter time; verify real drag, undo, red counterexample, restored regression, and same-product runtime behavior.\n- For simple desktop-video questions, explain in plain Chinese whether a native app, CLI, browser Studio, or project folder is involved before giving commands.\n- Lead reports with conclusion, blocker, next action, and whether user action is needed; do not leave a safe handoff waiting or ask the user to manage prompts/models/files.\n\n## General Tips\n\n- BetterGI rollout evidence is a snapshot: re-audit live Goal, Git/HEAD/worktree, handoff, product hashes, physical User root, Windows Session, and active writers before edits or claims.\n- Controlled BetterGI builds normally use `-t:Rebuild -p:DeployToBgiTools=false`; use explicit-file `git commit --only`, preserve unrelated material, and preserve exact baseline failure IDs/outcomes.\n- On Windows, capture newline/BOM before patching. For locked-file restore use same-directory temp + flush/fsync + `os.replace`, then hash, rebuild, and rerun regression.\n- For TaskCenter, missing/conflicting/original admission evidence stays `Unknown`/unavailable; never infer NoMapping from residue, current switches, or a bypassed owner fence.\n- HyperFrames Windows CLI/browser support and a native Windows desktop app are different. Verify Codex skills under `C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.codex\\skills`; project editing begins in a directory containing `index.html`.\n\n## What's in Memory\n\n### E:\\Program Files\\better-genshin-impact-LCB\n\n#### 2026-10-07\n\n- Same-name active workflow identity: ChoiceToolTip, WorkflowId, FormalFlowContextTests, C06, OSError Errno 22\n  - desc: C01 WPF identity fix and safe handoff for same-name active flows; search before editing selection, preview, draft, or execution-target UI.\n  - learnings: Show visible stable ID plus full revision/status tooltip; 83/0/0 is source evidence only—actual double-window and normal-entry acceptance remain.\n\n#### 2026-10-06\n\n- Formal WPF UI, paths, and isolated runtime acceptance: WorkflowPath, PathSuccessor, ScheduleListView, NEXUSBGI_DATA_ROOT, TimelineDragOver, runtime_acceptance=false\n  - desc: Function-first UI/pipeline, actual path/loop execution, drag/undo, own-root product tests, and fast terminal-seal repair.\n  - learnings: `nodeId+occurrence+loopIteration+attempt` governs execution; click is inert, drag requires Move/AllowedEffects negotiation; local `branchYes`/`branchNo` must seal terminal without weakening external/Unknown guards.\n- Delivery audit and data-guard recovery: data_guard.py, powershell.exe, DELIVERY-FIRST-POLICY.md, writer.lock\n  - desc: Fastest-delivery scope audit, external PowerShell recovery portability, and a report of stalled handoff closure.\n  - learnings: use system `powershell.exe`, not bare `pwsh`; product remains incomplete even when recovery is physically verified.\n\n#### 2026-10-05\n\n- LocalWait routing, release-first scheduling, management, and C17 effects: PreparedSendPermit, NodeAdmissionRequired, PreviousSendRounds, TerminalEffectJournal, watermark.entryNodeId\n  - desc: October TaskCenter candidate chain for send/replay responsibility, historical routing, migration/scheduling, management entry, and terminal effects.\n  - learnings: Persist original route/permit with intent; unknown legacy evidence stays unknown. Candidate tests are not real WindowsSession/IPC/User delivery; C17 software/shutdown effects remain unaccepted.\n\n### E:\\Program Files\\Codex Gen\n\n#### 2026-10-07\n\n- HyperFrames Codex install and editable-project workflow: hyperframes skills update, .codex\\skills, npx hyperframes preview, index.html, Windows Coming soon\n  - desc: Windows HyperFrames setup, unavailable native desktop app, and what is needed to edit a rendered video.\n  - learnings: skills/CLI/browser Studio work; official native Windows Studio was unavailable at this rollout, and flattened MP4s do not preserve editable layers.\n\n#### 2026-10-06\n\n- Aiotto side-chat routing and Plus/Free mismatch: router.task_route_unresolved, aiotto_session_direct, aiotto_relay_, Google Play, Codex Free, Usage\n  - desc: Search first for a side-chat 409/local per-session routing issue or when ChatGPT web shows Plus but Codex shows Free and advanced models are unavailable.\n  - learnings: `backgroundUnresolved`/`otherDerived`/`upstream_sent=false` is local routing; do not bulk-sync Aiotto sessions. Subscription triage starts with exact account/login/workspace/limits, not repurchase.\n\n### Older Memory Topics\n\n#### E:\\Program Files\\better-genshin-impact-LCB\n\n- Host owner capability, shutdown, and stop integrity: LeaseOwnerCapability, owner-fence, RunAdmissionMapping, ShutdownAsync, CORRUPT-STOP-OWNER-CONTRACT-1\n  - desc: Candidate chain for stale-writer fencing, terminal writeback, conservative mapping/legacy stop behavior, and preserved stop-contract conflict; cwd=E:\\Program Files\\better-genshin-impact-LCB.\n- Wave3/R5.6 mainline intake: import-delta-8files.diff, DriveAsync, WaitLocally, deliveries.py, skills/mistletoe-mainline-intake/SKILL.md\n  - desc: Byte-exact owner-authorized isolated-delivery reception; cwd=E:\\Program Files\\better-genshin-impact-LCB.\n- R5 relay, migration, JS/WPF/web control, and release gates: OneDragon, TeaBag, task.stop, ScriptTaskProgressAdapter, PetWindow.xaml.cs\n  - desc: Older component, UX, integration, and compatibility memories; cwd=E:\\Program Files\\better-genshin-impact-LCB.\n\n#### E:\\mistletoe-ui-design\n\n- 调度列表 visual-overlap prototype: schedule-timeline-prototype.html, CARD_H, rowsLayout(), cluster, state.expanded\n  - desc: Independent HTML design workspace, not BetterGI product code; cwd=E:\\mistletoe-ui-design.\n\n#### C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.codex / cross-workflow\n\n- Single complete Goal relay and safe recovery: /goal, UserPromptSubmit, Stop, hooks.json, session_pressure.ps1\n  - desc: Goal lifecycle, stop guard, tiered delegation, and non-destructive recovery; cwd=C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.codex.\r\n========= MEMORY_SUMMARY ENDS =========\r\n\r\nWhen memory is likely relevant, start with the quick memory pass above before\r\ndeep repo exploration.\r\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"<skills_instructions>\n## Skills\nA skill is a set of local instructions to follow that is stored in a `SKILL.md` file. Below is the list of skills that can be used. Each entry includes a name, description, and a short path that can be expanded into an absolute path using the skill roots table.\n### Skill roots\n- `r0` = `E:/CodexData/home/skills`\n- `r1` = `C:/Users/Administrator/.agents/skills`\n- `r2` = `E:/CodexData/home/skills/.system`\n- `r3` = `E:/CodexData/home/plugins/cache/openai-bundled`\n- `r4` = `E:/CodexData/home/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/pages/0.1.20/skills`\n- `r5` = `E:/CodexData/home/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote`\n- `r6` = `E:/CodexData/home/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/sites/0.1.75/skills`\n- `r7` = `E:/CodexData/home/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/work-pets/0.1.6/skills`\n- `r8` = `E:/CodexData/home/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime`\n- `r9` = `E:/CodexData/home/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime/spreadsheets/26.905.11957/skills`\n- `r10` = `E:/CodexData/home/plugins/cache/personal`\n- `r11` = `E:/Program Files/better-genshin-impact-LCB/.agents/skills`\n### Available skills\n- imagegen: Generate or edit raster images when the task benefits from AI-created bitmap visuals such as photos, illustrations, textures, sprites, mockups, or transparent-background cutouts. Use when Codex should create a brand-new image, transform an existing image, or derive visual variants from references, and the output should be a bitmap asset rather than repo-native code or vector. Do not use when the task is better handled by editing existing SVG/vector/code-native assets, extending an established icon or logo system, or building the visual directly in HTML/CSS/canvas. (file: r2/imagegen/SKILL.md)\n- openai-docs: Use for Codex models/pricing, scheduled tasks, skills, settings, setup, troubleshooting, customization, automations, and self-knowledge—including 'you,' 'your,' 'this app,' or 'this coding agent' when they refer to Codex—and for OpenAI APIs/products and ChatGPT Work. Also use for model choice/migration, prompting, SDKs, Responses, Realtime, agents, evals, and Chat/Work/Codex comparisons. Do not use for generic app/software tasks that merely mention Codex. (file: r2/openai-docs/SKILL.md)\n- skill-creator: Create or update a Codex skill with appropriately scoped instructions and any needed supporting resources. (file: r2/skill-creator/SKILL.md)\n- skill-installer: Install Codex skills into $CODEX_HOME/skills from a curated list or a GitHub repo path. Use when a user asks to list installable skills, install a curated skill, or install a skill from another repo (including private repos). (file: r2/skill-installer/SKILL.md)\n- bgi-project-development: 为 BetterGI 茶包版开发检索并核实项目经验，定位双引擎和助手/服务端/BGI 跨端问题，并更新有证据的项目记忆。适用于此仓库的开发、排障、重构接力与知识整理；纯文件操作或其他项目不触发。 (file: r11/bgi-project-development/SKILL.md)\n- public-merge-assistant: 将公版 origin-lcb/main 的指定提交或更新合入当前 BetterGI 茶包分支，审计本地增量、双引擎路由及回归风险。用于优选公版、同步上游或解决此方向的冲突；茶包功能向公版提 PR 使用 teabag-pr-upstream-assistant。 (file: r11/public-merge-assistant/SKILL.md)\n- teabag-pr-upstream-assistant: 将 BetterGI 茶包功能抽取到公版基线的独立 worktree，审计代码和资源依赖、整理最小功能差异及 PR 提交。用于茶包向公版贡献功能；上游合入茶包使用 public-merge-assistant。 (file: r11/teabag-pr-upstream-assistant/SKILL.md)\n- teabag-refactor-assistant: 按 BetterGI 茶包功能清单开展或接力指定功能的结构重构，核实双引擎与调用方、保持既有行为、减少公版侵入并记录进度。用于茶包功能隔离及重构接力，不自动启动旧 Spec 或执行整份待办。 (file: r11/teabag-refactor-assistant/SKILL.md)\n- codex: 将编码、代码库探索、实现、评审和验证任务委托给持久化 Codex CLI Agent。仅当用户明确要求“用 Codex”“让 Codex 执行”，或要求继续某个 Codex Agent 任务时使用。 (file: r0/codex/SKILL.md)\n- computer-use:computer-use: Control Windows apps from ChatGPT (file: r3/computer-use/26.1002.51308/skills/computer-use/SKILL.md)\n- documents:documents: Create, edit, redline, and comment on `.docx`, Word, and Google Docs-targeted document artifacts inside the container, with a strict render-and-verify workflow. Use `render_docx.py` to generate page PNGs (and optional PDF) for visual QA, then iterate until layout is flawless before delivering the final document. (file: r8/documents/26.905.11957/skills/documents/SKILL.md)\n- gpt-workspace-executor:gpt-workspace-executor: Use when the user explicitly asks for \"GPT会诊\", \"用GPT分析\", \"用GPT审核\", or invokes $gpt-workspace-executor. GPT provides scoped read-only consultation through MCP while the primary model continues execution. (file: r10/gpt-workspace-executor/0.1.0+codex.20260923130610/skills/gpt-workspace-executor/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes: Mandatory entry point: read this first for any request to make, create, edit, animate, or render a video, animation, or motion graphic, including a promo, explainer, captioned clip, title card, overlay, slideshow or interactive deck, Remotion port, or any HyperFrames HTML composition. Also use it to inspect, diagnose, validate, preview, publish, or batch-render an existing HyperFrames project. Inputs may be a website URL, GitHub PR, Figma design or URL, text or brief, existing footage, or music. It resumes project state, captures intent when applicable, selects and installs the owning workflow, and routes domain capabilities. HyperFrames is the default output framework unless the user explicitly chooses another framework for the deliverable or asks only to record a browser session. (file: r1/hyperframes/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes: Mandatory entry point: read this first for any request to make, create, edit, animate, or render a video, animation, or motion graphic, including a promo, explainer, captioned clip, title card, overlay, slideshow or interactive deck, Remotion port, or any HyperFrames HTML composition. Also use it to inspect, diagnose, validate, preview, publish, or batch-render an existing HyperFrames project. Inputs may be a website URL, GitHub PR, Figma design or URL, text or brief, existing footage, or music. It resumes project state, captures intent when applicable, selects and installs the owning workflow, and routes domain capabilities. HyperFrames is the default output framework unless the user explicitly chooses another framework for the deliverable or asks only to record a browser session. (file: r0/hyperframes/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-animation: All animation knowledge for HyperFrames — atomic motion rules, multi-phase scene blueprints, scene transitions, broader motion-design techniques, AND the seven runtime adapters (GSAP default, plus Lottie, Three.js, Anime.js, CSS keyframes, Web Animations API, TypeGPU). Use for any motion or animation task: pick 2-4 rules and compose, or load a blueprint, or look up runtime-specific API (e.g. GSAP eases / Lottie player / Three.js mixer). Also covers auditing an existing composition's choreography (animation map) and 24 named text-animation effects. HyperFrames-native: single paused timeline, seek-safe, deterministic. (file: r1/hyperframes-animation/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-animation: All animation knowledge for HyperFrames — atomic motion rules, multi-phase scene blueprints, scene transitions, broader motion-design techniques, AND the seven runtime adapters (GSAP default, plus Lottie, Three.js, Anime.js, CSS keyframes, Web Animations API, TypeGPU). Use for any motion or animation task: pick 2-4 rules and compose, or load a blueprint, or look up runtime-specific API (e.g. GSAP eases / Lottie player / Three.js mixer). Also covers auditing an existing composition's choreography (animation map) and 24 named text-animation effects. HyperFrames-native: single paused timeline, seek-safe, deterministic. (file: r0/hyperframes-animation/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-audio: Use when audio already placed in a HyperFrames composition needs to be mixed: fade-in/fade-out, crossfade, track gain or volume, volume automation, ducking, a music bed that fights a voiceover (voiceover carve), effects on a track (EQ, compressor, limiter, gate, saturation, delay, reverb, chorus, phaser, bitcrush), automation envelopes drawn on a track's volume or any effect parameter, or one submix bus carrying a chain, a fader and an automation clock for several tracks at once (`<hf-audio-group>`). Don't use for sourcing or generating audio — finding BGM, SFX, or making a voiceover is `/media-use`. Don't use for clip timing or track layout, which is `/hyperframes-core`. (file: r1/hyperframes-audio/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-audio: Use when audio already placed in a HyperFrames composition needs to be mixed: fade-in/fade-out, crossfade, track gain or volume, volume automation, ducking, a music bed that fights a voiceover (voiceover carve), effects on a track (EQ, compressor, limiter, gate, saturation, delay, reverb, chorus, phaser, bitcrush), automation envelopes drawn on a track's volume or any effect parameter, or one submix bus carrying a chain, a fader and an automation clock for several tracks at once (`<hf-audio-group>`). Don't use for sourcing or generating audio — finding BGM, SFX, or making a voiceover is `/media-use`. Don't use for clip timing or track layout, which is `/hyperframes-core`. (file: r0/hyperframes-audio/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-cli: Use the HyperFrames CLI development loop: init, add, catalog, capture, lint, check, snapshot, compare, grade-compare, preview, play, present, beats, keyframes, single or batch render, publish, cloud, cloudrun, feedback, lambda, doctor, browser, info, upgrade, skills, compositions, timeline, history, clean, docs, benchmark, telemetry, transcribe, auth, tts, and remove-background. Also use when diagnosing build or render failures. validate, inspect, and layout are deprecated aliases; use check. Covers local, HeyGen-hosted cloud, AWS Lambda, and Google Cloud Run rendering. (file: r1/hyperframes-cli/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-cli: Use the HyperFrames CLI development loop: init, add, catalog, capture, lint, check, snapshot, compare, grade-compare, preview, play, present, beats, keyframes, single or batch render, publish, cloud, cloudrun, feedback, lambda, doctor, browser, info, upgrade, skills, compositions, timeline, history, clean, docs, benchmark, telemetry, transcribe, auth, tts, and remove-background. Also use when diagnosing build or render failures. validate, inspect, and layout are deprecated aliases; use check. Covers local, HeyGen-hosted cloud, AWS Lambda, and Google Cloud Run rendering. (file: r0/hyperframes-cli/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-core: The HyperFrames composition contract — build one renderable project. Use for composition structure, the `data-*` timing attributes, `class=\"clip\"`, tracks, sub-compositions, variables, framework-owned media playback, deterministic-render rules, and validation. Read before writing composition HTML. (file: r1/hyperframes-core/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-core: The HyperFrames composition contract — build one renderable project. Use for composition structure, the `data-*` timing attributes, `class=\"clip\"`, tracks, sub-compositions, variables, framework-owned media playback, deterministic-render rules, and validation. Read before writing composition HTML. (file: r0/hyperframes-core/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-creative: Non-animation creative direction for HyperFrames videos. Use for design spec (frame.md / design.md) handling, palettes, typography, narration, beat planning, audio-reactive visuals, composition patterns, and brand / style decisions. For atomic motion patterns and scene blueprints, use `hyperframes-animation`. (file: r1/hyperframes-creative/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-creative: Non-animation creative direction for HyperFrames videos. Use for design spec (frame.md / design.md) handling, palettes, typography, narration, beat planning, audio-reactive visuals, composition patterns, and brand / style decisions. For atomic motion patterns and scene blueprints, use `hyperframes-animation`. (file: r0/hyperframes-creative/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-keyframes: Use when a HyperFrames composition needs a punch-in, punch-out, zoom, reframe, Ken Burns treatment, camera move, visual match/whip handoff, or other seek-safe 2D/3D keyframes; also for GSAP, CSS keyframes, Anime.js, WAAPI, FLIP, paths, masks, SVG morph/draw, text trails, 3D depth, or `hyperframes keyframes` diagnostics. Don't use for broad scene strategy, brand design, media sourcing, captions, or general video planning. (file: r1/hyperframes-keyframes/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-keyframes: Use when a HyperFrames composition needs a punch-in, punch-out, zoom, reframe, Ken Burns treatment, camera move, visual match/whip handoff, or other seek-safe 2D/3D keyframes; also for GSAP, CSS keyframes, Anime.js, WAAPI, FLIP, paths, masks, SVG morph/draw, text trails, 3D depth, or `hyperframes keyframes` diagnostics. Don't use for broad scene strategy, brand design, media sourcing, captions, or general video planning. (file: r0/hyperframes-keyframes/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-registry: Search, install, and wire registry blocks and components into HyperFrames compositions. Use BEFORE hand-building any named visual — whenever a brief, a user, or a storyboard names a look, effect, treatment, or transition such as CRT scanlines, glitch, chromatic aberration, film grain, a shimmer sweep, a chart, a code or terminal window, a map, or a confetti burst — because roughly 400 hosted items already cover many of them and the search ranks all of them with nothing installed, no project, and no account. Also use when running hyperframes add or hyperframes catalog, installing one item or every block matching a tag, wiring an installed item into index.html, or working with hyperframes.json. Covers discovery, install locations, block sub-composition wiring, component snippet merging, and authoring a new block or component to contribute upstream (idea → scaffold → validate → PR). (file: r1/hyperframes-registry/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-registry: Search, install, and wire registry blocks and components into HyperFrames compositions. Use BEFORE hand-building any named visual — whenever a brief, a user, or a storyboard names a look, effect, treatment, or transition such as CRT scanlines, glitch, chromatic aberration, film grain, a shimmer sweep, a chart, a code or terminal window, a map, or a confetti burst — because roughly 400 hosted items already cover many of them and the search ranks all of them with nothing installed, no project, and no account. Also use when running hyperframes add or hyperframes catalog, installing one item or every block matching a tag, wiring an installed item into index.html, or working with hyperframes.json. Covers discovery, install locations, block sub-composition wiring, component snippet merging, and authoring a new block or component to contribute upstream (idea → scaffold → validate → PR). (file: r0/hyperframes-registry/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-studio: Use when working with a person on a HyperFrames project in Studio: first, whether their message asks for a change at all (questions, loose ideas and \"don't change anything\" get an answer and a plan, not an edit); for a new film, the plan, storyboard and build order that the HyperFrames launch films follow; and how the timeline should be laid out so it reads well (one caption track, one element kind per track, every scene a sub-composition) and where captions and key content may sit (safe zones). Don't use for how to perform an individual edit (split, trim, retime, volume, copy, swap): that is `creator-editing-recipes.md` in `/hyperframes-core`. (file: r1/hyperframes-studio/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-studio: Use when working with a person on a HyperFrames project in Studio: first, whether their message asks for a change at all (questions, loose ideas and \"don't change anything\" get an answer and a plan, not an edit); for a new film, the plan, storyboard and build order that the HyperFrames launch films follow; and how the timeline should be laid out so it reads well (one caption track, one element kind per track, every scene a sub-composition) and where captions and key content may sit (safe zones). Don't use for how to perform an individual edit (split, trim, retime, volume, copy, swap): that is `creator-editing-recipes.md` in `/hyperframes-core`. (file: r0/hyperframes-studio/SKILL.md)\n- liangshen: 梁神模式——两阶段会话行为协议（复刻自 DSH 的 liangshen preset）：首轮以极简面工作（仅 shell 与文件编辑、不写计划、不派子代理），首轮完成后铺开完整工作流。仅在用户以 $liangshen 显式调用时启用，不要自动套用。 (file: r0/liangshen/SKILL.md)\n- media-use: Agent Media OS, the single skill for every media need in a HyperFrames project. Resolve BGM, SFX, image, icon, brand logo, voice, color grade, or LUT into a frozen local file or paste-ready block + ledger record (one verb, `resolve`); generate via TTS / music / image models when the catalog misses; produce voiceover, transcription, captions, and background removal through one shared audio engine; operate on media (cut / reframe / transform); and reuse assets across projects. Also use for vague feedback that real footage looks dark, flat, boring, should feel retro/camcorder/print/ASCII, needs privacy, or needs a media reveal. (file: r1/media-use/SKILL.md)\n- media-use: Agent Media OS, the single skill for every media need in a HyperFrames project. Resolve BGM, SFX, image, icon, brand logo, voice, color grade, or LUT into a frozen local file or paste-ready block + ledger record (one verb, `resolve`); generate via TTS / music / image models when the catalog misses; produce voiceover, transcription, captions, and background removal through one shared audio engine; operate on media (cut / reframe / transform); and reuse assets across projects. Also use for vague feedback that real footage looks dark, flat, boring, should feel retro/camcorder/print/ASCII, needs privacy, or needs a media reveal. (file: r0/media-use/SKILL.md)\n- mistletoe-independent-review: 为槲寄生批次执行独立方案审查、实现审查和修复复核；审查者可自主只读追查完整项目及入口外依赖，保存原生来源、阶段结果和原级问题。适用于本项目审查设施和产品批次，不自动启动其他旧任务。 (file: r0/mistletoe-independent-review/SKILL.md)\n- pages:maintain-space: Reconcile new evidence into existing ChatGPT Pages or a Space when the user requests upkeep. For a direct text correction, use write-page. Do not use for ordinary chat drafts, writing, or advice, or treat a selected Page as a request to save. Schedule future upkeep only when requested. (file: r4/maintain-space/SKILL.md)\n- pages:manage-schedules: Review a ChatGPT Space page and its schedules, recommend useful recurring work, and create, update, or remove scheduled automations. (file: r4/manage-schedules/SKILL.md)\n- pages:organize-space: Organize existing ChatGPT Pages and Space structure when the user requests changes to that structure. Do not use for ordinary chat drafts or advice; a selected Page alone does not authorize reorganization. A narrow text edit does not need this workflow. (file: r4/organize-space/SKILL.md)\n- pages:write-page: Create or edit requested Page/Space content, or use for prose you have already decided to save as a standalone Markdown file, only if the user did not explicitly request a Markdown file. Honor established formats, destinations, and repository documentation. A selected Page alone does not authorize a write. (file: r4/write-page/SKILL.md)\n- pdf:pdf: Read, create, inspect, render, and verify PDF files where visual layout matters, including fillable AcroForms. Use Poppler rendering plus Python tools such as reportlab, pdfplumber, and pypdf for generation and extraction. (file: r8/pdf/26.905.11957/skills/pdf/SKILL.md)\n- plugin-management:plugin-management: Discover and suggest relevant plugins, inspect app permissions and dependencies, and manage plugin connections or removal. Use when the user asks about plugins or when a task would materially benefit from an external app, account, service, or data source that available tools cannot access. (file: r5/plugin-management/0.1.0/skills/plugin-management/SKILL.md)\n- presentations:Presentations: Read, create or edit PowerPoint or Google Slides decks. Use for presentation, slide deck, PowerPoint, PPT, PPTX, or Google Slides requests. (file: r8/presentations/26.905.11957/skills/presentations/SKILL.md)\n- requesting-code-review: Use when completing tasks, implementing major features, or before merging to verify work meets requirements (file: r0/mistletoe-independent-review/references/upstream/skills/requesting-code-review/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-building: Use Sites when the user wants a complete website built for them, such as a landing page, portfolio, dashboard, portal, tracker, hub, or internal tool, or wants to modify a website built with Sites. Do not use for development work in other web projects unless the user explicitly requests Sites. (file: r6/sites-building/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-hosting: Host websites with Sites. Use after `sites-building` to publish new sites and edits, for requested website publishing or deployment, or for hosting management. A project containing `.openai/hosting.json` uses Sites hosting only when the current request concerns that Site. Publishing an npm package or standalone asset is not website publishing. Honor an explicit request to use another hosting provider. (file: r6/sites-hosting/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-mcp: Build or update a Site-hosted MCP server and help users access its tools through the Site's plugin in ChatGPT or Codex. (file: r6/sites-mcp/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-preview-troubleshooting: Diagnose and recover failed supervised sites-preview sessions after sites-building. Applies only to the managed-linux execution profile, not portable previews. (file: r6/sites-preview-troubleshooting/SKILL.md)\n- spreadsheets:Spreadsheets: Use skill when user requests to create, modify, analyze, visualize, or work with spreadsheet files (`.xlsx`, `.xls`, `.csv`, `.tsv`) or Google Sheets with formulas, formatting, charts, tables, and recalculation. Do not use for live controlling Microsoft Excel app or a live Excel session. (file: r9/spreadsheets/SKILL.md)\n- spreadsheets:excel-live-control: Control an open or active Microsoft Excel workbook through the ChatGPT add-in or connected session. Use when the user tags the Microsoft Excel app in Codex or follows up on an established live Excel task. Do not use for standalone spreadsheet files or Google Sheets. (file: r9/excel-live-control/SKILL.md)\n- template-creator:template-creator: Create or update a reusable personal Codex artifact-template skill. Use when the user invokes $template-creator or asks in natural language to create a reusable template from a reference document, presentation, spreadsheet, Google Docs, Slides, or Sheets link, ImageGen or Product Design image, email, Slack message, or Site project, or explicitly asks to edit or update a passed artifact-template skill. Do not use for one-off creation from an existing template. (file: r8/template-creator/26.905.11957/skills/template-creator/SKILL.md)\n- visualize:visualize: Create visualizations and interactive tools directly in conversation. Proactively use to show how something works; explore 'what happens when', 'what changes', or 'help me understand'; compare or inspect; create simulations, maps, charts, graphs, and mockups. Use standard tools for static scientific figures. (file: r3/visualize/1.0.47/skills/visualize/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:create-pet: Create, repair, validate, preview, upload, or activate an animated v2 pet in ChatGPT Work mode from a character idea, brand cue, or reference image. Use for new ChatGPT Pets, custom mascots, non-pixel styles, and unattached sprite sheets requiring nine animation states plus sixteen look directions. Preserve Library artifacts and Pets MCP lifecycle behavior. Exclude real pets, standalone images, and other-app pets; clarify before invoking. (file: r7/create-pet/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:pets: List, inspect, select, download, or delete animated pets in ChatGPT Work mode. Use for an explicit pet in ChatGPT or established ChatGPT Pets context. Exclude real-world and other-app pets; clarify before invoking. (file: r7/pets/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:update-pet: Inspect, validate, preview, repair, or update a custom pet in ChatGPT Work mode, including its name, description, or sprite sheet. Use for a pet in ChatGPT or established ChatGPT Pets context. Exclude real-world and other-app pets; clarify before invoking. (file: r7/update-pet/SKILL.md)\n</skills_instructions>"},{"type":"input_text","text":"<permissions instructions>\nFilesystem sandboxing defines which files can be read or written. `sandbox_mode` is `danger-full-access`: No filesystem sandboxing - all commands are permitted. Network access is enabled.\nApproval policy is currently never. Do not provide the `sandbox_permissions` for any reason, commands will be rejected.\r\n</permissions instructions>"},{"type":"input_text","text":"<collaboration_mode># Collaboration Mode: Default\n\nYou are now in Default mode. Any previous instructions for other modes (e.g. Plan mode) are no longer active.\n\nYour active mode changes only when new developer instructions with a different `<collaboration_mode>...</collaboration_mode>` change it; user requests or tool descriptions do not change mode by themselves. Known mode names are Default and Plan.\n\n## request_user_input availability\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only when it is listed in the available tools for this turn.\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only for optional questions where the answer would materially improve the quality of the work.\n\nIf `request_user_input` returns no answers, continue with best judgment instead of asking again or treating the turn as blocked.\n\nNever use the `request_user_input` tool for permission requests or permission-related escalations.\n</collaboration_mode>"},{"type":"input_text","text":"<recommended_plugins>\nHere is a list of plugins that are available but not installed.\n\n- Dropbox (app-69b31dc2110c8191b8b47dc98fe5a052@openai-curated-remote)\n- Box (box@openai-curated-remote)\n- Codex Security (codex-security@openai-curated-remote)\n- Figma (figma@openai-curated-remote)\n- Gmail (gmail@openai-curated-remote)\n- Google Calendar (google-calendar@openai-curated-remote)\n- Google Drive (google-drive@openai-curated-remote)\n- Linear (linear@openai-curated-remote)\n- Notion (notion@openai-curated-remote)\n- OpenAI Developers (openai-developers@openai-curated-remote)\n- Outlook Calendar (outlook-calendar@openai-curated-remote)\n- Outlook Email (outlook-email@openai-curated-remote)\n- SharePoint (sharepoint@openai-curated-remote)\n- Slack (slack@openai-curated-remote)\n- Teams (teams@openai-curated-remote)\n</recommended_plugins>"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a117b6-4012-7383-9a7b-a9e632df39b2","create_time":1791399187.5995984,"content_item_kinds":["generic.developer_instructions","memories.instructions","host_skills.instructions","permissions.instructions","collaboration_mode.instructions","plugins.recommendations"]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T18:53:07.599Z","ordinal":3,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a117b6-548f-7163-8de6-1f16f24d6646","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"<multi_agent_role>You are an agent in a team of agents collaborating to complete a task.\n\nYou can spawn sub-agents to handle subtasks, and those sub-agents can spawn their own sub-agents. All agents in the team, including the agents that you can assign tasks to, are equally intelligent and capable, and have access to the same set of tools.\n\nYou can use `spawn_agent` to create a new agent, `followup_task` to give an existing agent a new task and trigger a turn, and `send_message` to pass a message to a running agent.\n`send_message` calls may be read by a human, so ensure they are legible. Always put proper spaces between words and/or numbers.\nChild agents can also spawn their own sub-agents.\n\nWhen you provide a response in the final channel, that content is immediately delivered back to your parent agent.\nIn addition, your final answer may be read by a human, so ensure it is legible.\n\nYou will receive messages in the analysis channel in the form:\n```\nMessage Type: NEW_TASK | MESSAGE | FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: <recipient>\nSender: <author>\nPayload:\n<payload text>\n```\nYou may also see them addressed as to=/root/..., which indicates your identity is /root/...\n\nNote that collaboration tools cannot be called from inside `functions.exec`. Call `spawn_agent`, `send_message`, `followup_task`, `wait_agent`, `interrupt_agent`, and `list_agents` only as direct tool calls using the recipient shown in their tool definitions, such as `to=functions.collaboration.spawn_agent`, since they are intentionally absent from the `functions.exec` `tools.*` namespace. Available tools in `functions.exec` are explicitly described with a `tools` namespace in the developer message.\n\nAll agents share the same directory. In detail:\n- All agents have access to the same container and filesystem as you.\n- All agents use the same current working directory.\n- As a result, edits made by one agent are immediately visible to all other agents.\n\nWhen calling `wait_agent`, prefer longer waits (minutes) to avoid busy polling.\n\nThere are 4 available concurrency slots, meaning that up to 4 agents can be active at once, including you.\n\nFull-history forks (`fork_turns` omitted or `\"all\"`) inherit the parent model and reasoning effort and do not accept overrides. Only set `model` or `reasoning_effort` when explicitly requested by the user, applicable `AGENTS.md` instructions, or skill instructions; when doing so, set `fork_turns` to `\"none\"` or a positive integer string.</multi_agent_role>"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a117b6-4012-7383-9a7b-a9e632df39b2","create_time":1791399187.5995986,"content_item_kinds":["multi_agent.role_instructions"]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T18:53:07.599Z","ordinal":4,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a117b6-548f-7163-8de6-1f2e030eff1a","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"<multi_agent_mode>Any earlier instruction enabling proactive multi-agent delegation no longer applies. Do not spawn sub-agents unless the user or applicable AGENTS.md/skill instructions explicitly ask for sub-agents, delegation, or parallel agent work.</multi_agent_mode>"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a117b6-4012-7383-9a7b-a9e632df39b2","create_time":1791399187.599599,"content_item_kinds":["multi_agent.mode_instructions"]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T18:53:07.599Z","ordinal":5,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a117b6-548f-7163-8de6-1f362e4390ac","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"# AGENTS.md instructions for E:\\Program Files\\better-genshin-impact-LCB\n\n<INSTRUCTIONS>\n﻿# 全局协作约定（适用于所有项目）\r\n\r\n## 0. 自动交接与Goal生命周期闭环（2026-10-04用户明确授权）\r\n\r\n政策 ID：`handoff-auto-create-20261004-v1`。用户在侧聊 `01a102e9-6086-7440-b082-c32ecf10b44f` 明确要求：“那你就把现在的流程改成这样吧，自动创建新会话，是否可以。”这是对必要施工交接自动创建接续聊天并一次发送完整提示词的常驻授权，不再逐次请求确认；覆盖本文件、项目入口及旧Skill/提示词中冲突的“不自动创建聊天”“让用户手动粘贴”规则。原2026-10-03必要交接暂停自身Goal的常驻授权继续有效。\r\n\r\n- 只用于本聊天真实执行目标的跨会话交接；普通答复、侧聊审阅、流程维护或他人任务不触发施工接力，不据此暂停主聊天或其他聊天Goal。本轮规则维护不触发主任务换会话。\r\n- 仍按任务语义决定是否交接：可验证批次边界、切换独立目标或有可定位的上下文判断风险。仅时间长、工具多、普通一次编译错误不足以强制切换；跨文件一致性尚需连续推理且能安全推进时继续当前会话。仅是可选优化、尚未决定交接时保持Goal原状态并继续安全工作。\r\n- 决定交接后先完成并核对当前安全操作，保存目标、已完成/未完成、分支/HEAD/工作区、验证/失败、原级未决责任、在途任务终态或责任及唯一下一项。保护未提交成果，不制造干净工作区；源码/测试写入或突变恢复未结束时不得启动接班写者。\r\n- 查询自身Goal；未完成Goal调用原生暂停并再次查询确认同一Goal为paused，已paused保持原状。无Goal不为交接临时创建；真正已完成Goal保持complete。暂停不可用、失败或未知时不创建接班施工聊天，保存现场并只提出必要的用户暂停操作；不改Goal数据库、不伪造标记、不把未完成目标标complete。\r\n- 准备一个完整、自包含的接续提示词，首行为 `/goal <完整目标摘要>`，包含结果、约束、完成判据及从审计到实施/修复、验证和收口的全部要求、权威材料、原历史/opening/计数与受保护边界。全部要求放在同一初始消息，不再让用户复制，不拆成Goal与正文两次发送，不提前创建多个阶段。记录唯一交接标记和来源聊天，便于核对而非重开原批次账。\r\n- 原Goal暂停确认、旧执行者已停止写入后，先用 `list_projects` 核对当前项目/路径/host，调用 `create_thread` 自动创建恰好一个接续聊天并一次发送完整提示词。仓库任务默认使用同项目local，沿用原工作区，不新克隆、不换worktree；当前目录无法准确对应可用项目时保持阻断并提供人工回退，不误选项目。默认不指定模型；仅按用户已明确的模型要求显式设置，不擅自换模型或降低审查强度。\r\n- **自动接班继承模型（2026-10-04用户明确要求）**：政策ID `handoff-inherit-model-20261004-v1`。真实施工交接必须继承来源聊天当时实际使用的模型及推理档位，不固定为K3/GPT或某个强度，也不依赖全局默认、桌面缓存或owner手动选择。交接前只读核对来源聊天当前rollout中最近有效 `turn_context` 的 `model` 与 `effort`/`reasoning_effort`（以及 `collaboration_mode.settings.model` / `reasoning_effort`，如存在须一致），记录来源threadId和证据；调用 `create_thread` 时显式传入该实际 `model` 与对应 `thinking`。完整初始提示词写明继承值及本政策，后续接班按各自来源聊天的当前实际值继续继承，用户后来主动换模型/档位时以换后值为准。创建后只读核验新聊天当前rollout中实际模型及档位与来源一致，不能只凭提示词、自述、入参或标签认定生效；未知、字段冲突、模型/档位不支持或不一致时不得启动接班写入，保留已创建身份、报告具体阻断，不重复创建、不静默换模型或降档。仅当前用户明确指定接班改用别的模型/档位时覆盖继承值，默认配置修改本身不视为强制切换在途聊天的指令。本条覆盖上文默认不指定模型及旧固定K3 MAX要求；不改变独立会诊/审查的既有模型和强度，不切换旧聊天、不触发额外交接、不重启应用。\r\n- 创建返回即记录threadId/hostId；用 `wait_threads` 等待并核对新聊天已接收交接标记、实际cwd及自身完整Goal。新执行者先查询自身Goal，不存在时只建立一次并读回active；存在时核对完整范围。通过create_thread发送的 `/goal` 文字实测不会自动建Goal，不能据此宣称Goal已存在。新聊天在正确项目/Goal读回成立前不得改代码；不恢复旧Goal、不重置原包历史或审查义务。\r\n- 创建结果未知/超时先核对已创建聊天及其终态，禁止盲目重试或重复开接班写者。已创建但首轮失败/新Goal未确认时保留该聊天身份和旧paused状态，报告唯一必要操作；不自动再建一个、不把失败改成成功。仅在创建工具不可用或失败且已确认未创建接班聊天时，回退为一个完整 `/goal` 代码块供用户整块一次发送。旧Goal暂停未确认时不提供可立即施工的接班提示词。\r\n- 自动接班确认后最终给新聊天入口和 `::created-thread{threadId=\"实际返回ID\"}`，简述交接理由及Goal真实状态，无需再粘贴施工正文；对文本守卫使用“旧Goal状态：paused”（或真正complete/none）及“新Goal状态：active”。这些状态必须来自原生查询，不是自述证明。明确原总目标若未完成仍未完成，旧聊天停工；新Goal接续施工不意味着产品交付。\r\n- 已暂停旧聊天的缓存自动续做不恢复施工；只有用户明确选择继续原聊天，且先核对自动创建的接班聊天已停止写入/无在途写者，才可撤销停工，避免两边同时施工。侧聊不代操作其他Goal或自动干预在途聊天。\r\n- 本流程由执行者调用原生能力；hooks只提醒/检查文本，不创建聊天、不读取或修改Goal数据库、不新增hooks、心跳、定时器、时间盒或后台服务，不调低上下文安全网。已运行聊天须显式读回新规则，跨新工作区/机器确认入口存在，不承诺机械保证或永久热加载。\r\n\r\n## 1. 长任务：先明确\"什么时候才可以停\"\r\n\r\n允许结束本轮并等待用户输入的情况只有四种：\r\n\r\n1. 需要用户做产品/业务决策，且无法从现有文档、代码或既有约定中自行判定；\r\n2. 遇到外部阻塞（权限、网络、账号、依赖不可用），且已尝试合理的替代路径；\r\n3. 用户给定的\"完成判定\"已全部满足。\r\n4. 长任务经下述任务语义评估决定交接，已完成当前安全操作并交付可复核的交接材料。用户已授权这种计划性交接；交接不等于目标完成。\r\n\r\n以下都不是停下来的理由，禁止因此收尾等用户：\r\n\r\n- 等用户确认你已经能自己判定的事；\r\n- 等会诊/评审/复核返回（应当批量安排或在本轮内等待，不要把它变成检查点）；\r\n- 等\"更干净的方案\"；\r\n- 每轮例行汇报、\"我先给你看一下\"、\"下一步我会去做…\"。\r\n\r\n\"我下一轮继续…\"这类收尾按违规处理：要么本轮继续做完，要么落到上面四种允许停的情况之一，并写清是哪一种。\r\n\r\n## 2. 用户说\"不要停 / 一次性做完 / 直到完成\"时\r\n\r\n- 主动提醒并建议使用目标模式（在输入框输入 `/goal <完整目标摘要>`，目标文字与命令同一行），并把目标写成「结果 + 约束 + 怎么算完成」三要素；\r\n- 用户已开启目标模式或已配置定时任务时，不要再索取\"继续\"确认；按第 3 节提供有证据的进度，不用重复空泛汇报；\r\n- 一轮内尽量把可以自行判定的动作链连续做完，再统一汇报。\r\n\r\n## 3. 大型开发的任务批次、进度与跨会话交接\r\n\r\n- 开始前把总目标拆成可独立验证的小批次。一个批次只解决一个具体状态转换、入口或故障；写明完成判据、针对性证据、受影响回归和生产门。不要给整个跨端项目设一个需要十几个小时连续运行的单会话批次。\r\n- 开工时记录时间；每完成一笔提交，或连续工作约 45 分钟，向用户报一次有信息量的进度：已完成与提交号、当前验证、下一项、阻断。不要用“还在审查”代替进度。\r\n- 以任务语义判断是否交接：完成聚焦批次、切换到独立目标、或上下文质量有可定位风险时，比较继续与切分的成本。允许需要连续推理、跨文件强一致性的任务在一个会话内完成。90 分钟仅作为本约定明确保留的决策提醒，不是质量阈值或硬上限；有效的继续决策不因时间、工具数或提交数增长而失效。正在进行测试、写入或安全关键转换时先完成并核对，不能为赶时间截断、放宽质量门或擅自开生产门。\r\n- 交接前核实分支、HEAD、已跟踪／未跟踪工作区、提交范围、针对性与完整回归及失败身份、会诊模型／强度／次数和未取得结论的错误；把“已实现、仅设计、未验证、阻断”分开。仓库任务写一份短交接文件，链接权威设计而不复制整本历史；按第0节自动创建同项目接续聊天并发送完整提示词，只有确认无接班聊天的失败回退才给可粘贴提示词。未提交工作如实列出，不能为制造干净工作区而覆盖或删除。\r\n- 必要跨会话续办按第0节自动创建并核验接班聊天；不能自动创建且已确认无接班聊天时，人工回退提示词的唯一代码块首行须为 `/goal <本批完整目标摘要>`，目标文字与命令同一行，其余要求可在同块分行。新会话开工先查询并读回本线程 active Goal，核对它覆盖完整批次；若未建立，执行者自行调用 Goal 工具建立并读回，工具不可用则报告阻断，不得仅凭用户消息里的 `/goal` 字样认定已建立，也不得先改代码。原会话 GOAL 不会自动传到新会话，也不能把中途交接标为总目标完成。不能自动新建会话时，清楚提醒用户粘贴提示词；不要声称定时器能强制中断正在运行的任务。\r\n- 以上适用于所有项目；项目特殊质量门禁继续生效。短小任务无需刻意拆分，用户给出更短时间盒时按用户要求。\r\n\r\n## 4. 改动的安全边界（防误写、防越界）\r\n\r\n- 批量修改文件前后必须自检：改前记录大小/行数或 hash，改后复核；出现大幅缩水立即用 git 还原并重做。\r\n- 改完用 `git diff --stat` 复核改动范围，与预期不符就停下核查。\r\n- 提交只用 `git commit --only -m \"<msg>\" -- <files>`（只提交本次明确改动的文件），禁止 `git add -A` / `git add .`。\r\n- 未经用户明确要求，不执行 `rm -rf`、`git reset --hard`、`git checkout -- <path>`、批量删除等破坏性操作。\r\n- 遇到\"文件被大量删除/丢失\"的现象时，先验证可读性与真实工作区状态（权限、沙箱、路径），再决定是否恢复，不要直接动手。\r\n- 构建或测试通过不等于运行验证通过；结论里如实标出\"未验证\"的部分。\r\n\r\n## 4.1 自动本地提交节点（2026-10-04）\r\n\r\n政策 ID：`auto-local-checkpoint-commit-20261004-v1`。针对已获授权的开发/修复/集成/文档维护，主动保存本地 Git 检查点，不再等待用户逐次提醒提交；只读讨论和他人材料不据此获写入授权。提交进度与审查、验收、生产许可及 Goal 完成分别判断。\r\n\r\n- 聚焦修复批完成影响相称验证、所有突变恢复并核对源码后，提交本批及配套依赖；后审修复完成回归后，再提交对应修复。共享状态/协议可合批，不按文件碎片化；不以“等整个项目验收”拖延阶段提交。\r\n- 正式收口仍按原审查/认证/实机等要求提交最终交付；阶段提交不得替代或伪造这些证据，也不自行关闭原级未决项。\r\n- 必要施工交接前，先核对并提交归属明确的本聊天成果，再记录最新HEAD/工作区、保存交接、暂停Goal并创建接班。未审/未验收写候选状态；保全失败或未验证进度可明确WIP及原级责任，不能写成通过。\r\n- 提交前核对分支/HEAD、暂存/未暂存/新增文件、写者、归属、依赖和证据，用明确文件列表 `git commit --only`；多行说明可用 `--file`。保护其他暂存和材料外工作，不整库提交/清理。提交后读回commit、实际文件集、工作区/暂存区并更新当前交接；原opening/历史/receipt不改绑。\r\n- 在途写入/构建/测试/突变恢复未终态时不提交中间变体；归属或依赖不明、身份漂移或提交失败，记录具体阻断和保存位置，继续其它安全工作。总Goal未完成、未做正式后审、有已知旧失败，本身不是通用不提交理由。\r\n- 默认自动本地提交；push/合并/发布/部署仍需相应授权及质量门。按任务语义触发，不按时间/工具数/回复轮次，不增加hooks、后台程序或强制交接。既有冻结请求回收期间不漂移其身份，待安全终态后提交并建立后续真实快照。\r\n\r\n## 5. 汇报方式\r\n\r\n- 用简体中文，结论先行，用最小必要格式。\r\n- 每轮结尾不要反问\"要不要继续\"，只说明：已完成什么、证据是什么、是否卡住。\r\n- 项目自己的 AGENTS.md 若有汇报格式约定，以项目为准；第 1 节禁止无故等待与第 3 节时间盒交接同时执行。\r\n\r\n## 6. 开发任务的会话交接提醒（轻量；2026-09-24 修订）\r\n\r\n- 当前需求：模型在开发过程中按任务语义判断是否需要换会话。可验证批次完成、要切换独立目标、或出现有证据的上下文质量风险时，比较继续与切分的代价。跨文件一致性或连续推理尚未完成时允许留在同一会话。时间和数量仅作提醒参考，不强制换会话。\r\n- 决定交接时，先结束正在进行的安全操作并核验结果；给用户简短说明：目标、已完成、验证与失败、未完成、工作区状态、下一步。按第0节先确认旧Goal暂停，再自动创建并核验一个接班聊天，无需用户粘贴；创建不可用且确认无接班聊天时才附唯一完整提示词。\r\n- 不要求每个开发/工具任务提交 JSON、文件 hash 或 `finish/continue/handoff/wait` 状态。不为了普通收尾运行脚本。需要准确交接的项目任务仍应把关键证据写在交接文件中，但模型可以按任务规模自行判断格式。\r\n- hooks.json 保留 6 个事件定义。SessionStart、PreCompact/PostCompact 只记轻量日志/压缩信号，PreToolUse 只执行原有危险命令拦截，UserPromptSubmit 注入简短提醒。\r\n- **Stop 事件（2026-09-26 修订）**：唯一挂载 `stop_continue.ps1`，职责为「停因守卫」——当收尾段落出现「稍后继续／等你发话／说了要做却没做」这类宣告时，用 `decision:block` 让模型把本轮可自行判定的部分做完。它**不是**时间盒强制交接：按工具数／分钟／提交数强制换会话的旧守卫已被用户否决，永久废除。规则只匹配**收尾 200 字符内**的明确停因句式，并先过合法停机白名单（需用户决策／外部阻塞／完成判据已满足／已交接），不做全文子串匹配。\r\n- 已废除的旧通道：① ZCode 侧 `stop_reconnect.ps1` 截断拉起（上游掐流过频、噪声大于收益，owner 于 2026-09-26 撤销，现为纯直通存根，见 `~/.tools/zcode-relay/README.md` §4.6）；② CODEX 侧同名截断识别脚本已从 hooks.json 摘除（脚本留档）。等价能力由 Stop 停因守卫 + 原生 `/goal` 空闲续做共同承担。\r\n- **长任务续跑的主力是原生 `/goal`**：目标持久化（`~/.codex/goals_1.sqlite` 的 `thread_goals`）+ 空闲自动续做（`thread_goal_continuation_deferrals`）。目标模式负责「别停」，停因守卫负责「别嘴上说继续」，两者叠加才等价于 ZCode 槲寄生链。\r\n- 回归与实证：`~/.codex/hooks/test/test_stop_continue.py`（27 项）与 `test_stop_limit.py`（死循环保护）；真实历史收尾 264 条样本误报 0；反向突变 5/5 检出；真机 `codex exec` 已复现 `Stop Blocked → 续做 → 第二次 Stop 放行`。\r\n- 改 `hooks.json` 定义后信任失效，**必须提醒用户去 `/hooks` 重新信任**，否则钩子静默跳过。\r\n- **hooks 配置在 Codex 进程启动时加载并缓存在内存，改动 `hooks.json` 后不会热重载。**（2026-09-26 实证）桌面版进程 13:33 启动后，14:29 定型的 `hooks.json`（Stop 仅 1 钩子）**未生效**，日志里仍持续出现已被摘除的 `reconnect:` 记录；而新起的 `codex exec` 进程读磁盘配置则 0 次 reconnect。**结论：改完 `hooks.json` 必须完全退出并重启桌面版 Codex（不是新建会话），否则磁盘与运行时不一致。**这也正是「会话总是自动停止」的成因之一——常驻进程里跑的仍是改动前的旧钩子组合。\r\n- 保持 Codex 默认上下文安全网：不得调低 `model_auto_compact_token_limit`，不得为了交接主动 `/compact`。Hooks 不能中断工具，也不能自行创建新会话。仅改脚本不用重新信任；若改 hooks.json 定义，需在 `/hooks` 审查并信任。\r\n- 方法依据和旧实现历史见 [需求汇总](handoff-mechanism-requirements-2026-09-24.md) 与 [修复记录](handoff-audit-20260924/ADVISORY-REPAIR.md)；旧报告描述的强制 JSON 流程已停用。\r\n- **普通答复与正文保留（2026-09-27修复）**：交接守卫只针对本会话真实施工边界、已选定后续任务或实际交付的施工提示词；讨论他人任务、提示词归属和仅提供裁决回复不因出现“下一批”就触发。用户只要裁决回复时，不代写下一批施工提示词。Stop拉起补齐后，最终回复必须完整重现用户所需正文、结论和必要操作，再补交接判断；不得只给补充说明或要求用户回看上一条。真实施工交接及停因守卫仍生效；按第0节自动创建接续聊天，不按时间/工具数强制切换。证据见 `hooks/test/evidence-reply-visibility-20260927/`；仅修改脚本，hooks.json未改，无需重新信任或重启。\n\n--- project-doc ---\n\n﻿# BGI 项目长期协作入口\r\n\r\n用户要求将 KIRO/KIMI 历史经验筛选为可持续使用的项目记忆。本文件保存常驻约定；按需流程及筛选依据由项目 Skill 承载。首次整理于 2026-09-16，技术事实仍需结合当前代码复核。\r\n\r\n## 施工存储止损（2026-10-05用户授权）\r\n\r\n采用 `mistletoe-storage-limits-20261005-v1`，复工先读 [存储限制](Docs/design/mistletoe-storage-limits.md)，核对工具bundle，并明确记录采用。新快照/取证/审查/audit必须经已接入预算入口，不用手工复制整树、换输出目录/渠道/工作树绕过额度；已知输入超限须在复制前拒绝。默认单次4 GiB、累计新材料16 GiB、余量8 GiB，配置见说明；这是受控工具限制，子进程监测及任意外部写入不能声称系统硬配额。历史报告/收据/唯一成果/User保持，禁止以清理为由丢证据；只清精确登记、未发布的自有scratch。Serena未纳管缓存明确停用，普通文件/rg审查保留。规则不自动恢复产品Goal，不改变原审查和实际交付门。\r\n\r\n## 本版交付法则（2026-10-05，优先于冲突旧流程）\r\n\r\n执行[本版交付法则](_workflow/usable-delivery-20261003/DELIVERY-FIRST-POLICY.md#2026-10-05-本版交付法则优先适用)，政策 ID `mistletoe-release-first-20261005-v2`。用户要求严格按完整可运行版本交付，禁止无关施工扩张。本节及政策正文优先于本文件下文、旧 Skill、旧 Goal 提示词中“先闭合全部历史/认证整个依赖生态”等冲突解释；不修改原报告、原等级、原预算，不伪成功、不削减原约定功能。\r\n\r\n- **现在做**：缺失或不可用的约定功能、正常旧数据合同、本版实际可达的误执行/数据覆盖/停止失效风险、影响相称验证、独立综合复核和新产物全功能实际运行/停止/重启/数据保留验收，交付版本与启动步骤。\r\n- **交付后做**：不妨碍完整使用的普通 BUG、维护性重构、无本版现实影响的历史/工具问题、无具体可达依据的极端组合穷举、新增未约定功能和通用证明/认证设施。保留原级 open 与延期依据，延期不是 closed。\r\n- **新增任务须准入**：在现有计划用一行绑定本版功能、具体缺口、入口/证据、用户后果、最小修复验证及下一交付项；只为完善机制/历史/工具且无本版收益者不得开工。重要等级不自动等于全局施工阻断；未知针对性查证、局部阻断，不无限扩为全源证明。\r\n- **固定收口方向**：在途突变先安全恢复；集中补功能和实际入口，稳定版本做回归/综合复核/实际验收，再交付。未决语义只阻断关联部分；禁止按小函数另开整包前审、不重开包/Goal/预算，不拿测试数量代替产品进展。\r\n- **诚实与采用证据**：源码候选、测试、新产物实机、版本交付分开；运行中执行者必须在下一安全选择边界读回政策 ID 并记录本版必做/延期/唯一下一项。文件修改不等于主聊天已采用；不保证永久热加载或零偏离。本轮规则维护不操作主 Goal、不发消息、不改产品源码、hooks 或工具 bundle。\r\n\r\n## 当前owner流程修订（2026-10-03，交付优先）\r\n\r\n- owner已要求纠正无休止前审，以快速完整交付为第一要务。执行[交付优先流程修订](_workflow/usable-delivery-20261003/DELIVERY-FIRST-POLICY.md)，政策ID `mistletoe-delivery-first-20261003-v1`；本节覆盖下文及旧Skill中冲突的“必须全包方案pass才能开始修复”和“所有历史重要项都必须先闭合”解释。\r\n- 已知行为、入口、写集、保护边界和反例明确后，owner授权定向修复：可以保留blocked及原级open义务进入红反例、代码、Rebuild和受控回归。前审最多首审加一次限定复核；技术修复不滚动进行第三轮纯方案审核。修复许可不开放生产或实际验收。\r\n- 缺失约定功能、误执行、数据风险、错误释放和未知假成功仍阻断交付；不妨碍完整功能使用的普通BUG按原级登记延期。完整功能、实际运行/停止/重启/数据保留、独立综合后审和必要因果验证保持。\r\n- 工具/无关历史不能阻断可独立安全推进的产品源码修复；使用既有渠道或等价可复核来源，不扩建工具，不自造pass/receipt，不删发现、不重置请求、不重建Goal。运行中执行者须显式读回新政策；旧冻结身份原样保留。\r\n\r\n- **自动交接闭环（2026-10-04用户常驻授权）**：采用全局AGENTS第0节 `handoff-auto-create-20261004-v1`，覆盖本入口、旧Skill及旧Goal提示词中冲突的“不自动创建聊天/用户手动粘贴”限制。真实施工交接先完成安全操作、保存现场、原生暂停自身未完成Goal并读回paused，再自动创建恰好一个同项目local接班聊天并一次发送完整提示词；新聊天先建立/核对自身完整Goal并读回active后才能写代码。创建失败/未知先核对已有聊天，不重复开写者；仅工具不可用或确认未创建时人工回退。普通侧聊不操作主Goal、不触发本次主施工交接，不按时间/工具数强制切换。详见[交付优先政策的交接条款](_workflow/usable-delivery-20261003/DELIVERY-FIRST-POLICY.md#会话交接与goal自动暂停)。后续不让owner重复授权或搬提示词。\r\n- **自动接班继承模型（2026-10-04用户明确要求）**：政策ID `handoff-inherit-model-20261004-v1`。真实施工交接必须继承来源聊天当时实际使用的模型及推理档位，不固定为K3/GPT或某个强度，也不依赖全局默认、桌面缓存或owner手动选择。交接前只读核对来源聊天当前rollout中最近有效 `turn_context` 的 `model` 与 `effort`/`reasoning_effort`（以及 `collaboration_mode.settings.model` / `reasoning_effort`，如存在须一致），记录来源threadId和证据；调用 `create_thread` 时显式传入该实际 `model` 与对应 `thinking`。完整初始提示词写明继承值及本政策，后续接班按各自来源聊天的当前实际值继续继承，用户后来主动换模型/档位时以换后值为准。创建后只读核验新聊天当前rollout中实际模型及档位与来源一致，不能只凭提示词、自述、入参或标签认定生效；未知、字段冲突、模型/档位不支持或不一致时不得启动接班写入，保留已创建身份、报告具体阻断，不重复创建、不静默换模型或降档。仅当前用户明确指定接班改用别的模型/档位时覆盖继承值，默认配置修改本身不视为强制切换在途聊天的指令。本条覆盖上文默认不指定模型及旧固定K3 MAX要求；不改变独立会诊/审查的既有模型和强度，不切换旧聊天、不触发额外交接、不重启应用。\r\n\r\n## 自动本地提交节点（2026-10-04）\r\n\r\n采用 `auto-local-checkpoint-commit-20261004-v1`，详见 [自动本地提交节点](Docs/design/automatic-local-commit-policy-20261004.md)及全局AGENTS第4.1节。已授权任务默认在聚焦修复验证后、后审修复回归后、正式收口及必要施工交接前主动本地提交，不等待owner逐次提醒。候选/WIP提交与独立审查、认证、真实验收和最终Goal完成分开；原级义务及发布门保持。只按明确归属和配套依赖提交，保护材料外/其他暂存成果；在途写入和突变恢复先结束。不能安全提交时记录具体原因，不能以整包未验收一概拖延。提交后核验实际范围和HEAD，更新当前交接而不改旧证据。普通讨论或本轮规则维护不恢复产品施工、不触发接班。\r\n\r\n## 项目 Skill 与知识入口\r\n\r\n- 涉及本项目开发、历史经验检索、跨端排障或重构接力时，使用 $bgi-project-development，入口为 [.agents/skills/bgi-project-development/SKILL.md](.agents/skills/bgi-project-development/SKILL.md)。Skill 已在本轮加载且未变更时不重复读取。\r\n- 若技能列表尚未发现它，直接读取上述文件即可；不能仅凭文件存在宣称整个 Skill 已被本轮自动加载。\r\n- Skill 按任务路由到领域导航、跨端排障和记忆维护参考文件。已有 .agents/knowledge、.agents/memory、specs 继续作为资料来源，不全量加载、不复制整本历史。\r\n- 仅在用户明确要求使用/创建/继续 Spec 或调用 $bgi-spec-workflow 时，读取 [.agents/skills/bgi-spec-workflow/SKILL.md](.agents/skills/bgi-spec-workflow/SKILL.md)。该 Skill 仅显式启用；普通对话、一般开发或只查阅历史规格不触发。\r\n- Spec 只作用于用户指定的当前任务，沿用本次授权阶段；任务完成或用户明确退出后恢复普通流程。磁盘存在未完成 Spec 不代表新会话获准自动续做，也不等于切换宿主原生模式。\r\n- 简单文件操作不强制走完整流程。读取旧任务文档不意味着要执行其未完成清单。\r\n- 公版 → 茶包的优选/同步使用 $public-merge-assistant，入口为 [.agents/skills/public-merge-assistant/SKILL.md](.agents/skills/public-merge-assistant/SKILL.md)。\r\n- 茶包 → 公版的功能提取/PR 整理使用 $teabag-pr-upstream-assistant，入口为 [.agents/skills/teabag-pr-upstream-assistant/SKILL.md](.agents/skills/teabag-pr-upstream-assistant/SKILL.md)。\r\n- 茶包指定功能重构/接力使用 $teabag-refactor-assistant，入口为 [.agents/skills/teabag-refactor-assistant/SKILL.md](.agents/skills/teabag-refactor-assistant/SKILL.md)。三者按当前任务选择，未出现在技能列表时可直接读取入口；旧 .agents/skills/*.md 和 .kiro/agents/*.json 仅作历史资料，工具权限不随迁移继承。\r\n\r\n## 协作与项目边界\r\n- **开工提示词须是一个完整、自包含的 Goal**：先建立本批 Goal（结果、约束和完成判据），再开工；新会话须先用当前可用的 Goal 查询工具读回本线程 active Goal，核对目标覆盖本批完整任务。若未建立，执行者自行用 Goal 工具建立并读回；工具不可用时如实报告阻断，不得把消息里的 `/goal` 字样当作已建立，也不得先改代码。一次只交付一个后续任务。\r\n- **（2026-10-04 修订）接力提示词完整一次发送**：默认由执行者自动创建同项目聊天并把完整提示词放在create_thread的同一初始消息；只有确认未创建聊天的人工回退才给一个代码块，首行必须是 `/goal <本批完整目标摘要>`（目标文字与 `/goal` 同一行，不能让 `/goal` 独占一行），包含本任务从审计、实施/修复、验证到收口的完整要求、范围与权威材料引用。可以在同一个 Goal 块内分行组织详细要求，不把必需指令放到第二条正文。不得要求先单独发送 Goal 再发正文，也不得要求趁 Goal 活动时抢发补充。旧的分两次发送约定由本条替代；同一目标继续沿用当前 Goal，独立新目标须建立自己的完整 Goal。\r\n- 使用简体中文。在已有授权范围内主动完成，避免重复确认；必要的范围或产品决策不明时才澄清。\r\n- 当前用户要求决定目标；当前源码、配置与实际验证决定技术事实。旧规则与本次筛选冲突时以本入口及 Skill 的筛选结论为准，仍服从当前用户要求和运行环境约束。\r\n- 开始任务先核对分支、工作区差异和相关入口。「公版」默认 origin-lcb/main；「我的版本」包含未提交改动；茶包分支每次动态确认，不按编号大小选主线。\r\n- BGI 主程序、MultiplayerHoeingAssistant 助手与 BgiCoordinatorServer 服务端是独立项目。战斗和传送有双实现；实际路由、共享单机/联机调用方必须核实，不能凭同名文件或旧记忆决定改哪份。\r\n- 公版同步要检查本地增量和依赖。茶包重构按功能组织，尽量减少公版侵入；必要改写明确说明范围。继续旧重构先检查最新接力记录与当前代码。\r\n\r\n## 数据和验证底线\r\n\r\n- 保护 BetterGenshinImpact/bin/x64/Debug/net8.0-windows10.0.22621.0/User，以及其他运行目录的 User、配置、宏、脚本和截图；缓存清理不能递归波及 bin、运行数据或项目根。\r\n- 第三方 JS 脚本源码属于只读输入，一字不能改；需要适配状态、兼容或监控时放在 BGI 脚本宿主、助手或服务端层，通过项目生命周期与宿主 API 调用观察实现，不能向 `main.js` 注入代码。\r\n- .kiro/ 和用户级 KIRO 原档默认只读，修改需用户明确要求。保留其他 IDE/Agent 与用户的未提交工作，不做无差别 git add -A、整文件恢复或覆盖式同步。提交按本次范围选择文件，新增文件不被一概排除。\r\n- 编辑前识别实际编码、BOM 和换行，保持既有格式；新文本用 UTF-8。重要记忆修改保留可恢复版本，写后读回确认；超时后先查是否生效，不盲目重试或用 git restore 覆盖已有改动。\r\n- 多次修改无效果时先确认运行产物和实际入口。Git 显示大面积删除且读取被拒绝时，先核实权限与文件存在性，不据此恢复或提交删除。\r\n- 区分已发送、已入队、已执行和任务终态；未知状态不能当作空闲或成功。跨端推进复用当前注册表/协调器，协议和配置修改检查端到端兼容。\r\n- 构建前检查部署目标。源码验证可使用当前已存在的 DeployToBgiTools=false 条件跳过部署，使用前复核；不为解除文件锁擅自杀用户程序或改构建规则。\r\n- 构建结论看退出码与完整错误，不能仅看 error CS；构建、测试、UI/运行证据分别报告。测试失败对比相同条件基线，禁止为变绿自动移走或排除测试，旧失败名单不构成永久豁免。\r\n- 文档/技能改动验证内容、引用与格式即可，无需构建产品。对行为修改执行与影响相称的验证，不替用户宣布未经观测的运行效果。\r\n\r\n## 记忆维护与可用范围\r\n\r\n- 非平凡任务收尾主动判断是否有项目特有增量；有则按 Skill 的记忆维护流程记录证据、范围和局限。没有新经验不制造文件，不把猜测固化为规则。\r\n- 稳定协作约定留在本文件，流程放 Skill，任务证据留在对应知识/spec/专项记录。优先更新已有同主题内容，重构后同步修正受影响引用。\r\n- 不把分支号、HEAD、临时 PID、工作区差异、测试计数等瞬时状态写成长期事实；用户纠正和新证据可以替代旧结论，保留可追溯依据。\r\n- 当前 .gitignore 忽略 AGENTS.md 和 .agents/。这里的入口、Skill 与知识是本工作区的持久文件；换新克隆、独立 worktree 或机器后先确认文件已经同步，不能承诺完整聊天或全局永久记忆。\r\n\r\n## 长任务工序纪律（槲寄生 R5/R6 等 WBS 施工适用）\r\n\r\n- 正式条款见 [R5 设计稿 §17.4-A 返工抑制六条](Docs/design/onedragon-r5-2-entry-arbitration-wiring-2026-09-20.md)；\r\n  续做任务的入口与速查见 [R5 交接稿「会诊与执行纪律」](Docs/design/onedragon-r5-handoff-2026-09-21.md)。要点：\r\n  ① 措辞类必改须由 `ClaimSurfaceGuardTests` 证明**声明面逐行未变**才可跳过复会诊，声明面一变即等同语义必改项；\r\n  ② 「生产构造开门」类实现**反例先行**（先红夹具、后实现、只开一轮验证会诊）；\r\n  ③ 发现分级：建议级可书面拒绝并登记理由，影响正确性的必须升级为「重要」；\r\n  ④ owner 待决一次批量交付，未裁决期间不在未定语义上堆实现；\r\n  ⑤ 冻结后新发现先登记残项，由 owner 三选一，不自动扩批次；\r\n  ⑥ 安全敏感面冻结须交枚举（白名单／状态全表／交错矩阵全格），仅写不变量不构成可冻结设计。\r\n- **会诊处置硬规则（2026-09-24 立，因批次 15 把重要项降格为建议级拒绝的事故而增）**：完整条款见\r\n  [.agents/knowledge/domains/review-disposition-discipline.md](.agents/knowledge/domains/review-disposition-discipline.md)，**每批开会诊前必读**。要点：\r\n  ⓐ 会诊给出的**重要／必改不得由施工方降级**，只能升级；涉及并发、异常路径、不可撤销状态、身份一致性、跨代际语义者一律先按「重要」处理；\r\n  ⓑ **有未闭合的必改／重要项必须闭环**，通常须复会诊直至无未闭合项；若触及 ⓖ 累计上限则停止新增会诊、保留阻断并走 owner 检查点／有限追加授权，绝不可因此收口或降级。第 ② 条的「只开一轮验证会诊」仅指验证轮，不是预算规则。\r\n  ⓒ 禁止无尝试记录的**全称否定**（\"无…界限\"\"不可能…\"\"不存在…失败点\"）；必须附反例尝试记录，否则改记为「未验证」；\r\n  ⓓ **「部分采纳」必须写明生效层次**：新参数/开关在\"原问题发生的那一层（同一实例生命周期／同一代际／同一进程）\"是否真的生效；只在更外层生效就要如实写\"原层未解决\"；**不得用自己新写的代码否认会诊质疑**；\r\n  ⓔ 新增夹具的**关键断言须做反向突变验证**（改坏实现看是否变红）并在文档标注哪些已验证；\r\n  ⓕ 会诊送审材料固定包含 `git status --porcelain` 与相关未暂存 diff，报告中须区分\"本批文件\"与\"材料外变更\"；\r\n  ⓖ **会诊刹车（2026-09-27 澄清；批次 21 起）**：每个 owner 明确划定的子批累计最多 8 次会诊请求，涵盖所有模型／渠道的首审、复审、验证与收口；请求已发出但失败或超时也计次，本地预检拦截且未发出的不计。修复和回归本身不计次。\r\n  计数写入该子批台账，跨新发现、新证据、代码变化和审查范围细化持续累计；发现新问题、进入新审查周期、换标题或换编号均不重置。不得把同一目标人为拆批来绕过上限。\r\n  用完 8 次时，若阻断／必改／重要正确性项均已闭合且证据完整，可按其余规则收口；若仍有未闭合项，默认停止新增会诊，形成 owner 检查点（未决项、等级、证据、风险、已尝试处理、建议的有限范围和验收条件）。未决项不得降级、伪记为已修复或普通残项；未排除的正确性风险继续阻断收口并关闭相关生产门。可继续独立可行的修复与定向回归。\r\n  达到上限后，只有 owner 明确批准了额外会诊的固定次数及具体问题范围，才可继续会诊；新发现也从该固定额度扣除，不重置、不滚动续期。额度用尽仍未闭合时再次提交检查点，后续会诊须 owner 再批准一笔新的有限额度。真正独立的新目标仅在 owner 事先明确其交付物与验收条件、另立子批时单独计数；当前子批中发现的问题仍属当前计数。\r\n  刹车只限制会诊请求次数，不改变 ⓐ-ⓕ 分级与处置标准，也不减回归或允许丢弃发现；它阻止无界的会诊循环，不能把尚未解决的问题判成通过。\r\n  来历：批次 20 单批 49 轮不收敛、owner 两次人工止损的机制化。\r\n  缺其中任一项的批次，**不得主张已按本规则执行**，也不得在文档写\"处置完毕\"。该规则只做单向收紧，不减会诊点、不降模型强度、不放宽回归。\r\n- **边界**：以上不得用于削减固定会诊点、降低会诊模型、放宽回归/基线，或把阻断/重要发现降级。\r\n- 改声明面（状态词、门禁词、证据等级）后，设 `CLAIM_SURFACE_REGENERATE=1` 重跑声明面守卫以更新清单，并把清单变更纳入提交评审。\r\n\r\n## 守护自动化与心跳（2026-09-26 废除）\r\n\r\n- （2026-09-26 废除）此前试行的 ZCode 定时守护自动化与「守护-槲寄生心跳.md」机制已整体去除，\r\n  定时卡由 owner 在定时任务页面手动删除；任何会话不再维护心跳文件、不写值班状态、不期待守护接手，\r\n  断线续跑回归各会话收工时自行交接。\r\n- （2026-09-26 补注）长目标续跑用 ZCode 原生 `/goal`（目标持久化＋空闲自动续做＋完成校验，每个干活会话设一次）。\r\n  断流软停自动拉起钩子（zcode-relay 的 `stop_reconnect.ps1`）当日试行后**经 owner 决定撤销**——\r\n  上游 relay 截断过频且 goal 校验器调用同样被截断毒害，收益不抵噪音；脚本存档于 hooks 目录。\r\n  无定时轮询、无心跳、无值班复活。\r\n- （2026-09-26 再补注）CODEX 侧等价通道已落地并实证，与 ZCode 侧对齐：\r\n  ① 长目标续跑用 **CODEX 原生 `/goal`**（目标持久化 `~/.codex/goals_1.sqlite` → `thread_goals`；空闲自动续做 `thread_goal_continuation_deferrals`；完成校验）。\r\n  ② UserPromptSubmit 钩子 `~/.codex/hooks/session_pressure.ps1` 在每次用户输入时注入收尾检查：子批/Goal 完成、转入独立目标或出现具体上下文风险时，必须判断「继续当前会话」或「建议新会话」并写理由；交付后续任务时只给一个完整、自包含的 `/goal` 代码块，完整一次发送，不另发正文；按当前自动交接条款创建并核验接班聊天，只有确认未创建的失败回退才让用户复制。\r\n  ③ 停因与交接守卫 `~/.codex/hooks/stop_continue.ps1`（Stop 事件唯一钩子）：保留收尾 200 字符内的明确停因拦截和合法停机白名单；另在「已完成子批＋下一独立目标」或明确上下文风险时，若缺少显式交接判断/理由，或交付后续任务却缺少完整自包含 Goal、要求分两次发送或另发必需正文，则以 `decision:block` 拉起补齐。它只检查文本并提醒执行者按自动交接条款完成原生调用，本身不创建聊天，也不按时间/工具数强制切换；文本通过不证明Goal或接班状态。\r\n  ④ 已被用户否决、永久废除的旧机制：**时间盒强制交接**（按工具数／分钟／提交数强制换会话）。截断识别（ZCode `stop_reconnect.ps1` 等价物）已于当日从 hooks.json 摘除，脚本留档。\r\n  三者关系：`/goal` 负责同一目标的持久化和空闲续做；UserPromptSubmit 提醒在任务边界做接力判断；Stop 守卫防止交接判断缺项后直接收尾。hooks本身**不创建新会话**；执行者按当前用户授权自动创建并核验唯一接班聊天。同样**无定时轮询、无心跳、无值班**。\r\n  实证：真实历史收尾 264 条样本误报 0；回归 27 项 + 死循环保护 3 项全绿；反向突变 5/5 检出；真机 `codex exec` 复现 `Stop Blocked → 续做 → 第二次 Stop 放行`。\r\n  ⚠️ 改动 `~/.codex/hooks.json` 定义后信任失效，必须由用户去 `/hooks` 重新信任，否则钩子静默跳过。\r\n  ⚠️ **`hooks.json` 改动不会热重载**：Codex 在进程启动时加载 hooks 配置并缓存在内存。实证——桌面版进程 13:33 启动后，14:29 定型的 `hooks.json`（Stop 仅 1 钩子）未生效，日志仍持续出现已被摘除的 `reconnect:` 记录；新起的 `codex exec` 进程读磁盘配置则 0 次 reconnect。**改完 `hooks.json` 必须完全退出并重启桌面版 Codex（不是新建会话）**；常驻进程持旧配置也是「会话总是自动停止」的成因之一。\r\n\r\n## 建议与工期的证据门（2026-09-27）\r\n\r\n来源：owner 在本项目进度/提速讨论中纠正了无工时依据的交期，以及未核实在途任务就建议转发指令的问题。适用于本项目的进度、工期、提速、并行及对其他会话的干预建议；不额外增设产品构建/会诊门。\r\n\r\n- **先查再建议**：建议用户向在途会话追加指令、暂停、改范围、并行或换任务前，必须在当前回复内核对目标会话最新状态及相关计划/工作区。读取失败时标记未知，不把旧摘要当现状；不得让用户转发给已完成的任务。\r\n- **干预须有具体收益依据**：先识别有来源的具体瓶颈或错误，再说明追加指令改变什么、依赖什么、保留哪些质量门。一般性的最佳实践不能单独构成“现在请发送”的依据。没有具体瓶颈证据时不建议干预，但也不得推断“干预有害”。\r\n- **证据复用须说明失效条件**：确认相关源码、合同、依赖及运行条件没有改变，才可复用；修复前基线、桩测试、旧版本全量及组件证据不得替代修复后回归、真实进程/入口或集成验证。固定会诊点、模型强度、必改/重要闭环与规定回归不得因提速减少。\r\n- **工期有依据才给数值**：先列实际剩余交付物与依赖，再列可比较批次的实际耗时；拆开实测、推测和返工余量。无可比较工时/吞吐记录时，明确“暂不能可靠估时”，不报确定日期或点估计，不从未经校准的分项继续推出总交期。用户连续 24 小时工作不是效率倍增的证据。\r\n- **结论可追溯**：最终建议简短说明刚核实的事实与来源、推断和局限；给操作建议时同时说明用户实际需要做什么，无操作则明确“不需要额外操作”。不要求用户替模型完成这些检查。\r\n- **改口需解释差异**：指出原判断的哪条依据不足、新证据是什么、原建议保留/修订/撤回；事实未变时不能无理由反转。发现错误主动纠正，不等 owner 多次追问。\r\n- **流程完成核查**：答复前检查“对象仍在做吗、具体瓶颈有证据吗、建议是否越过范围/质量门、数字是否有工时依据”。任一必要项缺失，先补查或明确不能判定，不输出相应操作或确定工期。\r\n\r\n能力边界：这是可审计的常驻行为流程，不是能机械证明建议正确的自动守卫；不承诺零 BUG、零风险或全局永久生效。新克隆/独立 worktree 须确认本文件存在并读取；已运行会话不能假定会自动热加载此新增段落。现有 hooks 的停因/接力检查不能替代事实与语义核查。\r\n\r\n## 槲寄生后续施工设施（2026-09-27 接入）\r\n\r\n- owner 已授权将设施一次性纳入后续施工；后续新批次及自然接力时，先读 [设施接入计划](Docs/design/mistletoe-workflow-facilities.md) 和 [工具说明](tools/mistletoe/README.md)。执行者负责建本批 manifest、证据检查、送审预检及收口前版本复核，不让 owner 逐批安装、填表或触发。\r\n- **每个后续批次默认执行**：先核对现有交付与同条件证据、当前工作区和在途写者，建立 v2 manifest 并在改动前运行 `workflow.py begin`；代码批次先列状态／并发／故障路径矩阵。主执行者评估 1–2 个固定源码版本的只读子 Agent 是否有净收益，不适合时记录原因；已知问题和关键反例集中修复与验证，上轮重要/必改发现成批处置。送审和收口分别执行 `audit/verify` 及原有会诊预检，不跳过回归、突变或生产门。工具不能证明语义穷尽，执行者须人工复核。仅对新批次和自然接力生效，不热改在途 Goal。\r\n- **超大会诊自动分流**：后续新批次和自然接力的固定会诊点默认使用既有 GPT 会诊工具；先固定快照、运行 `audit --stage review`、`verify` 和渠道预检。附件文件数/字节限制只是传输门，不是模型上下文保证；公开模型卡窗口也不是当前 Codex 通道保证。送审前估算附件、目标、包装和另附 Git diff 的完整 token 占用，保留推理/输出余量并核对 diff 完整性。必需材料或 diff 无法完整送入原工具、预估 token 无法安全容纳，或同子批同范围原工具经允许的重试仍无报告且本次预估输入至少占模型上下文三分之一（且错误非明确认证/额度/模型不可用）时，执行者自行改用独立本地 GPT/Codex CLI `-s read-only` 对该次实质会诊按固定快照分步读取，无需 owner 再提醒。三分之一是基于 BO-6/7 样本的暂定通道阈值，须随实测校准，不推断体积是根因；本地同样受模型上下文限制。回退不减模型/强度、原始证据、规定会诊、跨渠道累计预算、重要/必改闭环、回归及生产门；保存预估/错误、触发依据、快照哈希、只读报告和退出码。细则见[设施接入计划「超大会诊材料的通道选择」](Docs/design/mistletoe-workflow-facilities.md#超大会诊材料的通道选择)。这是后续执行会话的条件式操作规则，不是后台钩子；在途 Goal 不假定热加载。\r\n- 开工提示词和交接稿的唯一完整 `/goal` 块必须携带此接入入口及执行要求；不另发安装任务，不改当前活动 Goal，不向在途会话自动发消息。\r\n- 工具成功不是语义通过；会诊点、模型强度、重要/必改闭环、累计预算、规定回归、反向突变、声明面与实机门均保留。失败由执行者修复或登记并完成同等人工核验，不能为了预检通过裁剪原质量要求。\r\n- 独立 worktree 先由执行者核对设施版本；缺失时按交接中权威工作区和哈希精确读取/同步设施文件，保护当地改动，不要求用户再导入。工具不增加 hooks、心跳、定时器或生产运行行为。\r\n\r\n- **并行成果回收**：槲寄生后续每个新批次/自然接力必须在选择剩余工作前读取 [并行成果索引](Docs/design/mistletoe-parallel-deliveries.md)，定向核对关联任务终态、独立报告和实际提交，再按依赖在安全写入窗口消费。独立完成不等于已合入或验收；后续 Goal/交接携带未消费成果入口，执行者自行获取资料，不让 owner 搬运，不把聊天记忆当登记。当前活动会话不假定已热加载。\r\n\r\n\r\n## 槲寄生并行成果自动接收责任（2026-09-27 owner明确要求）\r\n\r\n- 用户不用记住、提醒或搬运并行成果。后续执行者在开工、自然批次边界及收口读取 Docs/design/mistletoe-parallel-deliveries.md 与同名 .json，并运行 tools/mistletoe/deliveries.py 的只读发现检查。漏登记或漂移由执行者核实补账，不转交给用户。\r\n- 到对应目标集成批，将接收/最小适配/回归/回填提交证据写入完整Goal，由主线唯一写者在安全窗口按既有授权执行，不再索取“是否收取”确认。相关业务语义、资源和生产门不足仍明确阻断，不能自动越过。\r\n- 独立任务收口输出登记信息；主线忙时留在其report，由主线自然边界发现补账。后续Goal/交接必须携带索引/台账、待消费ID和阻断，不能依赖owner聊天记忆。原成果保留到集成验证完成。\r\n- 此流程不允许即时改写在途Goal、自动消息/创建会话或后台merge；新worktree缺入口由执行者从权威原工作区获取核验。工具通过不等于语义验收。\r\n\r\n\r\n## 完整审查工序 v3（2026-09-29，覆盖旧的可选前审分流）\r\n\r\n后续正式槲寄生代码批次必须先读 [完整审查工序](Docs/design/mistletoe-review-process.md)（路径相对仓库根）及工具 README，核验 review-bundle。执行者自行完成：完整可执行方案→独立本地只读模型方案审查→实施/限定修复许可→真实执行来源与规定回归/突变→独立本地综合实现审查→原级发现成批闭环→统一收口。导航不是读码白名单；审查者自主追查相关调用链，给根因、反例、精确修改和测试的统一修复方案。未知与重要项不能伪记通过。\r\n\r\n旧五因素triage的no_extra/reuse不再免除正式代码批次的两道审查；GPT工具保留小范围辅助核对，先记同批额度。新begin必须v3配置；暂停既有批次用adopt，原Goal/opening/累计请求（失败也计）/原级未决项不重置，不倒签已实现代码的前审。已运行会话不假定热加载。开工/接力的唯一完整Goal块携带v3入口、bundle核验、原账本与并行成果索引；用户无需另发导入指令。工具只核对机械条件，不替代语义审查或承诺零BUG；不新增hooks/后台任务；新聊天只按当前自动交接条款创建和核验。\r\n\r\n## 会诊模型逐次智能判断（2026-09-30 owner修订）\r\n\r\n每次会诊由执行者结合当前源码与方案、状态、并发、故障、影响链、改动规模、不确定性及原级未决项智能判断：统一使用 `gpt-6.1-sol`，默认 \n</INSTRUCTIONS>"},{"type":"input_text","text":"<environment_context>\n  <cwd>E:\\Program Files\\better-genshin-impact-LCB</cwd>\n  <shell>powershell</shell>\n  <current_date>2026-10-08</current_date>\n  <timezone>Asia/Shanghai</timezone>\n  <filesystem><workspace_roots><root>E:\\Program Files\\better-genshin-impact-LCB</root><root>E:\\CodexData\\home\\visualizations\\2026\\10\\07\\01a1176e-6732-7bd2-9b74-38989fbe5fbe</root></workspace_roots><permission_profile type=\"disabled\"><file_system type=\"unrestricted\" /></permission_profile></filesystem>\n</environment_context>"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a117b6-4012-7383-9a7b-a9e632df39b2","create_time":1791399187.599599,"content_item_kinds":["agents_md.instructions","environments.environment_context"]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T18:53:07.601Z","ordinal":6,"type":"world_state","payload":{"full":true,"state":{"agents_md":{"directory":"E:\\Program Files\\better-genshin-impact-LCB","text":"﻿# 全局协作约定（适用于所有项目）\r\n\r\n## 0. 自动交接与Goal生命周期闭环（2026-10-04用户明确授权）\r\n\r\n政策 ID：`handoff-auto-create-20261004-v1`。用户在侧聊 `01a102e9-6086-7440-b082-c32ecf10b44f` 明确要求：“那你就把现在的流程改成这样吧，自动创建新会话，是否可以。”这是对必要施工交接自动创建接续聊天并一次发送完整提示词的常驻授权，不再逐次请求确认；覆盖本文件、项目入口及旧Skill/提示词中冲突的“不自动创建聊天”“让用户手动粘贴”规则。原2026-10-03必要交接暂停自身Goal的常驻授权继续有效。\r\n\r\n- 只用于本聊天真实执行目标的跨会话交接；普通答复、侧聊审阅、流程维护或他人任务不触发施工接力，不据此暂停主聊天或其他聊天Goal。本轮规则维护不触发主任务换会话。\r\n- 仍按任务语义决定是否交接：可验证批次边界、切换独立目标或有可定位的上下文判断风险。仅时间长、工具多、普通一次编译错误不足以强制切换；跨文件一致性尚需连续推理且能安全推进时继续当前会话。仅是可选优化、尚未决定交接时保持Goal原状态并继续安全工作。\r\n- 决定交接后先完成并核对当前安全操作，保存目标、已完成/未完成、分支/HEAD/工作区、验证/失败、原级未决责任、在途任务终态或责任及唯一下一项。保护未提交成果，不制造干净工作区；源码/测试写入或突变恢复未结束时不得启动接班写者。\r\n- 查询自身Goal；未完成Goal调用原生暂停并再次查询确认同一Goal为paused，已paused保持原状。无Goal不为交接临时创建；真正已完成Goal保持complete。暂停不可用、失败或未知时不创建接班施工聊天，保存现场并只提出必要的用户暂停操作；不改Goal数据库、不伪造标记、不把未完成目标标complete。\r\n- 准备一个完整、自包含的接续提示词，首行为 `/goal <完整目标摘要>`，包含结果、约束、完成判据及从审计到实施/修复、验证和收口的全部要求、权威材料、原历史/opening/计数与受保护边界。全部要求放在同一初始消息，不再让用户复制，不拆成Goal与正文两次发送，不提前创建多个阶段。记录唯一交接标记和来源聊天，便于核对而非重开原批次账。\r\n- 原Goal暂停确认、旧执行者已停止写入后，先用 `list_projects` 核对当前项目/路径/host，调用 `create_thread` 自动创建恰好一个接续聊天并一次发送完整提示词。仓库任务默认使用同项目local，沿用原工作区，不新克隆、不换worktree；当前目录无法准确对应可用项目时保持阻断并提供人工回退，不误选项目。默认不指定模型；仅按用户已明确的模型要求显式设置，不擅自换模型或降低审查强度。\r\n- **自动接班继承模型（2026-10-04用户明确要求）**：政策ID `handoff-inherit-model-20261004-v1`。真实施工交接必须继承来源聊天当时实际使用的模型及推理档位，不固定为K3/GPT或某个强度，也不依赖全局默认、桌面缓存或owner手动选择。交接前只读核对来源聊天当前rollout中最近有效 `turn_context` 的 `model` 与 `effort`/`reasoning_effort`（以及 `collaboration_mode.settings.model` / `reasoning_effort`，如存在须一致），记录来源threadId和证据；调用 `create_thread` 时显式传入该实际 `model` 与对应 `thinking`。完整初始提示词写明继承值及本政策，后续接班按各自来源聊天的当前实际值继续继承，用户后来主动换模型/档位时以换后值为准。创建后只读核验新聊天当前rollout中实际模型及档位与来源一致，不能只凭提示词、自述、入参或标签认定生效；未知、字段冲突、模型/档位不支持或不一致时不得启动接班写入，保留已创建身份、报告具体阻断，不重复创建、不静默换模型或降档。仅当前用户明确指定接班改用别的模型/档位时覆盖继承值，默认配置修改本身不视为强制切换在途聊天的指令。本条覆盖上文默认不指定模型及旧固定K3 MAX要求；不改变独立会诊/审查的既有模型和强度，不切换旧聊天、不触发额外交接、不重启应用。\r\n- 创建返回即记录threadId/hostId；用 `wait_threads` 等待并核对新聊天已接收交接标记、实际cwd及自身完整Goal。新执行者先查询自身Goal，不存在时只建立一次并读回active；存在时核对完整范围。通过create_thread发送的 `/goal` 文字实测不会自动建Goal，不能据此宣称Goal已存在。新聊天在正确项目/Goal读回成立前不得改代码；不恢复旧Goal、不重置原包历史或审查义务。\r\n- 创建结果未知/超时先核对已创建聊天及其终态，禁止盲目重试或重复开接班写者。已创建但首轮失败/新Goal未确认时保留该聊天身份和旧paused状态，报告唯一必要操作；不自动再建一个、不把失败改成成功。仅在创建工具不可用或失败且已确认未创建接班聊天时，回退为一个完整 `/goal` 代码块供用户整块一次发送。旧Goal暂停未确认时不提供可立即施工的接班提示词。\r\n- 自动接班确认后最终给新聊天入口和 `::created-thread{threadId=\"实际返回ID\"}`，简述交接理由及Goal真实状态，无需再粘贴施工正文；对文本守卫使用“旧Goal状态：paused”（或真正complete/none）及“新Goal状态：active”。这些状态必须来自原生查询，不是自述证明。明确原总目标若未完成仍未完成，旧聊天停工；新Goal接续施工不意味着产品交付。\r\n- 已暂停旧聊天的缓存自动续做不恢复施工；只有用户明确选择继续原聊天，且先核对自动创建的接班聊天已停止写入/无在途写者，才可撤销停工，避免两边同时施工。侧聊不代操作其他Goal或自动干预在途聊天。\r\n- 本流程由执行者调用原生能力；hooks只提醒/检查文本，不创建聊天、不读取或修改Goal数据库、不新增hooks、心跳、定时器、时间盒或后台服务，不调低上下文安全网。已运行聊天须显式读回新规则，跨新工作区/机器确认入口存在，不承诺机械保证或永久热加载。\r\n\r\n## 1. 长任务：先明确\"什么时候才可以停\"\r\n\r\n允许结束本轮并等待用户输入的情况只有四种：\r\n\r\n1. 需要用户做产品/业务决策，且无法从现有文档、代码或既有约定中自行判定；\r\n2. 遇到外部阻塞（权限、网络、账号、依赖不可用），且已尝试合理的替代路径；\r\n3. 用户给定的\"完成判定\"已全部满足。\r\n4. 长任务经下述任务语义评估决定交接，已完成当前安全操作并交付可复核的交接材料。用户已授权这种计划性交接；交接不等于目标完成。\r\n\r\n以下都不是停下来的理由，禁止因此收尾等用户：\r\n\r\n- 等用户确认你已经能自己判定的事；\r\n- 等会诊/评审/复核返回（应当批量安排或在本轮内等待，不要把它变成检查点）；\r\n- 等\"更干净的方案\"；\r\n- 每轮例行汇报、\"我先给你看一下\"、\"下一步我会去做…\"。\r\n\r\n\"我下一轮继续…\"这类收尾按违规处理：要么本轮继续做完，要么落到上面四种允许停的情况之一，并写清是哪一种。\r\n\r\n## 2. 用户说\"不要停 / 一次性做完 / 直到完成\"时\r\n\r\n- 主动提醒并建议使用目标模式（在输入框输入 `/goal <完整目标摘要>`，目标文字与命令同一行），并把目标写成「结果 + 约束 + 怎么算完成」三要素；\r\n- 用户已开启目标模式或已配置定时任务时，不要再索取\"继续\"确认；按第 3 节提供有证据的进度，不用重复空泛汇报；\r\n- 一轮内尽量把可以自行判定的动作链连续做完，再统一汇报。\r\n\r\n## 3. 大型开发的任务批次、进度与跨会话交接\r\n\r\n- 开始前把总目标拆成可独立验证的小批次。一个批次只解决一个具体状态转换、入口或故障；写明完成判据、针对性证据、受影响回归和生产门。不要给整个跨端项目设一个需要十几个小时连续运行的单会话批次。\r\n- 开工时记录时间；每完成一笔提交，或连续工作约 45 分钟，向用户报一次有信息量的进度：已完成与提交号、当前验证、下一项、阻断。不要用“还在审查”代替进度。\r\n- 以任务语义判断是否交接：完成聚焦批次、切换到独立目标、或上下文质量有可定位风险时，比较继续与切分的成本。允许需要连续推理、跨文件强一致性的任务在一个会话内完成。90 分钟仅作为本约定明确保留的决策提醒，不是质量阈值或硬上限；有效的继续决策不因时间、工具数或提交数增长而失效。正在进行测试、写入或安全关键转换时先完成并核对，不能为赶时间截断、放宽质量门或擅自开生产门。\r\n- 交接前核实分支、HEAD、已跟踪／未跟踪工作区、提交范围、针对性与完整回归及失败身份、会诊模型／强度／次数和未取得结论的错误；把“已实现、仅设计、未验证、阻断”分开。仓库任务写一份短交接文件，链接权威设计而不复制整本历史；按第0节自动创建同项目接续聊天并发送完整提示词，只有确认无接班聊天的失败回退才给可粘贴提示词。未提交工作如实列出，不能为制造干净工作区而覆盖或删除。\r\n- 必要跨会话续办按第0节自动创建并核验接班聊天；不能自动创建且已确认无接班聊天时，人工回退提示词的唯一代码块首行须为 `/goal <本批完整目标摘要>`，目标文字与命令同一行，其余要求可在同块分行。新会话开工先查询并读回本线程 active Goal，核对它覆盖完整批次；若未建立，执行者自行调用 Goal 工具建立并读回，工具不可用则报告阻断，不得仅凭用户消息里的 `/goal` 字样认定已建立，也不得先改代码。原会话 GOAL 不会自动传到新会话，也不能把中途交接标为总目标完成。不能自动新建会话时，清楚提醒用户粘贴提示词；不要声称定时器能强制中断正在运行的任务。\r\n- 以上适用于所有项目；项目特殊质量门禁继续生效。短小任务无需刻意拆分，用户给出更短时间盒时按用户要求。\r\n\r\n## 4. 改动的安全边界（防误写、防越界）\r\n\r\n- 批量修改文件前后必须自检：改前记录大小/行数或 hash，改后复核；出现大幅缩水立即用 git 还原并重做。\r\n- 改完用 `git diff --stat` 复核改动范围，与预期不符就停下核查。\r\n- 提交只用 `git commit --only -m \"<msg>\" -- <files>`（只提交本次明确改动的文件），禁止 `git add -A` / `git add .`。\r\n- 未经用户明确要求，不执行 `rm -rf`、`git reset --hard`、`git checkout -- <path>`、批量删除等破坏性操作。\r\n- 遇到\"文件被大量删除/丢失\"的现象时，先验证可读性与真实工作区状态（权限、沙箱、路径），再决定是否恢复，不要直接动手。\r\n- 构建或测试通过不等于运行验证通过；结论里如实标出\"未验证\"的部分。\r\n\r\n## 4.1 自动本地提交节点（2026-10-04）\r\n\r\n政策 ID：`auto-local-checkpoint-commit-20261004-v1`。针对已获授权的开发/修复/集成/文档维护，主动保存本地 Git 检查点，不再等待用户逐次提醒提交；只读讨论和他人材料不据此获写入授权。提交进度与审查、验收、生产许可及 Goal 完成分别判断。\r\n\r\n- 聚焦修复批完成影响相称验证、所有突变恢复并核对源码后，提交本批及配套依赖；后审修复完成回归后，再提交对应修复。共享状态/协议可合批，不按文件碎片化；不以“等整个项目验收”拖延阶段提交。\r\n- 正式收口仍按原审查/认证/实机等要求提交最终交付；阶段提交不得替代或伪造这些证据，也不自行关闭原级未决项。\r\n- 必要施工交接前，先核对并提交归属明确的本聊天成果，再记录最新HEAD/工作区、保存交接、暂停Goal并创建接班。未审/未验收写候选状态；保全失败或未验证进度可明确WIP及原级责任，不能写成通过。\r\n- 提交前核对分支/HEAD、暂存/未暂存/新增文件、写者、归属、依赖和证据，用明确文件列表 `git commit --only`；多行说明可用 `--file`。保护其他暂存和材料外工作，不整库提交/清理。提交后读回commit、实际文件集、工作区/暂存区并更新当前交接；原opening/历史/receipt不改绑。\r\n- 在途写入/构建/测试/突变恢复未终态时不提交中间变体；归属或依赖不明、身份漂移或提交失败，记录具体阻断和保存位置，继续其它安全工作。总Goal未完成、未做正式后审、有已知旧失败，本身不是通用不提交理由。\r\n- 默认自动本地提交；push/合并/发布/部署仍需相应授权及质量门。按任务语义触发，不按时间/工具数/回复轮次，不增加hooks、后台程序或强制交接。既有冻结请求回收期间不漂移其身份，待安全终态后提交并建立后续真实快照。\r\n\r\n## 5. 汇报方式\r\n\r\n- 用简体中文，结论先行，用最小必要格式。\r\n- 每轮结尾不要反问\"要不要继续\"，只说明：已完成什么、证据是什么、是否卡住。\r\n- 项目自己的 AGENTS.md 若有汇报格式约定，以项目为准；第 1 节禁止无故等待与第 3 节时间盒交接同时执行。\r\n\r\n## 6. 开发任务的会话交接提醒（轻量；2026-09-24 修订）\r\n\r\n- 当前需求：模型在开发过程中按任务语义判断是否需要换会话。可验证批次完成、要切换独立目标、或出现有证据的上下文质量风险时，比较继续与切分的代价。跨文件一致性或连续推理尚未完成时允许留在同一会话。时间和数量仅作提醒参考，不强制换会话。\r\n- 决定交接时，先结束正在进行的安全操作并核验结果；给用户简短说明：目标、已完成、验证与失败、未完成、工作区状态、下一步。按第0节先确认旧Goal暂停，再自动创建并核验一个接班聊天，无需用户粘贴；创建不可用且确认无接班聊天时才附唯一完整提示词。\r\n- 不要求每个开发/工具任务提交 JSON、文件 hash 或 `finish/continue/handoff/wait` 状态。不为了普通收尾运行脚本。需要准确交接的项目任务仍应把关键证据写在交接文件中，但模型可以按任务规模自行判断格式。\r\n- hooks.json 保留 6 个事件定义。SessionStart、PreCompact/PostCompact 只记轻量日志/压缩信号，PreToolUse 只执行原有危险命令拦截，UserPromptSubmit 注入简短提醒。\r\n- **Stop 事件（2026-09-26 修订）**：唯一挂载 `stop_continue.ps1`，职责为「停因守卫」——当收尾段落出现「稍后继续／等你发话／说了要做却没做」这类宣告时，用 `decision:block` 让模型把本轮可自行判定的部分做完。它**不是**时间盒强制交接：按工具数／分钟／提交数强制换会话的旧守卫已被用户否决，永久废除。规则只匹配**收尾 200 字符内**的明确停因句式，并先过合法停机白名单（需用户决策／外部阻塞／完成判据已满足／已交接），不做全文子串匹配。\r\n- 已废除的旧通道：① ZCode 侧 `stop_reconnect.ps1` 截断拉起（上游掐流过频、噪声大于收益，owner 于 2026-09-26 撤销，现为纯直通存根，见 `~/.tools/zcode-relay/README.md` §4.6）；② CODEX 侧同名截断识别脚本已从 hooks.json 摘除（脚本留档）。等价能力由 Stop 停因守卫 + 原生 `/goal` 空闲续做共同承担。\r\n- **长任务续跑的主力是原生 `/goal`**：目标持久化（`~/.codex/goals_1.sqlite` 的 `thread_goals`）+ 空闲自动续做（`thread_goal_continuation_deferrals`）。目标模式负责「别停」，停因守卫负责「别嘴上说继续」，两者叠加才等价于 ZCode 槲寄生链。\r\n- 回归与实证：`~/.codex/hooks/test/test_stop_continue.py`（27 项）与 `test_stop_limit.py`（死循环保护）；真实历史收尾 264 条样本误报 0；反向突变 5/5 检出；真机 `codex exec` 已复现 `Stop Blocked → 续做 → 第二次 Stop 放行`。\r\n- 改 `hooks.json` 定义后信任失效，**必须提醒用户去 `/hooks` 重新信任**，否则钩子静默跳过。\r\n- **hooks 配置在 Codex 进程启动时加载并缓存在内存，改动 `hooks.json` 后不会热重载。**（2026-09-26 实证）桌面版进程 13:33 启动后，14:29 定型的 `hooks.json`（Stop 仅 1 钩子）**未生效**，日志里仍持续出现已被摘除的 `reconnect:` 记录；而新起的 `codex exec` 进程读磁盘配置则 0 次 reconnect。**结论：改完 `hooks.json` 必须完全退出并重启桌面版 Codex（不是新建会话），否则磁盘与运行时不一致。**这也正是「会话总是自动停止」的成因之一——常驻进程里跑的仍是改动前的旧钩子组合。\r\n- 保持 Codex 默认上下文安全网：不得调低 `model_auto_compact_token_limit`，不得为了交接主动 `/compact`。Hooks 不能中断工具，也不能自行创建新会话。仅改脚本不用重新信任；若改 hooks.json 定义，需在 `/hooks` 审查并信任。\r\n- 方法依据和旧实现历史见 [需求汇总](handoff-mechanism-requirements-2026-09-24.md) 与 [修复记录](handoff-audit-20260924/ADVISORY-REPAIR.md)；旧报告描述的强制 JSON 流程已停用。\r\n- **普通答复与正文保留（2026-09-27修复）**：交接守卫只针对本会话真实施工边界、已选定后续任务或实际交付的施工提示词；讨论他人任务、提示词归属和仅提供裁决回复不因出现“下一批”就触发。用户只要裁决回复时，不代写下一批施工提示词。Stop拉起补齐后，最终回复必须完整重现用户所需正文、结论和必要操作，再补交接判断；不得只给补充说明或要求用户回看上一条。真实施工交接及停因守卫仍生效；按第0节自动创建接续聊天，不按时间/工具数强制切换。证据见 `hooks/test/evidence-reply-visibility-20260927/`；仅修改脚本，hooks.json未改，无需重新信任或重启。\n\n--- project-doc ---\n\n﻿# BGI 项目长期协作入口\r\n\r\n用户要求将 KIRO/KIMI 历史经验筛选为可持续使用的项目记忆。本文件保存常驻约定；按需流程及筛选依据由项目 Skill 承载。首次整理于 2026-09-16，技术事实仍需结合当前代码复核。\r\n\r\n## 施工存储止损（2026-10-05用户授权）\r\n\r\n采用 `mistletoe-storage-limits-20261005-v1`，复工先读 [存储限制](Docs/design/mistletoe-storage-limits.md)，核对工具bundle，并明确记录采用。新快照/取证/审查/audit必须经已接入预算入口，不用手工复制整树、换输出目录/渠道/工作树绕过额度；已知输入超限须在复制前拒绝。默认单次4 GiB、累计新材料16 GiB、余量8 GiB，配置见说明；这是受控工具限制，子进程监测及任意外部写入不能声称系统硬配额。历史报告/收据/唯一成果/User保持，禁止以清理为由丢证据；只清精确登记、未发布的自有scratch。Serena未纳管缓存明确停用，普通文件/rg审查保留。规则不自动恢复产品Goal，不改变原审查和实际交付门。\r\n\r\n## 本版交付法则（2026-10-05，优先于冲突旧流程）\r\n\r\n执行[本版交付法则](_workflow/usable-delivery-20261003/DELIVERY-FIRST-POLICY.md#2026-10-05-本版交付法则优先适用)，政策 ID `mistletoe-release-first-20261005-v2`。用户要求严格按完整可运行版本交付，禁止无关施工扩张。本节及政策正文优先于本文件下文、旧 Skill、旧 Goal 提示词中“先闭合全部历史/认证整个依赖生态”等冲突解释；不修改原报告、原等级、原预算，不伪成功、不削减原约定功能。\r\n\r\n- **现在做**：缺失或不可用的约定功能、正常旧数据合同、本版实际可达的误执行/数据覆盖/停止失效风险、影响相称验证、独立综合复核和新产物全功能实际运行/停止/重启/数据保留验收，交付版本与启动步骤。\r\n- **交付后做**：不妨碍完整使用的普通 BUG、维护性重构、无本版现实影响的历史/工具问题、无具体可达依据的极端组合穷举、新增未约定功能和通用证明/认证设施。保留原级 open 与延期依据，延期不是 closed。\r\n- **新增任务须准入**：在现有计划用一行绑定本版功能、具体缺口、入口/证据、用户后果、最小修复验证及下一交付项；只为完善机制/历史/工具且无本版收益者不得开工。重要等级不自动等于全局施工阻断；未知针对性查证、局部阻断，不无限扩为全源证明。\r\n- **固定收口方向**：在途突变先安全恢复；集中补功能和实际入口，稳定版本做回归/综合复核/实际验收，再交付。未决语义只阻断关联部分；禁止按小函数另开整包前审、不重开包/Goal/预算，不拿测试数量代替产品进展。\r\n- **诚实与采用证据**：源码候选、测试、新产物实机、版本交付分开；运行中执行者必须在下一安全选择边界读回政策 ID 并记录本版必做/延期/唯一下一项。文件修改不等于主聊天已采用；不保证永久热加载或零偏离。本轮规则维护不操作主 Goal、不发消息、不改产品源码、hooks 或工具 bundle。\r\n\r\n## 当前owner流程修订（2026-10-03，交付优先）\r\n\r\n- owner已要求纠正无休止前审，以快速完整交付为第一要务。执行[交付优先流程修订](_workflow/usable-delivery-20261003/DELIVERY-FIRST-POLICY.md)，政策ID `mistletoe-delivery-first-20261003-v1`；本节覆盖下文及旧Skill中冲突的“必须全包方案pass才能开始修复”和“所有历史重要项都必须先闭合”解释。\r\n- 已知行为、入口、写集、保护边界和反例明确后，owner授权定向修复：可以保留blocked及原级open义务进入红反例、代码、Rebuild和受控回归。前审最多首审加一次限定复核；技术修复不滚动进行第三轮纯方案审核。修复许可不开放生产或实际验收。\r\n- 缺失约定功能、误执行、数据风险、错误释放和未知假成功仍阻断交付；不妨碍完整功能使用的普通BUG按原级登记延期。完整功能、实际运行/停止/重启/数据保留、独立综合后审和必要因果验证保持。\r\n- 工具/无关历史不能阻断可独立安全推进的产品源码修复；使用既有渠道或等价可复核来源，不扩建工具，不自造pass/receipt，不删发现、不重置请求、不重建Goal。运行中执行者须显式读回新政策；旧冻结身份原样保留。\r\n\r\n- **自动交接闭环（2026-10-04用户常驻授权）**：采用全局AGENTS第0节 `handoff-auto-create-20261004-v1`，覆盖本入口、旧Skill及旧Goal提示词中冲突的“不自动创建聊天/用户手动粘贴”限制。真实施工交接先完成安全操作、保存现场、原生暂停自身未完成Goal并读回paused，再自动创建恰好一个同项目local接班聊天并一次发送完整提示词；新聊天先建立/核对自身完整Goal并读回active后才能写代码。创建失败/未知先核对已有聊天，不重复开写者；仅工具不可用或确认未创建时人工回退。普通侧聊不操作主Goal、不触发本次主施工交接，不按时间/工具数强制切换。详见[交付优先政策的交接条款](_workflow/usable-delivery-20261003/DELIVERY-FIRST-POLICY.md#会话交接与goal自动暂停)。后续不让owner重复授权或搬提示词。\r\n- **自动接班继承模型（2026-10-04用户明确要求）**：政策ID `handoff-inherit-model-20261004-v1`。真实施工交接必须继承来源聊天当时实际使用的模型及推理档位，不固定为K3/GPT或某个强度，也不依赖全局默认、桌面缓存或owner手动选择。交接前只读核对来源聊天当前rollout中最近有效 `turn_context` 的 `model` 与 `effort`/`reasoning_effort`（以及 `collaboration_mode.settings.model` / `reasoning_effort`，如存在须一致），记录来源threadId和证据；调用 `create_thread` 时显式传入该实际 `model` 与对应 `thinking`。完整初始提示词写明继承值及本政策，后续接班按各自来源聊天的当前实际值继续继承，用户后来主动换模型/档位时以换后值为准。创建后只读核验新聊天当前rollout中实际模型及档位与来源一致，不能只凭提示词、自述、入参或标签认定生效；未知、字段冲突、模型/档位不支持或不一致时不得启动接班写入，保留已创建身份、报告具体阻断，不重复创建、不静默换模型或降档。仅当前用户明确指定接班改用别的模型/档位时覆盖继承值，默认配置修改本身不视为强制切换在途聊天的指令。本条覆盖上文默认不指定模型及旧固定K3 MAX要求；不改变独立会诊/审查的既有模型和强度，不切换旧聊天、不触发额外交接、不重启应用。\r\n\r\n## 自动本地提交节点（2026-10-04）\r\n\r\n采用 `auto-local-checkpoint-commit-20261004-v1`，详见 [自动本地提交节点](Docs/design/automatic-local-commit-policy-20261004.md)及全局AGENTS第4.1节。已授权任务默认在聚焦修复验证后、后审修复回归后、正式收口及必要施工交接前主动本地提交，不等待owner逐次提醒。候选/WIP提交与独立审查、认证、真实验收和最终Goal完成分开；原级义务及发布门保持。只按明确归属和配套依赖提交，保护材料外/其他暂存成果；在途写入和突变恢复先结束。不能安全提交时记录具体原因，不能以整包未验收一概拖延。提交后核验实际范围和HEAD，更新当前交接而不改旧证据。普通讨论或本轮规则维护不恢复产品施工、不触发接班。\r\n\r\n## 项目 Skill 与知识入口\r\n\r\n- 涉及本项目开发、历史经验检索、跨端排障或重构接力时，使用 $bgi-project-development，入口为 [.agents/skills/bgi-project-development/SKILL.md](.agents/skills/bgi-project-development/SKILL.md)。Skill 已在本轮加载且未变更时不重复读取。\r\n- 若技能列表尚未发现它，直接读取上述文件即可；不能仅凭文件存在宣称整个 Skill 已被本轮自动加载。\r\n- Skill 按任务路由到领域导航、跨端排障和记忆维护参考文件。已有 .agents/knowledge、.agents/memory、specs 继续作为资料来源，不全量加载、不复制整本历史。\r\n- 仅在用户明确要求使用/创建/继续 Spec 或调用 $bgi-spec-workflow 时，读取 [.agents/skills/bgi-spec-workflow/SKILL.md](.agents/skills/bgi-spec-workflow/SKILL.md)。该 Skill 仅显式启用；普通对话、一般开发或只查阅历史规格不触发。\r\n- Spec 只作用于用户指定的当前任务，沿用本次授权阶段；任务完成或用户明确退出后恢复普通流程。磁盘存在未完成 Spec 不代表新会话获准自动续做，也不等于切换宿主原生模式。\r\n- 简单文件操作不强制走完整流程。读取旧任务文档不意味着要执行其未完成清单。\r\n- 公版 → 茶包的优选/同步使用 $public-merge-assistant，入口为 [.agents/skills/public-merge-assistant/SKILL.md](.agents/skills/public-merge-assistant/SKILL.md)。\r\n- 茶包 → 公版的功能提取/PR 整理使用 $teabag-pr-upstream-assistant，入口为 [.agents/skills/teabag-pr-upstream-assistant/SKILL.md](.agents/skills/teabag-pr-upstream-assistant/SKILL.md)。\r\n- 茶包指定功能重构/接力使用 $teabag-refactor-assistant，入口为 [.agents/skills/teabag-refactor-assistant/SKILL.md](.agents/skills/teabag-refactor-assistant/SKILL.md)。三者按当前任务选择，未出现在技能列表时可直接读取入口；旧 .agents/skills/*.md 和 .kiro/agents/*.json 仅作历史资料，工具权限不随迁移继承。\r\n\r\n## 协作与项目边界\r\n- **开工提示词须是一个完整、自包含的 Goal**：先建立本批 Goal（结果、约束和完成判据），再开工；新会话须先用当前可用的 Goal 查询工具读回本线程 active Goal，核对目标覆盖本批完整任务。若未建立，执行者自行用 Goal 工具建立并读回；工具不可用时如实报告阻断，不得把消息里的 `/goal` 字样当作已建立，也不得先改代码。一次只交付一个后续任务。\r\n- **（2026-10-04 修订）接力提示词完整一次发送**：默认由执行者自动创建同项目聊天并把完整提示词放在create_thread的同一初始消息；只有确认未创建聊天的人工回退才给一个代码块，首行必须是 `/goal <本批完整目标摘要>`（目标文字与 `/goal` 同一行，不能让 `/goal` 独占一行），包含本任务从审计、实施/修复、验证到收口的完整要求、范围与权威材料引用。可以在同一个 Goal 块内分行组织详细要求，不把必需指令放到第二条正文。不得要求先单独发送 Goal 再发正文，也不得要求趁 Goal 活动时抢发补充。旧的分两次发送约定由本条替代；同一目标继续沿用当前 Goal，独立新目标须建立自己的完整 Goal。\r\n- 使用简体中文。在已有授权范围内主动完成，避免重复确认；必要的范围或产品决策不明时才澄清。\r\n- 当前用户要求决定目标；当前源码、配置与实际验证决定技术事实。旧规则与本次筛选冲突时以本入口及 Skill 的筛选结论为准，仍服从当前用户要求和运行环境约束。\r\n- 开始任务先核对分支、工作区差异和相关入口。「公版」默认 origin-lcb/main；「我的版本」包含未提交改动；茶包分支每次动态确认，不按编号大小选主线。\r\n- BGI 主程序、MultiplayerHoeingAssistant 助手与 BgiCoordinatorServer 服务端是独立项目。战斗和传送有双实现；实际路由、共享单机/联机调用方必须核实，不能凭同名文件或旧记忆决定改哪份。\r\n- 公版同步要检查本地增量和依赖。茶包重构按功能组织，尽量减少公版侵入；必要改写明确说明范围。继续旧重构先检查最新接力记录与当前代码。\r\n\r\n## 数据和验证底线\r\n\r\n- 保护 BetterGenshinImpact/bin/x64/Debug/net8.0-windows10.0.22621.0/User，以及其他运行目录的 User、配置、宏、脚本和截图；缓存清理不能递归波及 bin、运行数据或项目根。\r\n- 第三方 JS 脚本源码属于只读输入，一字不能改；需要适配状态、兼容或监控时放在 BGI 脚本宿主、助手或服务端层，通过项目生命周期与宿主 API 调用观察实现，不能向 `main.js` 注入代码。\r\n- .kiro/ 和用户级 KIRO 原档默认只读，修改需用户明确要求。保留其他 IDE/Agent 与用户的未提交工作，不做无差别 git add -A、整文件恢复或覆盖式同步。提交按本次范围选择文件，新增文件不被一概排除。\r\n- 编辑前识别实际编码、BOM 和换行，保持既有格式；新文本用 UTF-8。重要记忆修改保留可恢复版本，写后读回确认；超时后先查是否生效，不盲目重试或用 git restore 覆盖已有改动。\r\n- 多次修改无效果时先确认运行产物和实际入口。Git 显示大面积删除且读取被拒绝时，先核实权限与文件存在性，不据此恢复或提交删除。\r\n- 区分已发送、已入队、已执行和任务终态；未知状态不能当作空闲或成功。跨端推进复用当前注册表/协调器，协议和配置修改检查端到端兼容。\r\n- 构建前检查部署目标。源码验证可使用当前已存在的 DeployToBgiTools=false 条件跳过部署，使用前复核；不为解除文件锁擅自杀用户程序或改构建规则。\r\n- 构建结论看退出码与完整错误，不能仅看 error CS；构建、测试、UI/运行证据分别报告。测试失败对比相同条件基线，禁止为变绿自动移走或排除测试，旧失败名单不构成永久豁免。\r\n- 文档/技能改动验证内容、引用与格式即可，无需构建产品。对行为修改执行与影响相称的验证，不替用户宣布未经观测的运行效果。\r\n\r\n## 记忆维护与可用范围\r\n\r\n- 非平凡任务收尾主动判断是否有项目特有增量；有则按 Skill 的记忆维护流程记录证据、范围和局限。没有新经验不制造文件，不把猜测固化为规则。\r\n- 稳定协作约定留在本文件，流程放 Skill，任务证据留在对应知识/spec/专项记录。优先更新已有同主题内容，重构后同步修正受影响引用。\r\n- 不把分支号、HEAD、临时 PID、工作区差异、测试计数等瞬时状态写成长期事实；用户纠正和新证据可以替代旧结论，保留可追溯依据。\r\n- 当前 .gitignore 忽略 AGENTS.md 和 .agents/。这里的入口、Skill 与知识是本工作区的持久文件；换新克隆、独立 worktree 或机器后先确认文件已经同步，不能承诺完整聊天或全局永久记忆。\r\n\r\n## 长任务工序纪律（槲寄生 R5/R6 等 WBS 施工适用）\r\n\r\n- 正式条款见 [R5 设计稿 §17.4-A 返工抑制六条](Docs/design/onedragon-r5-2-entry-arbitration-wiring-2026-09-20.md)；\r\n  续做任务的入口与速查见 [R5 交接稿「会诊与执行纪律」](Docs/design/onedragon-r5-handoff-2026-09-21.md)。要点：\r\n  ① 措辞类必改须由 `ClaimSurfaceGuardTests` 证明**声明面逐行未变**才可跳过复会诊，声明面一变即等同语义必改项；\r\n  ② 「生产构造开门」类实现**反例先行**（先红夹具、后实现、只开一轮验证会诊）；\r\n  ③ 发现分级：建议级可书面拒绝并登记理由，影响正确性的必须升级为「重要」；\r\n  ④ owner 待决一次批量交付，未裁决期间不在未定语义上堆实现；\r\n  ⑤ 冻结后新发现先登记残项，由 owner 三选一，不自动扩批次；\r\n  ⑥ 安全敏感面冻结须交枚举（白名单／状态全表／交错矩阵全格），仅写不变量不构成可冻结设计。\r\n- **会诊处置硬规则（2026-09-24 立，因批次 15 把重要项降格为建议级拒绝的事故而增）**：完整条款见\r\n  [.agents/knowledge/domains/review-disposition-discipline.md](.agents/knowledge/domains/review-disposition-discipline.md)，**每批开会诊前必读**。要点：\r\n  ⓐ 会诊给出的**重要／必改不得由施工方降级**，只能升级；涉及并发、异常路径、不可撤销状态、身份一致性、跨代际语义者一律先按「重要」处理；\r\n  ⓑ **有未闭合的必改／重要项必须闭环**，通常须复会诊直至无未闭合项；若触及 ⓖ 累计上限则停止新增会诊、保留阻断并走 owner 检查点／有限追加授权，绝不可因此收口或降级。第 ② 条的「只开一轮验证会诊」仅指验证轮，不是预算规则。\r\n  ⓒ 禁止无尝试记录的**全称否定**（\"无…界限\"\"不可能…\"\"不存在…失败点\"）；必须附反例尝试记录，否则改记为「未验证」；\r\n  ⓓ **「部分采纳」必须写明生效层次**：新参数/开关在\"原问题发生的那一层（同一实例生命周期／同一代际／同一进程）\"是否真的生效；只在更外层生效就要如实写\"原层未解决\"；**不得用自己新写的代码否认会诊质疑**；\r\n  ⓔ 新增夹具的**关键断言须做反向突变验证**（改坏实现看是否变红）并在文档标注哪些已验证；\r\n  ⓕ 会诊送审材料固定包含 `git status --porcelain` 与相关未暂存 diff，报告中须区分\"本批文件\"与\"材料外变更\"；\r\n  ⓖ **会诊刹车（2026-09-27 澄清；批次 21 起）**：每个 owner 明确划定的子批累计最多 8 次会诊请求，涵盖所有模型／渠道的首审、复审、验证与收口；请求已发出但失败或超时也计次，本地预检拦截且未发出的不计。修复和回归本身不计次。\r\n  计数写入该子批台账，跨新发现、新证据、代码变化和审查范围细化持续累计；发现新问题、进入新审查周期、换标题或换编号均不重置。不得把同一目标人为拆批来绕过上限。\r\n  用完 8 次时，若阻断／必改／重要正确性项均已闭合且证据完整，可按其余规则收口；若仍有未闭合项，默认停止新增会诊，形成 owner 检查点（未决项、等级、证据、风险、已尝试处理、建议的有限范围和验收条件）。未决项不得降级、伪记为已修复或普通残项；未排除的正确性风险继续阻断收口并关闭相关生产门。可继续独立可行的修复与定向回归。\r\n  达到上限后，只有 owner 明确批准了额外会诊的固定次数及具体问题范围，才可继续会诊；新发现也从该固定额度扣除，不重置、不滚动续期。额度用尽仍未闭合时再次提交检查点，后续会诊须 owner 再批准一笔新的有限额度。真正独立的新目标仅在 owner 事先明确其交付物与验收条件、另立子批时单独计数；当前子批中发现的问题仍属当前计数。\r\n  刹车只限制会诊请求次数，不改变 ⓐ-ⓕ 分级与处置标准，也不减回归或允许丢弃发现；它阻止无界的会诊循环，不能把尚未解决的问题判成通过。\r\n  来历：批次 20 单批 49 轮不收敛、owner 两次人工止损的机制化。\r\n  缺其中任一项的批次，**不得主张已按本规则执行**，也不得在文档写\"处置完毕\"。该规则只做单向收紧，不减会诊点、不降模型强度、不放宽回归。\r\n- **边界**：以上不得用于削减固定会诊点、降低会诊模型、放宽回归/基线，或把阻断/重要发现降级。\r\n- 改声明面（状态词、门禁词、证据等级）后，设 `CLAIM_SURFACE_REGENERATE=1` 重跑声明面守卫以更新清单，并把清单变更纳入提交评审。\r\n\r\n## 守护自动化与心跳（2026-09-26 废除）\r\n\r\n- （2026-09-26 废除）此前试行的 ZCode 定时守护自动化与「守护-槲寄生心跳.md」机制已整体去除，\r\n  定时卡由 owner 在定时任务页面手动删除；任何会话不再维护心跳文件、不写值班状态、不期待守护接手，\r\n  断线续跑回归各会话收工时自行交接。\r\n- （2026-09-26 补注）长目标续跑用 ZCode 原生 `/goal`（目标持久化＋空闲自动续做＋完成校验，每个干活会话设一次）。\r\n  断流软停自动拉起钩子（zcode-relay 的 `stop_reconnect.ps1`）当日试行后**经 owner 决定撤销**——\r\n  上游 relay 截断过频且 goal 校验器调用同样被截断毒害，收益不抵噪音；脚本存档于 hooks 目录。\r\n  无定时轮询、无心跳、无值班复活。\r\n- （2026-09-26 再补注）CODEX 侧等价通道已落地并实证，与 ZCode 侧对齐：\r\n  ① 长目标续跑用 **CODEX 原生 `/goal`**（目标持久化 `~/.codex/goals_1.sqlite` → `thread_goals`；空闲自动续做 `thread_goal_continuation_deferrals`；完成校验）。\r\n  ② UserPromptSubmit 钩子 `~/.codex/hooks/session_pressure.ps1` 在每次用户输入时注入收尾检查：子批/Goal 完成、转入独立目标或出现具体上下文风险时，必须判断「继续当前会话」或「建议新会话」并写理由；交付后续任务时只给一个完整、自包含的 `/goal` 代码块，完整一次发送，不另发正文；按当前自动交接条款创建并核验接班聊天，只有确认未创建的失败回退才让用户复制。\r\n  ③ 停因与交接守卫 `~/.codex/hooks/stop_continue.ps1`（Stop 事件唯一钩子）：保留收尾 200 字符内的明确停因拦截和合法停机白名单；另在「已完成子批＋下一独立目标」或明确上下文风险时，若缺少显式交接判断/理由，或交付后续任务却缺少完整自包含 Goal、要求分两次发送或另发必需正文，则以 `decision:block` 拉起补齐。它只检查文本并提醒执行者按自动交接条款完成原生调用，本身不创建聊天，也不按时间/工具数强制切换；文本通过不证明Goal或接班状态。\r\n  ④ 已被用户否决、永久废除的旧机制：**时间盒强制交接**（按工具数／分钟／提交数强制换会话）。截断识别（ZCode `stop_reconnect.ps1` 等价物）已于当日从 hooks.json 摘除，脚本留档。\r\n  三者关系：`/goal` 负责同一目标的持久化和空闲续做；UserPromptSubmit 提醒在任务边界做接力判断；Stop 守卫防止交接判断缺项后直接收尾。hooks本身**不创建新会话**；执行者按当前用户授权自动创建并核验唯一接班聊天。同样**无定时轮询、无心跳、无值班**。\r\n  实证：真实历史收尾 264 条样本误报 0；回归 27 项 + 死循环保护 3 项全绿；反向突变 5/5 检出；真机 `codex exec` 复现 `Stop Blocked → 续做 → 第二次 Stop 放行`。\r\n  ⚠️ 改动 `~/.codex/hooks.json` 定义后信任失效，必须由用户去 `/hooks` 重新信任，否则钩子静默跳过。\r\n  ⚠️ **`hooks.json` 改动不会热重载**：Codex 在进程启动时加载 hooks 配置并缓存在内存。实证——桌面版进程 13:33 启动后，14:29 定型的 `hooks.json`（Stop 仅 1 钩子）未生效，日志仍持续出现已被摘除的 `reconnect:` 记录；新起的 `codex exec` 进程读磁盘配置则 0 次 reconnect。**改完 `hooks.json` 必须完全退出并重启桌面版 Codex（不是新建会话）**；常驻进程持旧配置也是「会话总是自动停止」的成因之一。\r\n\r\n## 建议与工期的证据门（2026-09-27）\r\n\r\n来源：owner 在本项目进度/提速讨论中纠正了无工时依据的交期，以及未核实在途任务就建议转发指令的问题。适用于本项目的进度、工期、提速、并行及对其他会话的干预建议；不额外增设产品构建/会诊门。\r\n\r\n- **先查再建议**：建议用户向在途会话追加指令、暂停、改范围、并行或换任务前，必须在当前回复内核对目标会话最新状态及相关计划/工作区。读取失败时标记未知，不把旧摘要当现状；不得让用户转发给已完成的任务。\r\n- **干预须有具体收益依据**：先识别有来源的具体瓶颈或错误，再说明追加指令改变什么、依赖什么、保留哪些质量门。一般性的最佳实践不能单独构成“现在请发送”的依据。没有具体瓶颈证据时不建议干预，但也不得推断“干预有害”。\r\n- **证据复用须说明失效条件**：确认相关源码、合同、依赖及运行条件没有改变，才可复用；修复前基线、桩测试、旧版本全量及组件证据不得替代修复后回归、真实进程/入口或集成验证。固定会诊点、模型强度、必改/重要闭环与规定回归不得因提速减少。\r\n- **工期有依据才给数值**：先列实际剩余交付物与依赖，再列可比较批次的实际耗时；拆开实测、推测和返工余量。无可比较工时/吞吐记录时，明确“暂不能可靠估时”，不报确定日期或点估计，不从未经校准的分项继续推出总交期。用户连续 24 小时工作不是效率倍增的证据。\r\n- **结论可追溯**：最终建议简短说明刚核实的事实与来源、推断和局限；给操作建议时同时说明用户实际需要做什么，无操作则明确“不需要额外操作”。不要求用户替模型完成这些检查。\r\n- **改口需解释差异**：指出原判断的哪条依据不足、新证据是什么、原建议保留/修订/撤回；事实未变时不能无理由反转。发现错误主动纠正，不等 owner 多次追问。\r\n- **流程完成核查**：答复前检查“对象仍在做吗、具体瓶颈有证据吗、建议是否越过范围/质量门、数字是否有工时依据”。任一必要项缺失，先补查或明确不能判定，不输出相应操作或确定工期。\r\n\r\n能力边界：这是可审计的常驻行为流程，不是能机械证明建议正确的自动守卫；不承诺零 BUG、零风险或全局永久生效。新克隆/独立 worktree 须确认本文件存在并读取；已运行会话不能假定会自动热加载此新增段落。现有 hooks 的停因/接力检查不能替代事实与语义核查。\r\n\r\n## 槲寄生后续施工设施（2026-09-27 接入）\r\n\r\n- owner 已授权将设施一次性纳入后续施工；后续新批次及自然接力时，先读 [设施接入计划](Docs/design/mistletoe-workflow-facilities.md) 和 [工具说明](tools/mistletoe/README.md)。执行者负责建本批 manifest、证据检查、送审预检及收口前版本复核，不让 owner 逐批安装、填表或触发。\r\n- **每个后续批次默认执行**：先核对现有交付与同条件证据、当前工作区和在途写者，建立 v2 manifest 并在改动前运行 `workflow.py begin`；代码批次先列状态／并发／故障路径矩阵。主执行者评估 1–2 个固定源码版本的只读子 Agent 是否有净收益，不适合时记录原因；已知问题和关键反例集中修复与验证，上轮重要/必改发现成批处置。送审和收口分别执行 `audit/verify` 及原有会诊预检，不跳过回归、突变或生产门。工具不能证明语义穷尽，执行者须人工复核。仅对新批次和自然接力生效，不热改在途 Goal。\r\n- **超大会诊自动分流**：后续新批次和自然接力的固定会诊点默认使用既有 GPT 会诊工具；先固定快照、运行 `audit --stage review`、`verify` 和渠道预检。附件文件数/字节限制只是传输门，不是模型上下文保证；公开模型卡窗口也不是当前 Codex 通道保证。送审前估算附件、目标、包装和另附 Git diff 的完整 token 占用，保留推理/输出余量并核对 diff 完整性。必需材料或 diff 无法完整送入原工具、预估 token 无法安全容纳，或同子批同范围原工具经允许的重试仍无报告且本次预估输入至少占模型上下文三分之一（且错误非明确认证/额度/模型不可用）时，执行者自行改用独立本地 GPT/Codex CLI `-s read-only` 对该次实质会诊按固定快照分步读取，无需 owner 再提醒。三分之一是基于 BO-6/7 样本的暂定通道阈值，须随实测校准，不推断体积是根因；本地同样受模型上下文限制。回退不减模型/强度、原始证据、规定会诊、跨渠道累计预算、重要/必改闭环、回归及生产门；保存预估/错误、触发依据、快照哈希、只读报告和退出码。细则见[设施接入计划「超大会诊材料的通道选择」](Docs/design/mistletoe-workflow-facilities.md#超大会诊材料的通道选择)。这是后续执行会话的条件式操作规则，不是后台钩子；在途 Goal 不假定热加载。\r\n- 开工提示词和交接稿的唯一完整 `/goal` 块必须携带此接入入口及执行要求；不另发安装任务，不改当前活动 Goal，不向在途会话自动发消息。\r\n- 工具成功不是语义通过；会诊点、模型强度、重要/必改闭环、累计预算、规定回归、反向突变、声明面与实机门均保留。失败由执行者修复或登记并完成同等人工核验，不能为了预检通过裁剪原质量要求。\r\n- 独立 worktree 先由执行者核对设施版本；缺失时按交接中权威工作区和哈希精确读取/同步设施文件，保护当地改动，不要求用户再导入。工具不增加 hooks、心跳、定时器或生产运行行为。\r\n\r\n- **并行成果回收**：槲寄生后续每个新批次/自然接力必须在选择剩余工作前读取 [并行成果索引](Docs/design/mistletoe-parallel-deliveries.md)，定向核对关联任务终态、独立报告和实际提交，再按依赖在安全写入窗口消费。独立完成不等于已合入或验收；后续 Goal/交接携带未消费成果入口，执行者自行获取资料，不让 owner 搬运，不把聊天记忆当登记。当前活动会话不假定已热加载。\r\n\r\n\r\n## 槲寄生并行成果自动接收责任（2026-09-27 owner明确要求）\r\n\r\n- 用户不用记住、提醒或搬运并行成果。后续执行者在开工、自然批次边界及收口读取 Docs/design/mistletoe-parallel-deliveries.md 与同名 .json，并运行 tools/mistletoe/deliveries.py 的只读发现检查。漏登记或漂移由执行者核实补账，不转交给用户。\r\n- 到对应目标集成批，将接收/最小适配/回归/回填提交证据写入完整Goal，由主线唯一写者在安全窗口按既有授权执行，不再索取“是否收取”确认。相关业务语义、资源和生产门不足仍明确阻断，不能自动越过。\r\n- 独立任务收口输出登记信息；主线忙时留在其report，由主线自然边界发现补账。后续Goal/交接必须携带索引/台账、待消费ID和阻断，不能依赖owner聊天记忆。原成果保留到集成验证完成。\r\n- 此流程不允许即时改写在途Goal、自动消息/创建会话或后台merge；新worktree缺入口由执行者从权威原工作区获取核验。工具通过不等于语义验收。\r\n\r\n\r\n## 完整审查工序 v3（2026-09-29，覆盖旧的可选前审分流）\r\n\r\n后续正式槲寄生代码批次必须先读 [完整审查工序](Docs/design/mistletoe-review-process.md)（路径相对仓库根）及工具 README，核验 review-bundle。执行者自行完成：完整可执行方案→独立本地只读模型方案审查→实施/限定修复许可→真实执行来源与规定回归/突变→独立本地综合实现审查→原级发现成批闭环→统一收口。导航不是读码白名单；审查者自主追查相关调用链，给根因、反例、精确修改和测试的统一修复方案。未知与重要项不能伪记通过。\r\n\r\n旧五因素triage的no_extra/reuse不再免除正式代码批次的两道审查；GPT工具保留小范围辅助核对，先记同批额度。新begin必须v3配置；暂停既有批次用adopt，原Goal/opening/累计请求（失败也计）/原级未决项不重置，不倒签已实现代码的前审。已运行会话不假定热加载。开工/接力的唯一完整Goal块携带v3入口、bundle核验、原账本与并行成果索引；用户无需另发导入指令。工具只核对机械条件，不替代语义审查或承诺零BUG；不新增hooks/后台任务；新聊天只按当前自动交接条款创建和核验。\r\n\r\n## 会诊模型逐次智能判断（2026-09-30 owner修订）\r\n\r\n每次会诊由执行者结合当前源码与方案、状态、并发、故障、影响链、改动规模、不确定性及原级未决项智能判断：统一使用 `gpt-6.1-sol`，默认 "},"apps_instructions":false,"collaboration_mode":{"mode":"default","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","instructions":"0a11049b0421e1e86f1e129af8d547a89548a0c3"},"context_window_guidance":"","environments":{"environments":{"local":{"cwd":"E:\\Program Files\\better-genshin-impact-LCB","status":"available","shell":"powershell"}},"current_date":"2026-10-08","timezone":"Asia/Shanghai","filesystem":"<filesystem><workspace_roots><root>E:\\Program Files\\better-genshin-impact-LCB</root><root>E:\\CodexData\\home\\visualizations\\2026\\10\\07\\01a1176e-6732-7bd2-9b74-38989fbe5fbe</root></workspace_roots><permission_profile type=\"disabled\"><file_system type=\"unrestricted\" /></permission_profile></filesystem>"},"environments_instructions":false,"git_attribution":false,"host_skills":{"body":"\n## Skills\nA skill is a set of local instructions to follow that is stored in a `SKILL.md` file. Below is the list of skills that can be used. Each entry includes a name, description, and a short path that can be expanded into an absolute path using the skill roots table.\n### Skill roots\n- `r0` = `E:/CodexData/home/skills`\n- `r1` = `C:/Users/Administrator/.agents/skills`\n- `r2` = `E:/CodexData/home/skills/.system`\n- `r3` = `E:/CodexData/home/plugins/cache/openai-bundled`\n- `r4` = `E:/CodexData/home/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/pages/0.1.20/skills`\n- `r5` = `E:/CodexData/home/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote`\n- `r6` = `E:/CodexData/home/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/sites/0.1.75/skills`\n- `r7` = `E:/CodexData/home/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/work-pets/0.1.6/skills`\n- `r8` = `E:/CodexData/home/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime`\n- `r9` = `E:/CodexData/home/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime/spreadsheets/26.905.11957/skills`\n- `r10` = `E:/CodexData/home/plugins/cache/personal`\n- `r11` = `E:/Program Files/better-genshin-impact-LCB/.agents/skills`\n### Available skills\n- imagegen: Generate or edit raster images when the task benefits from AI-created bitmap visuals such as photos, illustrations, textures, sprites, mockups, or transparent-background cutouts. Use when Codex should create a brand-new image, transform an existing image, or derive visual variants from references, and the output should be a bitmap asset rather than repo-native code or vector. Do not use when the task is better handled by editing existing SVG/vector/code-native assets, extending an established icon or logo system, or building the visual directly in HTML/CSS/canvas. (file: r2/imagegen/SKILL.md)\n- openai-docs: Use for Codex models/pricing, scheduled tasks, skills, settings, setup, troubleshooting, customization, automations, and self-knowledge—including 'you,' 'your,' 'this app,' or 'this coding agent' when they refer to Codex—and for OpenAI APIs/products and ChatGPT Work. Also use for model choice/migration, prompting, SDKs, Responses, Realtime, agents, evals, and Chat/Work/Codex comparisons. Do not use for generic app/software tasks that merely mention Codex. (file: r2/openai-docs/SKILL.md)\n- skill-creator: Create or update a Codex skill with appropriately scoped instructions and any needed supporting resources. (file: r2/skill-creator/SKILL.md)\n- skill-installer: Install Codex skills into $CODEX_HOME/skills from a curated list or a GitHub repo path. Use when a user asks to list installable skills, install a curated skill, or install a skill from another repo (including private repos). (file: r2/skill-installer/SKILL.md)\n- bgi-project-development: 为 BetterGI 茶包版开发检索并核实项目经验，定位双引擎和助手/服务端/BGI 跨端问题，并更新有证据的项目记忆。适用于此仓库的开发、排障、重构接力与知识整理；纯文件操作或其他项目不触发。 (file: r11/bgi-project-development/SKILL.md)\n- public-merge-assistant: 将公版 origin-lcb/main 的指定提交或更新合入当前 BetterGI 茶包分支，审计本地增量、双引擎路由及回归风险。用于优选公版、同步上游或解决此方向的冲突；茶包功能向公版提 PR 使用 teabag-pr-upstream-assistant。 (file: r11/public-merge-assistant/SKILL.md)\n- teabag-pr-upstream-assistant: 将 BetterGI 茶包功能抽取到公版基线的独立 worktree，审计代码和资源依赖、整理最小功能差异及 PR 提交。用于茶包向公版贡献功能；上游合入茶包使用 public-merge-assistant。 (file: r11/teabag-pr-upstream-assistant/SKILL.md)\n- teabag-refactor-assistant: 按 BetterGI 茶包功能清单开展或接力指定功能的结构重构，核实双引擎与调用方、保持既有行为、减少公版侵入并记录进度。用于茶包功能隔离及重构接力，不自动启动旧 Spec 或执行整份待办。 (file: r11/teabag-refactor-assistant/SKILL.md)\n- codex: 将编码、代码库探索、实现、评审和验证任务委托给持久化 Codex CLI Agent。仅当用户明确要求“用 Codex”“让 Codex 执行”，或要求继续某个 Codex Agent 任务时使用。 (file: r0/codex/SKILL.md)\n- computer-use:computer-use: Control Windows apps from ChatGPT (file: r3/computer-use/26.1002.51308/skills/computer-use/SKILL.md)\n- documents:documents: Create, edit, redline, and comment on `.docx`, Word, and Google Docs-targeted document artifacts inside the container, with a strict render-and-verify workflow. Use `render_docx.py` to generate page PNGs (and optional PDF) for visual QA, then iterate until layout is flawless before delivering the final document. (file: r8/documents/26.905.11957/skills/documents/SKILL.md)\n- gpt-workspace-executor:gpt-workspace-executor: Use when the user explicitly asks for \"GPT会诊\", \"用GPT分析\", \"用GPT审核\", or invokes $gpt-workspace-executor. GPT provides scoped read-only consultation through MCP while the primary model continues execution. (file: r10/gpt-workspace-executor/0.1.0+codex.20260923130610/skills/gpt-workspace-executor/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes: Mandatory entry point: read this first for any request to make, create, edit, animate, or render a video, animation, or motion graphic, including a promo, explainer, captioned clip, title card, overlay, slideshow or interactive deck, Remotion port, or any HyperFrames HTML composition. Also use it to inspect, diagnose, validate, preview, publish, or batch-render an existing HyperFrames project. Inputs may be a website URL, GitHub PR, Figma design or URL, text or brief, existing footage, or music. It resumes project state, captures intent when applicable, selects and installs the owning workflow, and routes domain capabilities. HyperFrames is the default output framework unless the user explicitly chooses another framework for the deliverable or asks only to record a browser session. (file: r1/hyperframes/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes: Mandatory entry point: read this first for any request to make, create, edit, animate, or render a video, animation, or motion graphic, including a promo, explainer, captioned clip, title card, overlay, slideshow or interactive deck, Remotion port, or any HyperFrames HTML composition. Also use it to inspect, diagnose, validate, preview, publish, or batch-render an existing HyperFrames project. Inputs may be a website URL, GitHub PR, Figma design or URL, text or brief, existing footage, or music. It resumes project state, captures intent when applicable, selects and installs the owning workflow, and routes domain capabilities. HyperFrames is the default output framework unless the user explicitly chooses another framework for the deliverable or asks only to record a browser session. (file: r0/hyperframes/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-animation: All animation knowledge for HyperFrames — atomic motion rules, multi-phase scene blueprints, scene transitions, broader motion-design techniques, AND the seven runtime adapters (GSAP default, plus Lottie, Three.js, Anime.js, CSS keyframes, Web Animations API, TypeGPU). Use for any motion or animation task: pick 2-4 rules and compose, or load a blueprint, or look up runtime-specific API (e.g. GSAP eases / Lottie player / Three.js mixer). Also covers auditing an existing composition's choreography (animation map) and 24 named text-animation effects. HyperFrames-native: single paused timeline, seek-safe, deterministic. (file: r1/hyperframes-animation/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-animation: All animation knowledge for HyperFrames — atomic motion rules, multi-phase scene blueprints, scene transitions, broader motion-design techniques, AND the seven runtime adapters (GSAP default, plus Lottie, Three.js, Anime.js, CSS keyframes, Web Animations API, TypeGPU). Use for any motion or animation task: pick 2-4 rules and compose, or load a blueprint, or look up runtime-specific API (e.g. GSAP eases / Lottie player / Three.js mixer). Also covers auditing an existing composition's choreography (animation map) and 24 named text-animation effects. HyperFrames-native: single paused timeline, seek-safe, deterministic. (file: r0/hyperframes-animation/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-audio: Use when audio already placed in a HyperFrames composition needs to be mixed: fade-in/fade-out, crossfade, track gain or volume, volume automation, ducking, a music bed that fights a voiceover (voiceover carve), effects on a track (EQ, compressor, limiter, gate, saturation, delay, reverb, chorus, phaser, bitcrush), automation envelopes drawn on a track's volume or any effect parameter, or one submix bus carrying a chain, a fader and an automation clock for several tracks at once (`<hf-audio-group>`). Don't use for sourcing or generating audio — finding BGM, SFX, or making a voiceover is `/media-use`. Don't use for clip timing or track layout, which is `/hyperframes-core`. (file: r1/hyperframes-audio/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-audio: Use when audio already placed in a HyperFrames composition needs to be mixed: fade-in/fade-out, crossfade, track gain or volume, volume automation, ducking, a music bed that fights a voiceover (voiceover carve), effects on a track (EQ, compressor, limiter, gate, saturation, delay, reverb, chorus, phaser, bitcrush), automation envelopes drawn on a track's volume or any effect parameter, or one submix bus carrying a chain, a fader and an automation clock for several tracks at once (`<hf-audio-group>`). Don't use for sourcing or generating audio — finding BGM, SFX, or making a voiceover is `/media-use`. Don't use for clip timing or track layout, which is `/hyperframes-core`. (file: r0/hyperframes-audio/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-cli: Use the HyperFrames CLI development loop: init, add, catalog, capture, lint, check, snapshot, compare, grade-compare, preview, play, present, beats, keyframes, single or batch render, publish, cloud, cloudrun, feedback, lambda, doctor, browser, info, upgrade, skills, compositions, timeline, history, clean, docs, benchmark, telemetry, transcribe, auth, tts, and remove-background. Also use when diagnosing build or render failures. validate, inspect, and layout are deprecated aliases; use check. Covers local, HeyGen-hosted cloud, AWS Lambda, and Google Cloud Run rendering. (file: r1/hyperframes-cli/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-cli: Use the HyperFrames CLI development loop: init, add, catalog, capture, lint, check, snapshot, compare, grade-compare, preview, play, present, beats, keyframes, single or batch render, publish, cloud, cloudrun, feedback, lambda, doctor, browser, info, upgrade, skills, compositions, timeline, history, clean, docs, benchmark, telemetry, transcribe, auth, tts, and remove-background. Also use when diagnosing build or render failures. validate, inspect, and layout are deprecated aliases; use check. Covers local, HeyGen-hosted cloud, AWS Lambda, and Google Cloud Run rendering. (file: r0/hyperframes-cli/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-core: The HyperFrames composition contract — build one renderable project. Use for composition structure, the `data-*` timing attributes, `class=\"clip\"`, tracks, sub-compositions, variables, framework-owned media playback, deterministic-render rules, and validation. Read before writing composition HTML. (file: r1/hyperframes-core/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-core: The HyperFrames composition contract — build one renderable project. Use for composition structure, the `data-*` timing attributes, `class=\"clip\"`, tracks, sub-compositions, variables, framework-owned media playback, deterministic-render rules, and validation. Read before writing composition HTML. (file: r0/hyperframes-core/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-creative: Non-animation creative direction for HyperFrames videos. Use for design spec (frame.md / design.md) handling, palettes, typography, narration, beat planning, audio-reactive visuals, composition patterns, and brand / style decisions. For atomic motion patterns and scene blueprints, use `hyperframes-animation`. (file: r1/hyperframes-creative/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-creative: Non-animation creative direction for HyperFrames videos. Use for design spec (frame.md / design.md) handling, palettes, typography, narration, beat planning, audio-reactive visuals, composition patterns, and brand / style decisions. For atomic motion patterns and scene blueprints, use `hyperframes-animation`. (file: r0/hyperframes-creative/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-keyframes: Use when a HyperFrames composition needs a punch-in, punch-out, zoom, reframe, Ken Burns treatment, camera move, visual match/whip handoff, or other seek-safe 2D/3D keyframes; also for GSAP, CSS keyframes, Anime.js, WAAPI, FLIP, paths, masks, SVG morph/draw, text trails, 3D depth, or `hyperframes keyframes` diagnostics. Don't use for broad scene strategy, brand design, media sourcing, captions, or general video planning. (file: r1/hyperframes-keyframes/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-keyframes: Use when a HyperFrames composition needs a punch-in, punch-out, zoom, reframe, Ken Burns treatment, camera move, visual match/whip handoff, or other seek-safe 2D/3D keyframes; also for GSAP, CSS keyframes, Anime.js, WAAPI, FLIP, paths, masks, SVG morph/draw, text trails, 3D depth, or `hyperframes keyframes` diagnostics. Don't use for broad scene strategy, brand design, media sourcing, captions, or general video planning. (file: r0/hyperframes-keyframes/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-registry: Search, install, and wire registry blocks and components into HyperFrames compositions. Use BEFORE hand-building any named visual — whenever a brief, a user, or a storyboard names a look, effect, treatment, or transition such as CRT scanlines, glitch, chromatic aberration, film grain, a shimmer sweep, a chart, a code or terminal window, a map, or a confetti burst — because roughly 400 hosted items already cover many of them and the search ranks all of them with nothing installed, no project, and no account. Also use when running hyperframes add or hyperframes catalog, installing one item or every block matching a tag, wiring an installed item into index.html, or working with hyperframes.json. Covers discovery, install locations, block sub-composition wiring, component snippet merging, and authoring a new block or component to contribute upstream (idea → scaffold → validate → PR). (file: r1/hyperframes-registry/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-registry: Search, install, and wire registry blocks and components into HyperFrames compositions. Use BEFORE hand-building any named visual — whenever a brief, a user, or a storyboard names a look, effect, treatment, or transition such as CRT scanlines, glitch, chromatic aberration, film grain, a shimmer sweep, a chart, a code or terminal window, a map, or a confetti burst — because roughly 400 hosted items already cover many of them and the search ranks all of them with nothing installed, no project, and no account. Also use when running hyperframes add or hyperframes catalog, installing one item or every block matching a tag, wiring an installed item into index.html, or working with hyperframes.json. Covers discovery, install locations, block sub-composition wiring, component snippet merging, and authoring a new block or component to contribute upstream (idea → scaffold → validate → PR). (file: r0/hyperframes-registry/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-studio: Use when working with a person on a HyperFrames project in Studio: first, whether their message asks for a change at all (questions, loose ideas and \"don't change anything\" get an answer and a plan, not an edit); for a new film, the plan, storyboard and build order that the HyperFrames launch films follow; and how the timeline should be laid out so it reads well (one caption track, one element kind per track, every scene a sub-composition) and where captions and key content may sit (safe zones). Don't use for how to perform an individual edit (split, trim, retime, volume, copy, swap): that is `creator-editing-recipes.md` in `/hyperframes-core`. (file: r1/hyperframes-studio/SKILL.md)\n- hyperframes-studio: Use when working with a person on a HyperFrames project in Studio: first, whether their message asks for a change at all (questions, loose ideas and \"don't change anything\" get an answer and a plan, not an edit); for a new film, the plan, storyboard and build order that the HyperFrames launch films follow; and how the timeline should be laid out so it reads well (one caption track, one element kind per track, every scene a sub-composition) and where captions and key content may sit (safe zones). Don't use for how to perform an individual edit (split, trim, retime, volume, copy, swap): that is `creator-editing-recipes.md` in `/hyperframes-core`. (file: r0/hyperframes-studio/SKILL.md)\n- liangshen: 梁神模式——两阶段会话行为协议（复刻自 DSH 的 liangshen preset）：首轮以极简面工作（仅 shell 与文件编辑、不写计划、不派子代理），首轮完成后铺开完整工作流。仅在用户以 $liangshen 显式调用时启用，不要自动套用。 (file: r0/liangshen/SKILL.md)\n- media-use: Agent Media OS, the single skill for every media need in a HyperFrames project. Resolve BGM, SFX, image, icon, brand logo, voice, color grade, or LUT into a frozen local file or paste-ready block + ledger record (one verb, `resolve`); generate via TTS / music / image models when the catalog misses; produce voiceover, transcription, captions, and background removal through one shared audio engine; operate on media (cut / reframe / transform); and reuse assets across projects. Also use for vague feedback that real footage looks dark, flat, boring, should feel retro/camcorder/print/ASCII, needs privacy, or needs a media reveal. (file: r1/media-use/SKILL.md)\n- media-use: Agent Media OS, the single skill for every media need in a HyperFrames project. Resolve BGM, SFX, image, icon, brand logo, voice, color grade, or LUT into a frozen local file or paste-ready block + ledger record (one verb, `resolve`); generate via TTS / music / image models when the catalog misses; produce voiceover, transcription, captions, and background removal through one shared audio engine; operate on media (cut / reframe / transform); and reuse assets across projects. Also use for vague feedback that real footage looks dark, flat, boring, should feel retro/camcorder/print/ASCII, needs privacy, or needs a media reveal. (file: r0/media-use/SKILL.md)\n- mistletoe-independent-review: 为槲寄生批次执行独立方案审查、实现审查和修复复核；审查者可自主只读追查完整项目及入口外依赖，保存原生来源、阶段结果和原级问题。适用于本项目审查设施和产品批次，不自动启动其他旧任务。 (file: r0/mistletoe-independent-review/SKILL.md)\n- pages:maintain-space: Reconcile new evidence into existing ChatGPT Pages or a Space when the user requests upkeep. For a direct text correction, use write-page. Do not use for ordinary chat drafts, writing, or advice, or treat a selected Page as a request to save. Schedule future upkeep only when requested. (file: r4/maintain-space/SKILL.md)\n- pages:manage-schedules: Review a ChatGPT Space page and its schedules, recommend useful recurring work, and create, update, or remove scheduled automations. (file: r4/manage-schedules/SKILL.md)\n- pages:organize-space: Organize existing ChatGPT Pages and Space structure when the user requests changes to that structure. Do not use for ordinary chat drafts or advice; a selected Page alone does not authorize reorganization. A narrow text edit does not need this workflow. (file: r4/organize-space/SKILL.md)\n- pages:write-page: Create or edit requested Page/Space content, or use for prose you have already decided to save as a standalone Markdown file, only if the user did not explicitly request a Markdown file. Honor established formats, destinations, and repository documentation. A selected Page alone does not authorize a write. (file: r4/write-page/SKILL.md)\n- pdf:pdf: Read, create, inspect, render, and verify PDF files where visual layout matters, including fillable AcroForms. Use Poppler rendering plus Python tools such as reportlab, pdfplumber, and pypdf for generation and extraction. (file: r8/pdf/26.905.11957/skills/pdf/SKILL.md)\n- plugin-management:plugin-management: Discover and suggest relevant plugins, inspect app permissions and dependencies, and manage plugin connections or removal. Use when the user asks about plugins or when a task would materially benefit from an external app, account, service, or data source that available tools cannot access. (file: r5/plugin-management/0.1.0/skills/plugin-management/SKILL.md)\n- presentations:Presentations: Read, create or edit PowerPoint or Google Slides decks. Use for presentation, slide deck, PowerPoint, PPT, PPTX, or Google Slides requests. (file: r8/presentations/26.905.11957/skills/presentations/SKILL.md)\n- requesting-code-review: Use when completing tasks, implementing major features, or before merging to verify work meets requirements (file: r0/mistletoe-independent-review/references/upstream/skills/requesting-code-review/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-building: Use Sites when the user wants a complete website built for them, such as a landing page, portfolio, dashboard, portal, tracker, hub, or internal tool, or wants to modify a website built with Sites. Do not use for development work in other web projects unless the user explicitly requests Sites. (file: r6/sites-building/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-hosting: Host websites with Sites. Use after `sites-building` to publish new sites and edits, for requested website publishing or deployment, or for hosting management. A project containing `.openai/hosting.json` uses Sites hosting only when the current request concerns that Site. Publishing an npm package or standalone asset is not website publishing. Honor an explicit request to use another hosting provider. (file: r6/sites-hosting/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-mcp: Build or update a Site-hosted MCP server and help users access its tools through the Site's plugin in ChatGPT or Codex. (file: r6/sites-mcp/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-preview-troubleshooting: Diagnose and recover failed supervised sites-preview sessions after sites-building. Applies only to the managed-linux execution profile, not portable previews. (file: r6/sites-preview-troubleshooting/SKILL.md)\n- spreadsheets:Spreadsheets: Use skill when user requests to create, modify, analyze, visualize, or work with spreadsheet files (`.xlsx`, `.xls`, `.csv`, `.tsv`) or Google Sheets with formulas, formatting, charts, tables, and recalculation. Do not use for live controlling Microsoft Excel app or a live Excel session. (file: r9/spreadsheets/SKILL.md)\n- spreadsheets:excel-live-control: Control an open or active Microsoft Excel workbook through the ChatGPT add-in or connected session. Use when the user tags the Microsoft Excel app in Codex or follows up on an established live Excel task. Do not use for standalone spreadsheet files or Google Sheets. (file: r9/excel-live-control/SKILL.md)\n- template-creator:template-creator: Create or update a reusable personal Codex artifact-template skill. Use when the user invokes $template-creator or asks in natural language to create a reusable template from a reference document, presentation, spreadsheet, Google Docs, Slides, or Sheets link, ImageGen or Product Design image, email, Slack message, or Site project, or explicitly asks to edit or update a passed artifact-template skill. Do not use for one-off creation from an existing template. (file: r8/template-creator/26.905.11957/skills/template-creator/SKILL.md)\n- visualize:visualize: Create visualizations and interactive tools directly in conversation. Proactively use to show how something works; explore 'what happens when', 'what changes', or 'help me understand'; compare or inspect; create simulations, maps, charts, graphs, and mockups. Use standard tools for static scientific figures. (file: r3/visualize/1.0.47/skills/visualize/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:create-pet: Create, repair, validate, preview, upload, or activate an animated v2 pet in ChatGPT Work mode from a character idea, brand cue, or reference image. Use for new ChatGPT Pets, custom mascots, non-pixel styles, and unattached sprite sheets requiring nine animation states plus sixteen look directions. Preserve Library artifacts and Pets MCP lifecycle behavior. Exclude real pets, standalone images, and other-app pets; clarify before invoking. (file: r7/create-pet/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:pets: List, inspect, select, download, or delete animated pets in ChatGPT Work mode. Use for an explicit pet in ChatGPT or established ChatGPT Pets context. Exclude real-world and other-app pets; clarify before invoking. (file: r7/pets/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:update-pet: Inspect, validate, preview, repair, or update a custom pet in ChatGPT Work mode, including its name, description, or sprite sheet. Use for a pet in ChatGPT or established ChatGPT Pets context. Exclude real-world and other-app pets; clarify before invoking. (file: r7/update-pet/SKILL.md)\n","includeInstructions":true},"managed_developer_instructions":{},"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","model_catalog":"ea1a55de2973a50e2e404222c5499c