y selected back edges, node-arrival repetition and existing scheduled-loop behavior; do not introduce lane quotas, daily deduplication or scanning of unselected branches.\",\r\n        \"Apply this together with LOOP-CUTOFF-TIMED-NODE-1 in one bounded Planner/Runner repair.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"tests\": [\r\n        \"Finite planner counterexamples with an earlier secondary-lane node: both $end and implicit primary tail must restart the same primary entry with PathLane=0 and a fresh round identity.\",\r\n        \"A finite Runner fixture must observe only the intended selected resources across two rounds, with distinct submission identities; an unselected secondary resource must receive zero submissions.\",\r\n        \"A scheduled-loop fixture with primary entry at a nonzero array index must retain the intended round wait. Preserve existing explicit-back-edge repetition and stop behavior.\",\r\n        \"Reverse the canonical-entry repair and require failure of the wrong-resource/entry assertions, then restore source and rerun the affected path/schedule tests.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"closure_evidence\": []\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"LOOP-CUTOFF-TIMED-NODE-1\",\r\n      \"severity\": \"important\",\r\n      \"obligation\": \"implementation\",\r\n      \"status\": \"open\",\r\n      \"root_cause\": \"DriveAsync checks LoopDeadlineAt before AwaitNodeScheduleAsync. The node wait neither caps its target at the cutoff nor rechecks the cutoff before returning permission to execute. After that asynchronous wait, DriveAsync proceeds directly to condition/end handling, prerequisites and resource submission. The production boundary and admission path do not add a LoopDeadlineAt guard.\",\r\n      \"counterexample\": \"At 09:00 start a normally authored immediate loop with an absolute deadline of 10:00 and a resource node scheduled for 11:00 in sequence or fixed mode. The pre-wait cutoff check passes. WaitAsync waits until 11:00; AwaitNodeScheduleAsync returns 