index 0 can be a secondary-lane node that was never selected by the path. The Runner also identifies round entry by SequenceIndex==0 rather than the same canonical path entry.\",\r\n      \"counterexample\": \"Use the formal editor to place a secondary-lane resource at 07:00 and the primary-lane entry at 08:00, configure a structural loop, and end the primary path through $end or its implicit lane tail. Global sorting places the secondary resource at array index 0. FirstOccurrence correctly starts the primary entry at index 1. Its next structural round incorrectly selects index 0, potentially waits for and executes the unselected secondary resource, and ceases to repeat the intended primary entry. The code trace is supported directly by the frozen implementation; this reviewer did not execute the counterexample.\",\r\n      \"paths\": [\r\n        \"MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowPlanner.cs:88\",\r\n        \"MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowPlan.Path.cs:97\",\r\n        \"MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowPlan.Path.cs:118\",\r\n        \"MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/ViewModels/WorkflowScheduleViewModel.cs:67\",\r\n        \"MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowRunner.cs:765\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"repair_steps\": [\r\n        \"Use one canonical structural-round entry calculation for first entry and both structural-loop restarts. Preserve its stable node identity and primary PathLane, and increment the durable round identity.\",\r\n        \"Make structural-round scheduling use that same entry identity rather than array position zero.\",\r\n        \"Preserve explicitly selected back edges, node-arrival repetition and existing scheduled-loop behavior; do not introduce lane quotas, daily deduplication or scanning of unselected branches.\",\r\n        \"Apply this together with LOOP-CUTOFF-TIMED-NODE-1 in one bounded Planner/Runner repair.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"tests\": [\r\n        \"Finite planner counterexamples with an earlier secondary-lane node: both $end and implicit primary tail must restart the same primary entry with PathLane=0 and a fresh round identity.\",\r\n        \"A finite Runner fixture must observe only the intended selected resources across two rounds, with distinct submission identities; an unselected secondary resource must receive zero submissions.\",\r\n        \"A scheduled-loop fixture with primary entry at a nonzero array index must retain the intended round wait. Preserve existing explicit-back-edge repetition and stop behavior.\",\r\n        \"Reverse the canonical-entry repair and require failure of the wrong-resource/entry assertions, then restore source and rerun the affected path/schedule tests.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"closure_evidence\": []\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"LOOP-CUTOFF-TIMED-NODE-1\",\r\n      \"severity\": \"important\",\r\n      \"obligation\": \"implementation\",\r\n      \"status\": \"open\",\r\n      \"root_cause\": \"DriveAsync checks LoopDeadlineAt before AwaitNodeScheduleAsync. The node wait neither caps its target at the cutoff nor rechecks the cutoff before returning permission to execute. After that asynchronous wait, DriveAsync proceeds directly to condition/end handling, prerequisites and resource submission. The production boundary and admission path do not add a LoopDeadlineAt guard.\",\r\n      \"counterexample\": \"At 09:00 start a normally authored immediate loop with an absolute deadline of 10:00 and a resource node scheduled for 11:00 in sequence or fixed mode. The pre-wait cutoff check passes. WaitAsync waits until 11:00; AwaitNodeScheduleAsync returns true; the Runner starts that resource after the declared deadline. Existing deadline fixtures advance time while an already-started resource completes or resume LocalWait, and therefore do not exercise this timed-node waiting gap. This is a supported source trace, not a newly executed test.\",\r\n      \"paths\": [\r\n        \"MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowRunner.cs:677\",\r\n        \"MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowRunner.cs:739\",\r\n        \"MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowRunner.cs:792\",\r\n        \"MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowRunner.cs:834\",\r\n        \"MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowRunner.cs:854\",\r\n        \"MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowRunner.cs:1749\",\r\n        \"MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowNodeSchedule.cs:99\",\r\n        \"MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Views/MistletoePage.xaml:1718\",\r\n        \"MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/ViewModels/TaskCenterPanelViewModel.EditParts.cs:309\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"repair_steps\": [\r\n        \"Recheck the existing absolute cutoff after timed-node waits and before a newly arriving node obtains permission for prerequisites or resource submission.\",\r\n        \"Let waiting converge at the relevant cutoff rather than waiting until a later node time. Reuse the existing deadline settlement path and preserve durable timing, cursor, stop authority and unresolved external responsibility.\",\r\n        \"Review the existing scheduled-round expiry check at the same asynchronous wait boundary; do not permit a wait to bypass the already-defined skipAcrossDays rule.\",\r\n        \"Preserve the existing behavior that an already-started node may finish, while no subsequent node starts after the cutoff. Do not manufacture a user Stop or release unknown external facts.\",\r\n        \"Implement and verify this in the same consolidated repair as PATH-STRUCTURAL-LOOP-ENTRY-1.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"tests\": [\r\n        \"Finite fake-clock Runner fixtures: sequence and fixed nodes due after a loop deadline must have zero prerequisite calls and zero resource submissions, and converge through the existing deadline behavior.\",\r\n        \"A flexible node window spanning the cutoff must not start a resource when idle facts become available only after the cutoff.\",\r\n        \"A node started before the cutoff may finish afterward, but its successor must not start. Preserve the existing deadline fixture for this positive case.\",\r\n        \"A timed wait crossing the already-defined scheduled-round end must not execute the expired round's remaining resource.\",\r\n        \"Delete the post-wait cutoff protection in a focused mutant, require the zero-side-effect assertion to fail, restore source and rerun affected path/schedule/deadline/stop tests. No stress loop or game action is needed.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"closure_evidence\": []\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"unified_repair_plan\": {\r\n    \"scope\": \"Only the two current Planner/Runner arrival and wait-boundary defects above, their necessary scheduling helper changes and targeted fixtures.\",\r\n    \"order\": [\r\n      \"Add the finite wrong-entry and post-cutoff zero-submission counterexamples.\",\r\n      \"Unify structural-loop entry identity and protect the post-wait execution boundary.\",\r\n      \"Run one affected Rebuild and the relevant path, schedule, deadline, stop and terminal-release regression set; preserve original unrelated failures.\",\r\n      \"Perform focused reverse mutations for the two behavior assertions, restore exact source and verify restoration.\",\r\n      \"Bind the repaired source and product identity, then use at most the remaining single consolidated repair-verification request. Do not start per-function review chains.\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"excluded_expansion\": [\r\n      \"No new stress-loop acceptance project.\",\r\n      \"No unrelated history, tool or SDK certification project.\",\r\n      \"No game/account/redeem/team/shutdown execution by this reviewer.\",\r\n      \"No reduction of agreed features, formal WPF UI, path repetition or protected data boundaries.\"\r\n    ]\r\n  },\r\n  \"executor_obligation_dispositions\": [\r\n    {\r\n 