ingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowRunner.cs:834\",\r\n        \"MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowRunner.cs:854\",\r\n        \"MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowRunner.cs:1749\",\r\n        \"MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowNodeSchedule.cs:99\",\r\n        \"MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Views/MistletoePage.xaml:1718\",\r\n        \"MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/ViewModels/TaskCenterPanelViewModel.EditParts.cs:309\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"repair_steps\": [\r\n        \"Recheck the existing absolute cutoff after timed-node waits and before a newly arriving node obtains permission for prerequisites or resource submission.\",\r\n        \"Let waiting converge at the relevant cutoff rather than waiting until a later node time. Reuse the existing deadline settlement path and preserve durable timing, cursor, stop authority and unresolved external responsibility.\",\r\n        \"Review the existing scheduled-round expiry check at the same asynchronous wait boundary; do not permit a wait to bypass the already-defined skipAcrossDays rule.\",\r\n        \"Preserve the existing behavior that an already-started node may finish, while no subsequent node starts after the cutoff. Do not manufacture a user Stop or release unknown external facts.\",\r\n        \"Implement and verify this in the same consolidated repair as PATH-STRUCTURAL-LOOP-ENTRY-1.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"tests\": [\r\n        \"Finite fake-clock Runner fixtures: sequence and fixed nodes due after a loop deadline must have zero prerequisite calls and zero resource submissions, and converge through the existing deadline behavior.\",\r\n        \"A flexible node window spanning the cutoff must not start a resource when idle facts become available only after the cutoff.\",\r\n        \"A node started before the cutoff may finish afterward, but its successor must not start. Preserve the existing deadline fixture for this positive case.\",\r\n        