yerHoeingAssistant.UnitTest/ServiceTests/TaskCenter/PathLoopCutoffTests.cs:15\"\n      ],\n      \"repair_steps\": [\n        \"Completed: FirstOccurrence and both structural restart branches use StructuralRoundEntry, preserving the primary entry and PathLane=0.\",\n        \"Completed: Runner binds round-start waiting to IsStructuralRoundEntry's stable node/occurrence identity.\",\n        \"Completed: Structural restart increments durable LoopIteration; explicitly selected back edges retain their existing target/lane semantics.\",\n        \"Completed: No lane quota, daily deduplication or scan of unselected branches was introduced.\"\n      ],\n      \"tests\": [\n        {\"test_id\": \"cbc65cd2-3741-cb57-df1d-5087715a15fd\", \"case\": \"StructuralLoop_RestartsPrimaryEntryAfterEarlierSecondaryNode(explicitEnd: True)\"},\n        {\"test_id\": \"9a7d16ef-05a4-ea04-4381-422b8551b41b\", \"case\": \"StructuralLoop_RestartsPrimaryEntryAfterEarlierSecondaryNode(explicitEnd: False)\"},\n        {\"test_id\": \"c8a95ff4-2aaa-a9d4-e33d-3262d847e05a\", \"case\": \"StructuralLoop_TwoRoundsSubmitOnlySelectedPrimaryWithFreshIdentity(explicitEnd: True)\"},\n        {\"test_id\": \"e6ed5485-3fa8-975d-99ba-7cdecb1bbc59\", \"case\": \"StructuralLoop_TwoRoundsSubmitOnlySelectedPrimaryWithFreshIdentity(explicitEnd: False)\"},\n        {\"test_id\": \"44de1881-ef12-d159-5469-941dcc230fad\", \"case\": \"ScheduledLoop_NonzeroPrimaryEntryStillWaitsForNextRound\"}\n      ],\n      \"closure_evidence\": [\n        \"PC/red/path-cutoff.trx: all five entry cases fail; actual second resource is secondary.\",\n        \"PC/green/path-cutoff.trx: all five pass, including distinct submission keys and PathLane=0.\",\n        \"PC/negative-entry/path-cutoff.trx: reverting only the two structural restart branches makes the same five cases fail; first entry remains correct.\",\n        \"PC/restored-entry/path-cutoff.trx and PC/restored/path-cutoff.trx: the five cases pass again.\",\n        \"PC/negative-entry-source-restored.json and independent byte comparison: both saved original files exactly equal the frozen current files.\",\n        \"PC/product-actual/actual-terminal-runs/run-7f32238e28d0.run.json: only primary at SequenceIndex=1, LoopIteration=0 and 1; LastScheduledRoundWait=1; zero secondary outcomes and zero resource submissions.\",\n        \"PC/product-actual/private/native-ui-source.jsonl: actual formal WPF startup and 02:23 terminal observation, with the retimed definition/revision bound to that persisted run.\",\n        \"Current Host.CreateRunner uses this shared WorkflowRunner, including the production arbitration boundary; no alternate Planner/Runner instance bypass was found.\"\n      ],\n      \"limits\": \"The five fake-boundary cases prove wrong-resource selection and fresh submission identity. The actual WPF condition flow proves shared primary entry and real round waiting; it does not prove resource/game effects or every unrelated explicit-entry permutation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"LOOP-CUTOFF-TIMED-NODE-1\",\n      \"severity\": \"important\",\n      \"obligation\": \"implementation\",\n      \"status\": \"resolved_with_evidence\",\n      \"root_cause\": \"The prior pre-wait deadline check did not protect execution after an asynchronous timed-node wait. The wait could target a later node time and return execution permission after the absolute cutoff. Its shared scheduled-round expiry rule also lacked a post-node-wait application.\",\n      \"counterexample\": \"A 09:00 run with deadline 10:00 and a sequence/fixed resource at 11:00 previously invoked its prerequisite after the cutoff. A flexible node becoming idle only after cutoff also invoked it. The original expired scheduled-round case submitted late at 11:00 instead of skipping the old round.\",\n      \"paths\": [\n        \"source/MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowRunner.cs:739\",\n        \"source/MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCente